[{"sha":"db70043993b73b149c3f6428c1d2249447fa2e28","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRiNzAwNDM5OTNiNzNiMTQ5YzNmNjQyOGMxZDIyNDk0NDdmYTJlMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T19:40:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T19:40:05Z"},"message":"chore(code): prune superseded entries from `_RECOMMENDED_MODELS` (#5263)\n\nThe `/model` picker and onboarding no longer promote Claude Opus 4.7,\nOpus 4.7 Fast, Opus 4.6, GPT-5.5, GPT-5.5 Pro, GPT-5.4, GPT-5.4 mini,\nGPT-5.4 Pro, GPT-5.3 Codex, GPT-5.2, Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview, or Kimi\nK2.7 Code. They remain selectable in the full (Ctrl+R expanded) list\nwherever the provider offers them. The startup fallback for\nauto-detected credentials also moves up: a fresh launch with no saved\nmodel preference now picks `anthropic:claude-opus-5` or\n`openai:gpt-5.6-terra` (the Google fallback stays on\n`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`).\n\n---\n\nThe curated recommendation set is meant to promote only the current\nfrontier tier; these entries have been superseded (Opus 4.8/5, GPT-5.6,\nGemini 3.6 Flash, Kimi K3). Removing them across every provider trims 25\nspec keys down to 39, so the recommended-only view and the onboarding\npicker stay short and current.\n\nThe `CODEX_MODELS` allowlist for the ChatGPT OAuth backend still lists\nthe older GPT ids. That set defines which models the Codex backend\naccepts rather than which ones we promote, so it was left alone —\npruning it would make those models unselectable under `openai_codex`,\nnot just unrecommended.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9ad1ad0f-99db-0d38-eade-c9c88d44f409)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9ad1ad0f-99db-0d38-eade-c9c88d44f409/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"38be415986ad0f7a35353c3ec73b3955e46751df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/38be415986ad0f7a35353c3ec73b3955e46751df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/db70043993b73b149c3f6428c1d2249447fa2e28","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcO6WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd5oQAG2en1rJdut+nruJ6P0JSaFm\n6LuVfwnSt8sfWqX2hVBs27LtAw75w+IMKGDa5zG96D6eG7gq5/766UnpYp45HsUa\ne7ZZEdzMB00K3YxWLjiUjvI6Of4o1Ao5PRkNfBUg337N8cAcD/xLYjwVnBf8eU9f\nRClr2dIfyhzjyXxvIOYiUXc4fN1+hjY9gIsr/5vWuaG3pSgr2pkzY50QTTg9sTnB\nczNOaZHoIFuqSBVUoMWGiVfwt8WdVU01mMmCoeb6+f6Zg2pirPrhCR7huXk3P9JZ\nYvVbwVC5+8sdxpq0eczK2bjay5th6fnfyM+4g7FRQQH4XiieXurJ/EqJoGO2znnp\ntyr4dqH4jXCWxeGtAbqj9C9Gq9IsuD+KxqTU6eossizGht5P2euPOr/PXyah1Wv6\ngph/Ipb/ZsPJV+cjxkchJaBgVz7Z5hCcuPN8k6mUt3nBhVv6rGfRptTRBs3qAT2Z\nb6T8gQ/jYWJOiIUAW/a4hDji6OBP2zoKJfzbT0f1zMDB1O2v99lvkr1gaKyV200w\nK4RtIm6upzFJaFk1soARrKhiaqJmYPI7l2tmJwWlO8yZktdheAmq3WJJQsa9lF1d\ndpB1MWu3JGm0fdlBF3Ntrp68NIHj+AC/LVhsDFviKHEY+TsUB3lWDHKBoMqN6E+f\nF+G39UtskSFtHjTIwJ4c\n=UhkS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38be415986ad0f7a35353c3ec73b3955e46751df\nparent 89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785786005 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785786005 -0400\n\nchore(code): prune superseded entries from `_RECOMMENDED_MODELS` (#5263)\n\nThe `/model` picker and onboarding no longer promote Claude Opus 4.7,\nOpus 4.7 Fast, Opus 4.6, GPT-5.5, GPT-5.5 Pro, GPT-5.4, GPT-5.4 mini,\nGPT-5.4 Pro, GPT-5.3 Codex, GPT-5.2, Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview, or Kimi\nK2.7 Code. They remain selectable in the full (Ctrl+R expanded) list\nwherever the provider offers them. The startup fallback for\nauto-detected credentials also moves up: a fresh launch with no saved\nmodel preference now picks `anthropic:claude-opus-5` or\n`openai:gpt-5.6-terra` (the Google fallback stays on\n`gemini-3.1-pro-preview`).\n\n---\n\nThe curated recommendation set is meant to promote only the current\nfrontier tier; these entries have been superseded (Opus 4.8/5, GPT-5.6,\nGemini 3.6 Flash, Kimi K3). Removing them across every provider trims 25\nspec keys down to 39, so the recommended-only view and the onboarding\npicker stay short and current.\n\nThe `CODEX_MODELS` allowlist for the ChatGPT OAuth backend still lists\nthe older GPT ids. That set defines which models the Codex backend\naccepts rather than which ones we promote, so it was left alone —\npruning it would make those models unselectable under `openai_codex`,\nnot just unrecommended.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9ad1ad0f-99db-0d38-eade-c9c88d44f409)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9ad1ad0f-99db-0d38-eade-c9c88d44f409/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T19:40:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db70043993b73b149c3f6428c1d2249447fa2e28","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db70043993b73b149c3f6428c1d2249447fa2e28","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/db70043993b73b149c3f6428c1d2249447fa2e28/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e"}]},{"sha":"89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg5YzgxNGIyOTI0OWI0NGE4YTYxMjJmNmMzNTlkYjM2MDFhNjgwMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T18:43:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T18:43:02Z"},"message":"feat(code): frame HITL rejection reasons for the model (#5259)\n\nRejecting a tool call with a typed reason now tells the model that a\nuser rejected the call, instead of sending the bare reason on its own.\n\n---\n\nWhen a reason is typed into the rejection reason field (`Tab` on\nReject), the human-in-the-loop middleware uses that string as the\n*entire* synthetic tool result, replacing its built-in \"user rejected\nthe tool call…\" wording. A terse reason like \"wrong file\" therefore\nreached the model with no signal about who produced it or why the tool\nnever ran — only an error status.\n\nThe client now frames the typed reason as `User rejected the tool call\nwith reason: <reason>` before it becomes the rejection decision's\nmessage. The framing is applied at the point where the approval decision\nis translated into a `RejectDecision`, so the tool row in the transcript\nstill renders the user's raw text, and a bare reject (no reason) still\nfalls back to the middleware's canned wording.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/439b5190-9172-bba9-92d4-a7061034b065)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2bf04c14112caa5553edb1bcdb046d7e89caaeff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2bf04c14112caa5553edb1bcdb046d7e89caaeff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcOE2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8CIQAHRvImuRrQwEPAY7AGEEztT5\nD2b5BXVLsfoQp7dlR85JJThi6WYCB2OtwPEmGE69cenkpJqHFIFOHkJvKh2aZnQ2\n6GMZJjZcogb8baEEXH4m63VFHQog6dBInWyYlgMxmRImOHxIor6yFMfV5k5NBvzQ\ne82CysTBbLgqosQqbsjsM/D+2+CHhptt4hvY9d4O+Fe1D3N/0XLKipiE4zTTI8Pr\n5t5M6sxftqx6FCQH/BJeN1qVhOm6dYBRu5isZwW+DebT2NoJy+FOLiNvC8WZ1ZaR\nAtAyFUrDsNT8622AnLjnBV2XrxPp1M1BUuH/aR/0cSpvFRKCNQ2BsKEO500bjX1t\nivQlFXdNg7m/BNDGAlK9giQft3XE26t8ZwCcimzP8v8ccLX9EvzY8cBgp3jc4tC2\nK44jgXdLNgb55fiUnPplzamvYK2V2JO9niO4n3cuHxVtRsBhhwe5s7/v6MbgVGrj\nsK7iQO7tmh25ySXFrki93eP8xt4k2+vxmzqMDnlo7KxbyZvy8edCrROl+w3FFDB+\ngZn6PBd2q9p03ajMb3jcTMYJihtLIX0abWynLhbmHHtI8c8unts9b9GCPUjKV3/d\nCBncWGWE+GexfDd6Q/z4xrxqFpOnq9rS3cd84lLNtceS0k1uEB15rP4vj/Gw5I8U\nbxArUfQ5KKpnulUrFYYZ\n=gNBF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2bf04c14112caa5553edb1bcdb046d7e89caaeff\nparent bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785782582 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785782582 -0400\n\nfeat(code): frame HITL rejection reasons for the model (#5259)\n\nRejecting a tool call with a typed reason now tells the model that a\nuser rejected the call, instead of sending the bare reason on its own.\n\n---\n\nWhen a reason is typed into the rejection reason field (`Tab` on\nReject), the human-in-the-loop middleware uses that string as the\n*entire* synthetic tool result, replacing its built-in \"user rejected\nthe tool call…\" wording. A terse reason like \"wrong file\" therefore\nreached the model with no signal about who produced it or why the tool\nnever ran — only an error status.\n\nThe client now frames the typed reason as `User rejected the tool call\nwith reason: <reason>` before it becomes the rejection decision's\nmessage. The framing is applied at the point where the approval decision\nis translated into a `RejectDecision`, so the tool row in the transcript\nstill renders the user's raw text, and a bare reject (no reason) still\nfalls back to the middleware's canned wording.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/439b5190-9172-bba9-92d4-a7061034b065)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T18:43:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/89c814b29249b44a8a6122f6c359db3601a6802e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3"}]},{"sha":"bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJjNDlmZmJlNzY1MjJlOTg2ZmNjMGFkOTk5MWM5YjUwM2Y3NTllZDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T18:23:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T18:23:49Z"},"message":"chore(code): bump genai-prices minimum to 0.1.1 (#5256)\n\nBumps the minimum `genai-prices` version for `deepagents-code` from\n0.1.0 to 0.1.1, pulling in the latest bundled pricing data refresh. The\n`<0.2.0` upper bound is unchanged.\n\nLockfile-only resolution change otherwise; cost-tracking unit tests pass\nagainst 0.1.1.","tree":{"sha":"806a84010826a4c04fbf47ce9f1d7372347ca06b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/806a84010826a4c04fbf47ce9f1d7372347ca06b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcNy1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmpQQADfvfc7Sp3Jltj6kAsNqwS4r\nIX8Y/tMVaV4brdvzc+eJfZGMi9uKP6roMApikJV/a4IBCx2FvoNstDhBk2ungPi9\nWP38lpxy4/s4Sfnu7HnUofRijhDqjLft77ztRXaEgDNZSSulF84uT7pOxdfLeSfs\nw+JVAhyq+iuffWvJsFwO4Mc4qqsUicMCYZcWPKJzRTnfq7ZeLXT9r97kZ3GS+cfb\nI9UexrSi/WwR/Qe3y5ckpJz1BT8CKUlfPBJe9SeU2YOY1HTLBkB7Olm45x93KU4G\nKcrS4gi/4EroQwouUKoCks4qZPM+gkmZDwWgvOrUbZNGaupijPwua3s0JnX0xmgg\nCIx9IZ3jcnTu9Ac10YhgWvu/bWcA+euW6g7qf3lF1MtM4znwx0a4B55L5kfxcjpl\nPgJqzuSGREUvZIOLTIIZDcaNmdTg/b7Pi/2WqydCK1HWH0sEK+ObSrxE295CxIgE\nZes70JVqXrvW4WhMPXQbJxaYDnTwCgS3LIBciJpxoBQyh734NMUg1UA5Hreci/1m\nogWy/cb8W7DFaYMq4gvb69ejgJkNgy/zxVHEiX3QGfRstwf94iZshUEzGyOayDuh\n7VBbqpDvoP6nszmOBIm1Dgqhsa+WIFk/yjrysARRe4O8tsJeracCdRVQKQdeBju+\ngRitA9K59mA/Rz5l5fOi\n=1qBb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 806a84010826a4c04fbf47ce9f1d7372347ca06b\nparent a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785781429 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785781429 -0400\n\nchore(code): bump genai-prices minimum to 0.1.1 (#5256)\n\nBumps the minimum `genai-prices` version for `deepagents-code` from\n0.1.0 to 0.1.1, pulling in the latest bundled pricing data refresh. The\n`<0.2.0` upper bound is unchanged.\n\nLockfile-only resolution change otherwise; cost-tracking unit tests pass\nagainst 0.1.1.","verified_at":"2026-08-03T18:23:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bc49ffbe76522e986fcc0ad9991c9b503f759ed3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875"}]},{"sha":"a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE3ZTM1NjZmOTA4ZjM5NDM3ODBhN2JlZThmYWM3NGIxZmI0YzY4NzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T17:55:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T17:55:18Z"},"message":"style(code): status bar model label flush with the right edge (#5254)\n\nThe model name in the status bar now runs all the way to the right edge\nof the terminal instead of stopping two columns short.\n\n---\n\nThe model slot is the last widget in the status bar, but it carried two\ncells of *right* padding. Since nothing follows it, that padding was\npure dead space: the model text ended two columns before the terminal\nedge while every other full-width element (the chat input border, the\napproval pill's colored background) sits flush. Removing it makes the\nfooter line span the same width as the chrome above it — matching what\nother status lines (tmux, shells) do.\n\nThe left padding stays: it is the separator between the token counter\nand the model name, not edge inset.\n\n(The approval-mode pill on the far left is deliberately left alone. Its\nhorizontal padding is filled with the pill's own background color, so\nthe badge already starts on column 0 — only its text is inset, which is\nwhat makes it read as a badge. A regression test now pins both edges.)\n\nWidths in the existing `ModelLabel` truncation tests were reduced by two\nso each case still exercises the same content width (and therefore the\nsame truncation rung) as before.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/895084d4-7f5a-087d-3f27-6aade8a39e1c)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"99483b837ca6cd423cce3acc9ac0e41611a2f7ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/99483b837ca6cd423cce3acc9ac0e41611a2f7ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcNYGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxTUQAD53p8/tAam8I1b0FaY7TmTK\n9TR73pUBPZyOjW2DzwTBVZzHDyZu4/EvKp/AtA3aeeuEF9O6kbT+PEegFfSaHFgH\nlZKBomCiQ7dwa++iDlQA5bzqQeMrQ41EH1iL2CgR6fNU7z1rrS64Ur08xLQJdzcQ\nx4lgV8DWBwAhhzMz/grdYzUr3o46CS6WQge6rSmWaghh7qNeUe+V9rvmI3Ipu15M\nS2r3+dRUs6q5W0fGKrNbejHdyG42SyQHq7VJkpukO5ZLoZrtLSRO46mp2En2APnl\n94DtEPJ4zNRgKJ0DrQBtdKmJP1DAxjwj4kaI4kWtEECVyZ6RnnWw0HeO/zRqTDsh\nY4pxPmbI4De+41UGtlKZYeLck8Iu/OdvX8kH9xKUuswHb4wzM9pDPfoqJnwc6QIj\nh1D1jreS1967TqKq6tuo2tkIYYV+NFECaeNfoNshRfVbE1bhivpdGQpGIabhP+I2\nFyHXj+ZssC1aAeTGi9yLIlAofRVYIRNY+28kjD6UjnJ9uN/x/MhW3c0SHL0CcnI0\n2kqzKmj5treOLTdUUbxn/jObPMQCjNl2seVLb/Gnu6XReMP1myus3L8cj27pRO/j\ntIWQNV4ppqdzPUEF7DWqBf7xybR62tXjWPUzUk2TEZQ40BDVA8CloRww0DM+rxMS\nPmyGfXXwCilJ85BdgIvk\n=Ap91\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 99483b837ca6cd423cce3acc9ac0e41611a2f7ab\nparent cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785779718 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785779718 -0400\n\nstyle(code): status bar model label flush with the right edge (#5254)\n\nThe model name in the status bar now runs all the way to the right edge\nof the terminal instead of stopping two columns short.\n\n---\n\nThe model slot is the last widget in the status bar, but it carried two\ncells of *right* padding. Since nothing follows it, that padding was\npure dead space: the model text ended two columns before the terminal\nedge while every other full-width element (the chat input border, the\napproval pill's colored background) sits flush. Removing it makes the\nfooter line span the same width as the chrome above it — matching what\nother status lines (tmux, shells) do.\n\nThe left padding stays: it is the separator between the token counter\nand the model name, not edge inset.\n\n(The approval-mode pill on the far left is deliberately left alone. Its\nhorizontal padding is filled with the pill's own background color, so\nthe badge already starts on column 0 — only its text is inset, which is\nwhat makes it read as a badge. A regression test now pins both edges.)\n\nWidths in the existing `ModelLabel` truncation tests were reduced by two\nso each case still exercises the same content width (and therefore the\nsame truncation rung) as before.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/895084d4-7f5a-087d-3f27-6aade8a39e1c)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T17:55:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a7e3566f908f3943780a7bee8fac74b1fb4c6875/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f"}]},{"sha":"cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNmODcyNjYxMDVlZTZlZDc5ZTU2ZDcyZGVhNThjMWM1ZjQzMTIyOGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T16:15:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T16:15:12Z"},"message":"feat(code): `/model` footer Ctrl+N hint follows display mode (#5247)\n\n`/model` selector footer now toggles its Ctrl+N hint between \"IDs\" and\n\"names\" to match the current row display mode.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` selector footer always read \"Ctrl+N IDs\", even once rows\nwere flipped to raw `provider:model` specs, so the hint no longer\ndescribed what the next press does. The hint is now derived from\n`_show_specs` (\"Ctrl+N IDs\" while friendly names show, \"Ctrl+N names\"\nwhile specs show) and the footer is refreshed when the toggle fires.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d455c068-331f-2953-88b0-d3751f58b63e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e850c191d2ff51f93d974643b93431a265cc25d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0e850c191d2ff51f93d974643b93431a265cc25d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcL6QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0r0QAI1a8AuU4FXjZdaDWiNMtPm/\nwjHUDdKoV1qIxRVk8kDWD8KqD8Pd2oX5m4oEMQl5AchoZ1EG6p3WTro3tTiLk9a5\nwL9ABjGhTKVVdC1gvbqcXAwBenU6qzl2h+c1iKffxia9bJmDtkpJR9R5g5GRKyPV\n+dqavhAbdJEHZokIHnWYDiO2IaSVon6yCZDAUEaq789GaRXKK/g5zyE913hAI8Ez\niMxypnGwjl1/YD7kiFg1bMHo9zLMHOVXmKFur5SSASCPniwmCIm3P2+xcj/mY/gt\nCAmpQ6zVcNMPnjYu8C2oBDHpNzQHmIM2mjDhMwl1++QBQnjem1AJINCv0hnO6+b7\nzrRzAn9G/E2oFcsTYeO0D5ENh+XTEMJJVsCMu0yRhVG0xB/7kuYZOQaWVGIJ79Ck\nPXjrW79Y7ylPLBacYg90hKePHom0vy9r0/Qif/yyK36gy/NGMVDQOYNfmWQ1gOz7\nKKz7VS4M2mWQUcqxd3vTnsgMpTCxNZVBjRphPPxnEKQDHUoSqwJO0z+xckzcrH4V\nyPWMihuPT5ptM26tdQ6PWvpAn7SRpAWYkXzsrtRhxkKDm8++UBZhHrqR6OuuwJm9\nDWpHShP2HmpcHu+hkpHUuocYTl7ul2QZZllAsycmmnP+PHgUg1ah0omqhGKwlWAn\nhgNjuKf/35a04b5/+D9n\n=alI0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0e850c191d2ff51f93d974643b93431a265cc25d\nparent bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785773712 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785773712 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `/model` footer Ctrl+N hint follows display mode (#5247)\n\n`/model` selector footer now toggles its Ctrl+N hint between \"IDs\" and\n\"names\" to match the current row display mode.\n\n---\n\nThe `/model` selector footer always read \"Ctrl+N IDs\", even once rows\nwere flipped to raw `provider:model` specs, so the hint no longer\ndescribed what the next press does. The hint is now derived from\n`_show_specs` (\"Ctrl+N IDs\" while friendly names show, \"Ctrl+N names\"\nwhile specs show) and the footer is refreshed when the toggle fires.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d455c068-331f-2953-88b0-d3751f58b63e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T16:15:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf87266105ee6ed79e56d72dea58c1c5f431228f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05"}]},{"sha":"bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJkNTYyYzg3OWFkM2E4ZWVjMGE5MzBiYmEyM2VmNTdmZWUxNjNjMDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-03T15:58:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T15:58:40Z"},"message":"fix(code): handle malformed hook resumes (#5233)\n\nMalformed server-owned hook resume payloads raised a validation error\nthrough `_invoke_hook`, which could fail the graph instead of allowing\nthe tool lifecycle to continue. Normalize invalid resume data through\nthe existing reducer as a neutral event decision and retain an\n`invalid_resume` warning diagnostic.\n\nAdded a focused regression test and verified the full hooks suite (207\ntests).","tree":{"sha":"27fb949b7fea29e550a6f865bb65bb5bf301a658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/27fb949b7fea29e550a6f865bb65bb5bf301a658"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcLqwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk9YQABAXajx+md9S45C/0Hn/XHIT\nBYwQd+qQgKrPpVBkoIoQMcBsREOCqRcpOnEqbn2DAkgXxbuA1FYkcVJLciGX2Cop\npNVlrUaW8lten3GX/ExRryaCmOg43UMvsyVk/ZNdyYNB6uk5Rlg4sGjQ4utaGYD5\nLiacYQwuzkujld7m/WfkoE0HRPJrPnYze7IZ+zHYcMoLnSvpA1XUaQTA6GuRlOcf\n2HYcHyovfD31aRVB//+RZ1WbBB/Tnv9e+7o0WSx8RxEh6GVxHe/jBhiLlkGE9tVC\n3FewRdtvzXIUREBatpwsIm/S9CbGj6EfZztrTYyJWESNMfqPAMz2StkRqQJVmNze\n6s4klZ1hOewb2pLeKQ/NENoWvnZxWSHctyTPLSfxBn64UHAqoCdYcf9GojbX/oWI\no3NGGizFX7zWPOCxegGI/QQz604hI7OXORbwXg4vzyFeRNIPKfAtA30NProOKVWa\n1sIsekmPPYBm08Q2dXKF9EhfEIy98r1LDbdDTAQ/1tdHtgDkKTS+Zc71Q2Hsms+o\nY2Md4vEV9DgOgNYSdzLbNtLGgXFPqLnxfMiCAMiKUcSHkDabATtu8OEV5wuw9oeQ\neVsLlWWjXl+tbG238HdBLsBkWYmYjAc+plesjSMncuJGfkuGf21S/Q7GeRTrYC0V\nfGjt2h+epS+7YavXYXYU\n=vN2m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 27fb949b7fea29e550a6f865bb65bb5bf301a658\nparent fbe4ec8046c35313c6c05a986779111d84fe2536\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785772720 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785772720 -0700\n\nfix(code): handle malformed hook resumes (#5233)\n\nMalformed server-owned hook resume payloads raised a validation error\nthrough `_invoke_hook`, which could fail the graph instead of allowing\nthe tool lifecycle to continue. Normalize invalid resume data through\nthe existing reducer as a neutral event decision and retain an\n`invalid_resume` warning diagnostic.\n\nAdded a focused regression test and verified the full hooks suite (207\ntests).","verified_at":"2026-08-03T15:58:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bd562c879ad3a8eec0a930bba23ef57fee163c05/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_u