se\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"824e85cf99cb6a4ce78f245f11ae1c9deb33e550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/824e85cf99cb6a4ce78f245f11ae1c9deb33e550"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/00637212084c7fe4c12993c95ab559b92aaa4fef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcKS5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZYQQAAfikSr6o3FLkCwd0nGC8e9/\n7oONLj52WvCC+YRfeDY9GdaYbr1l+hdneoOl+BRQyBVKYfWaD/gd6tOYrKPSsXJv\n3U7bNWU5lm95NRY6T1383U5IGfD2ByS0vqVUxYqcUIUE0fzvoTA6hYZvVMlrGSIx\nBJTd5MDK6IG5DDNMD6uzRyIhUZY3fzXQt26ov8NCMSsQ4zv0NZwZhOYRT6D7feJO\nJVwDm84ebWiR+HG1PD0h7okiIPhMtkWS2r7GEZtQ4F2jFVUSoSsdMqaax208AJYE\n/kTf4UlYddnL9Dab/RzItF/FjxBw3PYBV7drxj05QxmwgeGm2EKrH3O5rUQhFpGx\noGrR6j+0Nj5+i7VbwF1UaoAUWwCVjS1hD2MfJkTWoZv+u/Fj9w3eokD8qDJ77Oj7\nAw4jvjat0Ai/59NvwxQ/mg+PISGdJ58I8Con1/Vy3CZmbPna/mq4aDj+rAW3YPNG\nsXviwSC8QkWwHGilwrmJ9UhHqeua0b+9SGSk8MMA3l41c5gWlp6VTos3GYhAvlCY\nTFX+gG1XFaXv7yB6ElxebEVRjbVI2mM4u5A1AsSl5sL/X38cPSoezAgxcoH5Ceej\n8LmX3Uek0d5YZANSTuUOEFdpiGZISSQw65Afv2jSBXbH3r7DA7ilquBVgynpwiiX\n/ZtpmNwQ2fwuiPhYu/JG\n=rSQR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 824e85cf99cb6a4ce78f245f11ae1c9deb33e550\nparent 59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785767097 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785767097 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents): 0.7.2 (#5230)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.7.2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.7.1...deepagents==0.7.2)\n(2026-08-03)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Scrub multimodal content blocks that are unsupported by the model's\nprofile.\n([#5194](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5194))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T14:24:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/00637212084c7fe4c12993c95ab559b92aaa4fef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/00637212084c7fe4c12993c95ab559b92aaa4fef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/00637212084c7fe4c12993c95ab559b92aaa4fef/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22"}]},{"sha":"59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU5ZGQyZmM5Mjk3MGZlOWNjMDk5OTRiMjhlNDRlYjJkMTcyNjNhMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-03T13:54:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T13:54:14Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump the minor-and-patch group with 2 updates (#5235)\n\nBumps the minor-and-patch group with 2 updates:\n[actions/checkout](https://github.com/actions/checkout) and\n[pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish](https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish).\n\nUpdates `actions/checkout` from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/releases\">actions/checkout's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>skip running unsafe pr check if input is default by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2518\">actions/checkout#2518</a></li>\n<li>trim only ascii whitespace for branch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2521\">actions/checkout#2521</a></li>\n<li>escape values passed to --unset by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2530\">actions/checkout#2530</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...v7.0.1\">https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...v7.0.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">actions/checkout's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Changelog</h1>\n<h2>v7.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Skip running unsafe pr check if input is default by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2518\">actions/checkout#2518</a></li>\n<li>Trim only ascii whitespace for branch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2521\">actions/checkout#2521</a></li>\n<li>Escape values passed to --unset by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2530\">actions/checkout#2530</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v7.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Block checking out fork PR for pull_request_target and workflow_run\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2454\">actions/checkout#2454</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.3</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix checkout init for SHA-256 repositories by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/yaananth\"><code>@​yaananth</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2439\">actions/checkout#2439</a></li>\n<li>fix: expand merge commit SHA regex and add SHA-256 test cases by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/yaananth\"><code>@​yaananth</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2414\">actions/checkout#2414</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix tag handling: preserve annotations and explicit fetch-tags by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2356\">actions/checkout#2356</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add worktree support for persist-credentials includeIf by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2327\">actions/checkout#2327</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Persist creds to a separate file by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2286\">actions/checkout#2286</a></li>\n<li>Update README to include Node.js 24 support details and requirements\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2248\">actions/checkout#2248</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v5.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Port v6 cleanup to v5 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2301\">actions/checkout#2301</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v5.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update actions checkout to use node 24 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2226\">actions/checkout#2226</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.3.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Port v6 cleanup to v4 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2305\">actions/checkout#2305</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.3.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: update README.md by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/motss\"><code>@​motss</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1971\">actions/checkout#1971</a></li>\n<li>Add internal repos for checking out multiple repositories by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mouismail\"><code>@​mouismail</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1977\">actions/checkout#1977</a></li>\n<li>Documentation update - add recommended permissions to Readme by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/benwells\"><code>@​benwells</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2043\">actions/checkout#2043</a></li>\n<li>Adjust positioning of user email note and permissions heading by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/joshmgross\"><code>@​joshmgross</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2044\">actions/checkout#2044</a></li>\n<li>Update README.md by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nebuk89\"><code>@​nebuk89</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2194\">actions/checkout#2194</a></li>\n<li>Update CODEOWNERS for actions by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/TingluoHuang\"><code>@​TingluoHuang</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2224\">actions/checkout#2224</a></li>\n<li>Update package dependencies by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2236\">actions/checkout#2236</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.2.2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>url-helper.ts</code> now leverages well-known environment\nvariables by <a href=\"https://github.com/jww3\"><code>@​jww3</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1941\">actions/checkout#1941</a></li>\n<li>Expand unit test coverage for <code>isGhes</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jww3\"><code>@​jww3</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1946\">actions/checkout#1946</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.2.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out other refs/* by commit if provided, fall back to ref by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/orhantoy\"><code>@​orhantoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1924\">actions/checkout#1924</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` from 1.14.1 to 1.14.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/releases\">pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.14.2</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>🛠️ Urgh… Another release!? Again? Explain yourself!</h2>\n<p>Looking at the diff, you'll only witness updates across the\ndependency tree. That's it! It's not a security fix or anything like\nthat even, no. But you'll want this update.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[!tip]\nSo what <em>most</em> people will find useful is <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/takluyver\"><code>@​takluyver</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/takluyver\">💰</a>'s update of Twine to\nv7 that we use internally (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a>).\nThis version will let them upload their sdists and wheels containing\ncore packaging metadata v2.5 to (Test)PyPI.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>🧐 Tell me why..</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>TL;DR non-pure-python projects with C-extensions tend to have dozens\n(sometimes hundreds) wheels to upload to PyPI per release. They are\noften quite big and take time to transfer over the network. People\nstarted noticing problems and coming up with DIY sharding workarounds\nlike <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/13226\">aio-libs/aiohttp#13226</a>\naround July 23.\nOn this date, projects with a good amount of bytes to publish would\nstart getting timeouts 5 minutes after the PyPI publishing job begun.\nThe same job that worked just fine before.</p>\n<p>I had to start pinging upstream library and ecosystem people, on\nGitHub and privately, to start making sense of what was happening.\nEventually, we collectively concluded that GitHub must've shortened the\nlifetime of their OIDC identity — it seems to have used to be 10 minutes\nlong (at some point in the past) and is now 5 minutes, apparently. It's\nnot documented clearly, and we have not been able to get any clarity by\nattempting to contact GitHub through private channels, using personal\nconnections.</p>\n<p>Over the course of investigation, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/facutuesca\"><code>@​facutuesca</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/facutuesca\">💰</a> found and fixed a\nrelated underlying cache invalidation bug in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1838\">sigstore/sigstore-python#1838</a>,\nwhich he then coordinated propagation through the dependency chain\nupdates in sigstore-python, pypi-attestations, gh-action-pypi-publish\nand gh-action-sigstore-python.</p>\n<p>Mike's also discovered that Sigstore's Rekor slowdown seems to have\nbecome the main contributing cause of the last week's incident. He's\ncollected some data to support this claim: <a\nhref=\"https://publishing-five-minute-timeout.tiiny.site\">https://publishing-five-minute-timeout.tiiny.site</a>.</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>🫶 New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/davidbrochart\"><code>@​davidbrochart</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/415\">#415</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/takluyver\"><code>@​takluyver</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>🪞 Full Diff</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.1...v1.14.2\">https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.1...v1.14.2</a></p>\n<p><strong>🧔‍♂️ Release Manager:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/webknjaz\"><code>@​webknjaz</code></a>\n<a href=\"https://stand-with-ukraine.pp.ua\">🇺🇦</a></p>\n<p><strong>🙏 Special Thanks</strong> to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/davidbrochart\"><code>@​davidbrochart</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/davidbrochart\">💰</a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Dreamsorcerer\"><code>@​Dreamsorcerer</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/Dreamsorcerer\">💰</a> for turning my\nattention (in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/415\">#415</a>\nand in private) to the newly surfaced corner case in GitHub's behavior\nthat only affected a narrow category of projects while many others\nremained blissfully unaware. <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/bdraco\"><code>@​bdraco</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/bdraco\">💰</a> came up with a DIY\nsharding workaround for aiohttp that served as a demo for other\nprojects. <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/miketheman\"><code>@​miketheman</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/miketheman\">💰</a> confirmed the\nWarehouse-side details. Also, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jku\"><code>@​jku</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/jku\">💰</a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/woodruffw\"><code>@​woodruffw</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/woodruffw\">💰</a> helped work through,\nreview and release the Sigstore ecosystem upstream libs.</p>\n<p><strong>💬 Discuss</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:ve6s3mxkefjaxty3m4fdqumn/post/3mrsqy2xba22j\">on\nBluesky 🦋</a>, <a\nhref=\"https://mastodon.social/@webknjaz/117005132816750073\">on Mastodon\n🐘</a> and [on GitHub][release discussion].</p>\n<p>[![GH Sponsors badge]][GH Sponsors URL]</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33\"><code>dc37677</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/417\">#417</a>\nfrom trail-of-forks/ft/bump-deps</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/8b2f23418f024937cf97f77534a597947105e772\"><code>8b2f234</code></a>\nBump <code>pypi-attestations</code> and <code>sigstore</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/78b72dbfed6e025eb89577c059edc936f8a2df14\"><code>78b72db</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a>\nfrom takluyver/twine-v7</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/92f4d2a159875dd135a7e56b7b3262f502b23a13\"><code>92f4d2a</code></a>\nUpdate twine to v7</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/ba38be9e461d3875417946c167d0b5f3d385a247...dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3ef3cb9d6b9110c58e4efc8d9da28cc1497a9a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e3ef3cb9d6b9110c58e4efc8d9da28cc1497a9a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcJ2GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUdEQABglBTq/RbMlGu8N+S/pIL5J\nmbejaUjHwCwde5iVHibxV2DQeYGIwkhIxEKw9Jhqp4ZEn6yR3Feiv5RDOeDMdrP6\n6qO76RtJHTkKJ6h95Eo3snSTUZ3pOYPdM88yxM4qIcjvzf4VKd1/GtABpjl+6EWC\nIKOn0MyA2hSoderWFX2q7LdIlkLSOBzGlo6ZtpuCjkv7hw+Modl1xHpHcM7Hq+Ux\n8cP37GEKCDvK6pyYSvpGZUtWvgk2LXAesA/yLoQtqe/4cnBaVaDKxFefjMwJ1SZH\nQFNPmezPJnWiHfE8+mhtGO0HYCnjaiGektf/zZGjZuljbz0KJA/pnh1esV5xzZnz\nUEqdZp/N58ypUR80EmaSvpBihX7sW0Ip8L0X0U+WKkfA6qbTZ9nMa6jDR+WOb8Jv\nmBqr/+rHrlPqTPPp9feNJCGP0xa7Zuu+662g0gkx8lLkQT8Klxe2fq4VmXpTrf+1\nEUUFFjMs8+NU7Vm3oUOwWu/cLfZPHPLxuXsSwlaU5NlNmo5kCGcqdjwNh0NtAcHG\nopPFRRrZi/1Vc2O4HAl0+M8vA6PLRJyC6bjffvjj5yKP/EpXsOyqcAM6eEqPnWeO\n4nP3nduCCMkEQIkIeaH4h73R8hMxC/4gKqx24a0IrWXLH7igMJ2VtrNM6dvUjZ1B\nd/FZIrCFNela1AutIWyR\n=DMBd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e3ef3cb9d6b9110c58e4efc8d9da28cc1497a9a0\nparent 1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785765254 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785765254 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump the minor-and-patch group with 2 updates (#5235)\n\nBumps the minor-and-patch group with 2 updates:\n[actions/checkout](https://github.com/actions/checkout) and\n[pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish](https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish).\n\nUpdates `actions/checkout` from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/releases\">actions/checkout's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>skip running unsafe pr check if input is default by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2518\">actions/checkout#2518</a></li>\n<li>trim only ascii whitespace for branch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2521\">actions/checkout#2521</a></li>\n<li>escape values passed to --unset by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2530\">actions/checkout#2530</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...v7.0.1\">https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...v7.0.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">actions/checkout's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Changelog</h1>\n<h2>v7.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Skip running unsafe pr check if input is default by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2518\">actions/checkout#2518</a></li>\n<li>Trim only ascii whitespace for branch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2521\">actions/checkout#2521</a></li>\n<li>Escape values passed to --unset by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2530\">actions/checkout#2530</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v7.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Block checking out fork PR for pull_request_target and workflow_run\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/aiqiaoy\"><code>@​aiqiaoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2454\">actions/checkout#2454</a></li>\n<li>Various dependency updates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.3</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix checkout init for SHA-256 repositories by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/yaananth\"><code>@​yaananth</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2439\">actions/checkout#2439</a></li>\n<li>fix: expand merge commit SHA regex and add SHA-256 test cases by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/yaananth\"><code>@​yaananth</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2414\">actions/checkout#2414</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix tag handling: preserve annotations and explicit fetch-tags by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2356\">actions/checkout#2356</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Add worktree support for persist-credentials includeIf by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2327\">actions/checkout#2327</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v6.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Persist creds to a separate file by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2286\">actions/checkout#2286</a></li>\n<li>Update README to include Node.js 24 support details and requirements\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2248\">actions/checkout#2248</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v5.0.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Port v6 cleanup to v5 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2301\">actions/checkout#2301</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v5.0.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update actions checkout to use node 24 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2226\">actions/checkout#2226</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.3.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Port v6 cleanup to v4 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ericsciple\"><code>@​ericsciple</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2305\">actions/checkout#2305</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.3.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: update README.md by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/motss\"><code>@​motss</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1971\">actions/checkout#1971</a></li>\n<li>Add internal repos for checking out multiple repositories by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mouismail\"><code>@​mouismail</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1977\">actions/checkout#1977</a></li>\n<li>Documentation update - add recommended permissions to Readme by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/benwells\"><code>@​benwells</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2043\">actions/checkout#2043</a></li>\n<li>Adjust positioning of user email note and permissions heading by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/joshmgross\"><code>@​joshmgross</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2044\">actions/checkout#2044</a></li>\n<li>Update README.md by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nebuk89\"><code>@​nebuk89</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2194\">actions/checkout#2194</a></li>\n<li>Update CODEOWNERS for actions by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/TingluoHuang\"><code>@​TingluoHuang</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2224\">actions/checkout#2224</a></li>\n<li>Update package dependencies by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/salmanmkc\"><code>@​salmanmkc</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/2236\">actions/checkout#2236</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.2.2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>url-helper.ts</code> now leverages well-known environment\nvariables by <a href=\"https://github.com/jww3\"><code>@​jww3</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1941\">actions/checkout#1941</a></li>\n<li>Expand unit test coverage for <code>isGhes</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jww3\"><code>@​jww3</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1946\">actions/checkout#1946</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.2.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out other refs/* by commit if provided, fall back to ref by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/orhantoy\"><code>@​orhantoy</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/actions/checkout/pull/1924\">actions/checkout#1924</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/v7...3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` from 1.14.1 to 1.14.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/releases\">pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.14.2</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>🛠️ Urgh… Another release!? Again? Explain yourself!</h2>\n<p>Looking at the diff, you'll only witness updates across the\ndependency tree. That's it! It's not a security fix or anything like\nthat even, no. But you'll want this update.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[!tip]\nSo what <em>most</em> people will find useful is <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/takluyver\"><code>@​takluyver</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/takluyver\">💰</a>'s update of Twine to\nv7 that we use internally (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a>).\nThis version will let them upload their sdists and wheels containing\ncore packaging metadata v2.5 to (Test)PyPI.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>🧐 Tell me why..</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<p>TL;DR non-pure-python projects with C-extensions tend to have dozens\n(sometimes hundreds) wheels to upload to PyPI per release. They are\noften quite big and take time to transfer over the network. People\nstarted noticing problems and coming up with DIY sharding workarounds\nlike <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/13226\">aio-libs/aiohttp#13226</a>\naround July 23.\nOn this date, projects with a good amount of bytes to publish would\nstart getting timeouts 5 minutes after the PyPI publishing job begun.\nThe same job that worked just fine before.</p>\n<p>I had to start pinging upstream library and ecosystem people, on\nGitHub and privately, to start making sense of what was happening.\nEventually, we collectively concluded that GitHub must've shortened the\nlifetime of their OIDC identity — it seems to have used to be 10 minutes\nlong (at some point in the past) and is now 5 minutes, apparently. It's\nnot documented clearly, and we have not been able to get any clarity by\nattempting to contact GitHub through private channels, using personal\nconnections.</p>\n<p>Over the course of investigation, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/facutuesca\"><code>@​facutuesca</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/facutuesca\">💰</a> found and fixed a\nrelated underlying cache invalidation bug in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1838\">sigstore/sigstore-python#1838</a>,\nwhich he then coordinated propagation through the dependency chain\nupdates in sigstore-python, pypi-attestations, gh-action-pypi-publish\nand gh-action-sigstore-python.</p>\n<p>Mike's also discovered that Sigstore's Rekor slowdown seems to have\nbecome the main contributing cause of the last week's incident. He's\ncollected some data to support this claim: <a\nhref=\"https://publishing-five-minute-timeout.tiiny.site\">https://publishing-five-minute-timeout.tiiny.site</a>.</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>🫶 New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/davidbrochart\"><code>@​davidbrochart</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/415\">#415</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/takluyver\"><code>@​takluyver</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>🪞 Full Diff</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.1...v1.14.2\">https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/v1.14.1...v1.14.2</a></p>\n<p><strong>🧔‍♂️ Release Manager:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/webknjaz\"><code>@​webknjaz</code></a>\n<a href=\"https://stand-with-ukraine.pp.ua\">🇺🇦</a></p>\n<p><strong>🙏 Special Thanks</strong> to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/davidbrochart\"><code>@​davidbrochart</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/davidbrochart\">💰</a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Dreamsorcerer\"><code>@​Dreamsorcerer</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/Dreamsorcerer\">💰</a> for turning my\nattention (in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/415\">#415</a>\nand in private) to the newly surfaced corner case in GitHub's behavior\nthat only affected a narrow category of projects while many others\nremained blissfully unaware. <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/bdraco\"><code>@​bdraco</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/bdraco\">💰</a> came up with a DIY\nsharding workaround for aiohttp that served as a demo for other\nprojects. <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/miketheman\"><code>@​miketheman</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/miketheman\">💰</a> confirmed the\nWarehouse-side details. Also, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jku\"><code>@​jku</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/jku\">💰</a> and <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/woodruffw\"><code>@​woodruffw</code></a><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/woodruffw\">💰</a> helped work through,\nreview and release the Sigstore ecosystem upstream libs.</p>\n<p><strong>💬 Discuss</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:ve6s3mxkefjaxty3m4fdqumn/post/3mrsqy2xba22j\">on\nBluesky 🦋</a>, <a\nhref=\"https://mastodon.social/@webknjaz/117005132816750073\">on Mastodon\n🐘</a> and [on GitHub][release discussion].</p>\n<p>[![GH Sponsors badge]][GH Sponsors URL]</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33\"><code>dc37677</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/417\">#417</a>\nfrom trail-of-forks/ft/bump-deps</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/8b2f23418f024937cf97f77534a597947105e772\"><code>8b2f234</code></a>\nBump <code>pypi-attestations</code> and <code>sigstore</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/78b72dbfed6e025eb89577c059edc936f8a2df14\"><code>78b72db</code></a>\nMerge pull request <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/issues/416\">#416</a>\nfrom takluyver/twine-v7</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/commit/92f4d2a159875dd135a7e56b7b3262f502b23a13\"><code>92f4d2a</code></a>\nUpdate twine to v7</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish/compare/ba38be9e461d3875417946c167d0b5f3d385a247...dc37677b2e1c63e2034f94d8a5b11f265b73ba33\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-03T13:54:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59dd2fc92970fe9cc09994b28e44eb2d17263a22/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233"}]},{"sha":"1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFmYTM4NjZhNmJlM2YzMzY5MjUyNGYxZjE2ZTVlMDYzYTI4NzkyMzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-03T13:54:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-03T13:54:03Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 4.19.1 to 5.0.1 in the major group (#5236)\n\nBumps the major group with 1 update:\n[CodSpeedHQ/action](https://github.com/codspeedhq/action).\n\nUpdates `CodSpeedHQ/action` from 4.19.1 to 5.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/codspeedhq/action/releases\">CodSpeedHQ/action's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v5.0.1</h2>\n<h2>🚀 Highlights</h2>\n<h3>More precise measurements by default</h3>\n<p><code>cycle-estimation</code> is now enabled by default, giving more\nprecise benchmark cycle estimation in Simulation mode. See <a\nhref=\"https://codspeed.io/docs/instruments/cpu#estimating-cycles\">docs</a>.</p>\n<h3>New: allocation exclusion</h3>\n<p>Opt in to <code>exclude-allocations</code> to remove allocator time\nfrom benchmarks in Simulation mode and reduce variance. See <a\nhref=\"https://codspeed.io/docs/instruments/cpu/allocation-exclusion\">docs</a>.</p>\n<h3><code>samply</code>-based profiler by default on Linux</h3>\n<p>The walltime profiler now uses <code>samply</code> on all OSes. Set\n<code>CODSPEED_WALLTIME_PROFILER=perf</code> to restore the previous\nbehavior.</p>\n<h2>⚠️ Breaking changes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>cycle-estimation</code> is now enabled by default (see\nabove)</li>\n<li>The <code>samply</code>-based profiler is now the default on Linux;\nset <code>CODSPEED_WALLTIME_PROFILER=perf</code> to revert</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Details</h2>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->🚀 Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Load eBPF through a delegated BPF token by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n<li>Enable cycle estimation and allocation exclusion by default by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/461\">#461</a></li>\n<li>Make samply profiler default for all OSes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/codspeedhq/action/issues/472\">#472</a>)\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/475\">#475</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->🐛 Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Classify mapped libraries without init-userns privilege by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n<li>Disable allocator exclusion by default (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/codspeedhq/action/issues/489\">#489</a>)\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/not-matthias\"><code>@​not-matthias</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/489\">#489</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->💼 Other</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump the memtrack pin to 1.4.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriencaccia\"><code>@​adriencaccia</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/484\">#484</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->🏗️ Refactor</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Hook-based CPU isolation for the walltime runner by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->🧪 Testing</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Run every tracking test under both BPF variants by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><!-- raw HTML omitted -->⚙️ Internals</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>chore: bump runner version to 5.0.1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/pull/228\">CodSpeedHQ/action#228</a></li>\n<li>docs: bump documented action version to v5 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriencaccia\"><code>@​adriencaccia</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/pull/227\">CodSpeedHQ/action#227</a></li>\n<li>Bump submodule to reduce debug info server timeouts by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n<li>Make tests run release builds of the binaries by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/CodSpeedHQ/runner/pull/456\">#456</a></li>\n<li>Update submodule to fix fmt and ignore ubuntu debuginfod serv by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeLagrange\"><code>@​GuillaumeLagrange</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Install codspeed-runner 5.0.1</h2>\n<h3>Install prebuilt binaries via shell script</h3>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/88472375d0a4572cf70a9f1fe3a4e0ab8da1b924\"><code>8847237</code></a>\nRelease v5.0.1 🚀</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/81795c3bf3884331d2e4cfc0d13d743e484a10c1\"><code>81795c3</code></a>\nfix: remove yanked 5.0.0 version hash</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/eaace1405d0fccb869927040921ac93617234929\"><code>eaace14</code></a>\ndocs: bump documented action version to v5</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/a3e4fe0ad61b10d61e8ec28447ca2a7f0f220055\"><code>a3e4fe0</code></a>\nchore: bump runner version to 5.0.1</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/f87ba88d8df49f904707c82ddc254bc791b049f5\"><code>f87ba88</code></a>\nRelease v5.0.0 🚀</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/CodSpeedHQ/action/commit/7ab72f20ff7e70881f52add1370c74a56ba53965\"><code>7ab72f2</code></a>\nchore: bump runner version to 5.0.0</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/codspeedhq/action/compare/f22792bfac16f3e14eb9fbea76f4a48e9cc22b93...88472375d0a4572cf70a9f1fe3a4e0ab8da1b924\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=CodSpeedHQ/action&package-manager=github_actions&previous-version=4.19.1&new-version=5.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7082620b7148ad286a8d1fa94d49221c7fec6815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7082620b7148ad286a8d1fa94d49221c7fec6815"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1fa3866a6be3f33692524f1f16e5e063a2879233","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcJ17CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASGMQAE0zDzu1lvWFezpKSRb0NXn6\nsbbYPpw3uFCBTNoqN39IT1W779qSTkYLX1gJVJZr3HNV70Os6bRB3OAFwwvLVe96\nfplJ1MmPIxpI9wKfFevX4IhQ76XTeFtWOiWaYfCla1TCZh+AUWAIRHxnMOuGgIPz\nYh5kGH2i/q0hT/gxXcaA5aFWUQzTzueuJA7asftq7pQ+x9wwaCKGwsQsrydV3V8h\nzdusDnIlELqyfR7i9UAX10cyFXSD0K/34xg