:"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbRzuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqA0QAFQuurQ8mQ97vGDM1JSh6ZOL\nhYr9Ux2mfAl9qvG3OJ1WAsEhccQ7RQzfllt5yrFUCuTQ0XOX1+8ctnOy4kzMCxqd\nCCq2xq0szy+iE/22jIR2ify2C8b0SvnqAM3ToBR/0Ala0w+ZRU3a5ygfOnqKted8\n8iazVuOsWpqMuj8Lx9zciDxuZDhF4CyD5/FuuNSX8vWfltEuZ4V9UjXAhwtLB0il\n92GMqvBSmzYuGpKJWHLVzCyi+HXeblONHsYWhgzO3Tyi27YPnuPmL0wO6LKBO6kJ\nM/RrV7/iZJiJ3D0O3w3SnIwn6bJO6/c72KLDZqXy6t4jZKDC2wLztO7MGEWD36TP\nMBtCwVhQ/inmWMjWRJJpbhLzEony9WMX7aC3VPvr7LIxISe+KXNFaXCQBE4S8Cw9\n7KjFh9mtCMwkBUv77MAcF2VEQ5cVqbpxEe+90h+mrwPfFDal96AIkoz+MXp2DBEr\nIiHLI/jr7Mhx/Nfk6nO93hpqukEsj2FlFekK7x5835ATZKuzLK/HKbDfKl2Tk+pT\njqk2eC612nZKGVJPk2OuMcjvOC0WSf1FWzSv8crQn8EdEk9YDRyzvURIpcWQxMkj\nN4ffkWOqcEm120Hh8slgY7c0o1u2rOzrznfEdK8+MCSUbun+9i4VbjZCC1YCKQ4D\nj2YD2LB4RQwP64EcWWL4\n=cB8z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9131faf7c10ea7ba22c599d93ec00cb3f9b1515f\nparent bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1785535726 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785535726 -0700\n\nchore(talon): require deepagents 0.7 (#5231)\n\nTalon's dependency floor still referenced the `0.7.0a3` prerelease after\nDeep Agents 0.7 became stable. Require `deepagents>=0.7.0` instead.\n\nVerified with Talon's tests, lint, type checks, and `uv lock --check`.\n\nCo-authored-by: John LangChain <jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T22:08:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46ee772b45e1d80e65c26524b0ef05914a503533","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/46ee772b45e1d80e65c26524b0ef05914a503533","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/46ee772b45e1d80e65c26524b0ef05914a503533/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d"}]},{"sha":"bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJkYzYxMDQ0NTUzNGJhMzM5MzYwZjM5ODhkZTZiNTBiNjA0ODJmMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-31T20:19:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T20:19:30Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): scrub multimodal content blocks unsupported by the model's profile (#5194)\n\nfixes https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/37576\n\nReading a file that `read_file` can't attach to the current model (e.g.\na `.docx`) no longer fails the thread with a non-retryable provider\nerror. Instead, the unsupported attachment is replaced with a text\nplaceholder before the request is sent.\n\nReported error: calling `read_file` on a `.docx` caused Anthropic to\nreject the request with a `media_type` validation error, leaving the\nagent unable to recover.\n\n**Root cause:** `read_file` returns non-text files as multimodal content\nblocks. Anthropic only accepts inline `file` blocks for\n`application/pdf`; other document types (e.g. `.docx`, `.pptx`) are\nrejected server-side.\n\n**Fix:** `FilesystemMiddleware.wrap_model_call` / `awrap_model_call` now\nscrub outgoing requests, replacing unsupported multimodal blocks with a\ntext placeholder before they reach the provider.\n\n- Images, audio, video, and PDFs are filtered using `ModelProfile`\ncapabilities (`image_inputs`, `audio_inputs`, `video_inputs`,\n`pdf_inputs`, plus `*_tool_message` variants). Missing profile fields\ndefault to supported; only an explicit `False` strips a block.\n- Non-PDF file types currently use a small provider allowlist (`openai`,\n`google_genai`). Other providers (including Anthropic) receive a\nplaceholder instead of an unsupported attachment.\n\nNote: This is a hot fix to resolve the error. Broader fix is to extend\nthe model profiles.\n\nRelated issues: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4397,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/1313,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3864,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3660,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/36939,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/38872","tree":{"sha":"28996740b564121888b152ae0e9525ebd60eebc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/28996740b564121888b152ae0e9525ebd60eebc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbQNSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP0QQAKojbfgCuJzPu3O6+BdjkZ8E\nA0VqeMP/iXsEGnPVsJ0CfsJmjPrYIw4Bszd2/1aupKBSOUqUwHR1Fzqa+LIdYDq0\nTJKDJ6pTpfheL1fYcsObZavu5ZFYadzYvHXG7YpG4vsrGCr5LKWNzDlfZPJ06LPE\nts87HqNB7EDz5gJlwM4Wgmep6vTFetFcY/7Q3fDHtA9QaYBVjNRl8WYWK7iJWsdJ\ndQk93ASnqzxTrtapdGFZEmdA7EIpkEeJC+VHBwoxjPNCM2PEg2uGeImCD3gqS0fu\nZAEUDd9uHf6Ex9acsc6IbJX8N/bWMnPZyPCge9I8GEuEO+jfjVR0gcSyhXRzxNel\n3j3uwQ6PZPqrDvUIkGP6Pcn5aqcVPYNSa1teCGoPJVYUMFZFEw1yrMncsgsCFdjA\nucetJHvEa6KhWsHq1aI6PGX28JxeV8WquzgfIDb9UWeYseAIt1yF8a9ADVzglAQH\nxqqiJ7jMo0wsBdrMHPO/MNsSKJepxphvMAfm++dDmUrmiZ6viaFmZFO69b7We7BW\nyTdmJm2yUgL0jFmeU7yG9NpuRw4vbfFQA598ttRQjpZSb3S+xOh/0b6eA9/dU0jM\nx+Fk+Ebp3StzlDOlltQbsDjudHVgNuENxjAy52XNQiUWf/neBD6xANmhdRIbQ0dv\n3oQw+wJlyjfUCka8ypCC\n=C3Ys\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 28996740b564121888b152ae0e9525ebd60eebc7\nparent 0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1785529170 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785529170 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): scrub multimodal content blocks unsupported by the model's profile (#5194)\n\nfixes https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/37576\n\nReading a file that `read_file` can't attach to the current model (e.g.\na `.docx`) no longer fails the thread with a non-retryable provider\nerror. Instead, the unsupported attachment is replaced with a text\nplaceholder before the request is sent.\n\nReported error: calling `read_file` on a `.docx` caused Anthropic to\nreject the request with a `media_type` validation error, leaving the\nagent unable to recover.\n\n**Root cause:** `read_file` returns non-text files as multimodal content\nblocks. Anthropic only accepts inline `file` blocks for\n`application/pdf`; other document types (e.g. `.docx`, `.pptx`) are\nrejected server-side.\n\n**Fix:** `FilesystemMiddleware.wrap_model_call` / `awrap_model_call` now\nscrub outgoing requests, replacing unsupported multimodal blocks with a\ntext placeholder before they reach the provider.\n\n- Images, audio, video, and PDFs are filtered using `ModelProfile`\ncapabilities (`image_inputs`, `audio_inputs`, `video_inputs`,\n`pdf_inputs`, plus `*_tool_message` variants). Missing profile fields\ndefault to supported; only an explicit `False` strips a block.\n- Non-PDF file types currently use a small provider allowlist (`openai`,\n`google_genai`). Other providers (including Anthropic) receive a\nplaceholder instead of an unsupported attachment.\n\nNote: This is a hot fix to resolve the error. Broader fix is to extend\nthe model profiles.\n\nRelated issues: https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4397,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/1313,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3864,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3660,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/36939,\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/issues/38872","verified_at":"2026-07-31T20:19:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bdc610445534ba339360f3988de6b50b60482f1d/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571"}]},{"sha":"0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA4MjhiMDJkMzBjN2I1NTU3ZWNmY2U3YzRhNDAzOWUwZDljNGM1NzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T18:09:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T18:09:33Z"},"message":"feat(code): load hooks from installed plugins (#5198)\n\nEnabled plugins can now contribute Hooks v2 handlers through\n`hooks/hooks.json`, manifest paths, or inline configuration. Their hooks\nreceive plugin path variables, appear in the plugin manager, and\nactivate on startup or `/reload`.\n\n---\n\nPlugin hook sources retain provenance for deterministic snapshots and\nper-plugin environments. Invalid plugin documents are isolated and\nsurfaced as diagnostics without disabling user, project, or other plugin\nhooks.\n\n## Review Guide\n1. Plugin declarations:\n- `manifest.py`\n- `hooks.py`\n\n2. Hook loading and execution:\n- `loading.py`\n- `snapshot.py`\n- `engine.py`\n\n3. Reload behavior:\n- `app.py`","tree":{"sha":"66f7f47c968f5943b170f18ed8bf2ee7f78c8397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/66f7f47c968f5943b170f18ed8bf2ee7f78c8397"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbOTdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEKgQAAONETDAn1bD27lUABcGBWqC\nOjCDNjdO2ECUriFmWZ1ssEDd1QVp7VFbNJVElt8jep9dV/3ewS+F9vrfAihyrxnZ\n5042EiMPN7Yw2xusVEZ8Yo9bXxHQdH+dTVfpTTs5QBSTgIVQzBgkCmb5Bni75Dbk\nU2/RQY5JL5jZhE/NgbgRKYU8sECljGNR22TCmwg8vQUKiKVJ9USBlOD507Nxd6Ag\nQ2aotMcOyupfq13RLE4Egrd/xMj0a2fmwSFnQuvcAZaiyVCHsq9MNFOyZ3YJu1Gn\nF1T8Ie7UQpTUyNFQ5Dy5kbbCBpoxJut66IUuwcUYBM40I4mmH4STDHCelD9SkKCo\nWudlflwJs0X1hsEVZzpWEVe00BGfLvVv0W7IvqceYHMQ8PrVUyzEhMIkv4hBiTHS\nIj5oFT/CxXXPfjt2dtBZ0pc6rwbRnb6+Bmcow8VAp2aVf7l45h/ZcvdqEqgNc+4M\ndg48rxve4r/SzUNqbsO601EBG3m77/j0NZmjGnc/RrsAmUDG3WAG0pMscQhjS9SF\nk5jnFGZVqX3jViu2idQ83GJQAe8lZSIsiaFCqXhh/nLHtSWa79/KAk7RsbZ+vyj9\nLYaVMkxt292VlLMcMOTr8rdahI8udjCe9Ez/92s7w9fwt4tOTIKopUNNwF0y5q09\n5ULmx8L3G1wKk18yUNbl\n=r5iB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 66f7f47c968f5943b170f18ed8bf2ee7f78c8397\nparent bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785521373 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785521373 +0000\n\nfeat(code): load hooks from installed plugins (#5198)\n\nEnabled plugins can now contribute Hooks v2 handlers through\n`hooks/hooks.json`, manifest paths, or inline configuration. Their hooks\nreceive plugin path variables, appear in the plugin manager, and\nactivate on startup or `/reload`.\n\n---\n\nPlugin hook sources retain provenance for deterministic snapshots and\nper-plugin environments. Invalid plugin documents are isolated and\nsurfaced as diagnostics without disabling user, project, or other plugin\nhooks.\n\n## Review Guide\n1. Plugin declarations:\n- `manifest.py`\n- `hooks.py`\n\n2. Hook loading and execution:\n- `loading.py`\n- `snapshot.py`\n- `engine.py`\n\n3. Reload behavior:\n- `app.py`","verified_at":"2026-07-31T18:09:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0828b02d30c7b5557ecfce7c4a4039e0d9c4c571/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f"}]},{"sha":"bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJlYmFmYWEwYzgzMzFhZjI3NjY1YWMwOTQ2MTExMWJhOGM3NWFkN2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T06:01:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T06:01:01Z"},"message":"fix(infra): tolerate unpublished tags in fan-out watch (#5216)\n\nThe release-please fan-out watch no longer crashes while a merged\nrelease is waiting to publish its tag. It skips that component with a\nvisible warning and continues checking the remaining packages.\n\n---\n\nRelease-please updates the manifest when its release PR merges, but the\npackage tag is created later, after pre-release checks pass. If those\nchecks fail, as they did for `deepagents-code` 0.1.51, the manifest\npoints to a tag that does not yet exist. The fan-out detector currently\npasses that tag directly to `git diff`, which exits with `fatal: bad\nrevision` and prevents the watch from examining any other package.\n\nThe detector now verifies each baseline ref before diffing. `git\nrev-parse` return code 1 means the release tag is absent, so the\ncomponent is skipped with a warning and checked again on the next\nrelease-please run or hourly backstop. Any other git failure raises and\nmakes `main()` exit 2, preserving the advisory's fail-closed behavior.\nDiff failures for an existing tag also remain fatal.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `.github/scripts/tests/release/test_check_open_release_fanout.py` — 9\npassed, covering ref found, ref absent, operational lookup failure, and\nexisting-ref diff failure.\n- Full workflow-helper suite — 891 passed.\n- Ruff checks pass for the detector and its tests.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"e3b33f77a17e9cb4e1ad870c066fd3dc24657173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e3b33f77a17e9cb4e1ad870c066fd3dc24657173"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbDodCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATVEQAHi+FJJvs0yHOyG4TDAOW/DA\nuqnqg2vU/ro1nr+or6zmgPrVilVHSxVZnXwX0TbzIUo/WvpTU/b1/DIOQWS6SZx3\n9O2YEAICG43dRautGaaciqGFd/Q0XHnmNf6YOczRrcxm/b6hW+YRri9H9sX7Kzm6\nl4e3+zDfxmS413bi3u+4wv2xmLHsWrhiYeidphVX3GmhTkj7fdAFyOmrtZEoU6mN\n/pSOCgtm8/bh7Z3C09dOBlQpHHswpOXsh7+jx9F8G43q6zFrIZtjoKZVmec5wX5D\nYhrbxKQGo8eayMFSlh9CaIdMpYuZWBZKvkBMRQf+S6s1otpZRPH4E+Tf8UwOuTJm\na+x6KCW5HDEzsZ33qhyQkyPYhVW1qD2a8vH6Q88cXY+VlRrCz3ehAGGzsZ5396px\nL1+MEnW2Un7EY/sqpNB1tzpRPLxOjdAgJKZ75ydeaXru7YMDBYVmGp2bx5l+HxJe\nHTCzfIOeozo79eAeijk0SrBw0st05VxggGfu/1JO/0dFlWZq+GRJPSbAOlKJkEOD\ndW8ufOthcz53qn5rA35L9+U2BczByybt+VOldQAT60RM+WlAwwx4XRHcEsN+DEpC\nLebhBcS7asQMfJTMzu6IakYXTfzZU6VVxkzRtqprFZa90dTENf1Gp7/n1dhffzeV\nhCqRFmYODBU3Mcpv+SPM\n=8k6F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e3b33f77a17e9cb4e1ad870c066fd3dc24657173\nparent d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785477661 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785477661 -0400\n\nfix(infra): tolerate unpublished tags in fan-out watch (#5216)\n\nThe release-please fan-out watch no longer crashes while a merged\nrelease is waiting to publish its tag. It skips that component with a\nvisible warning and continues checking the remaining packages.\n\n---\n\nRelease-please updates the manifest when its release PR merges, but the\npackage tag is created later, after pre-release checks pass. If those\nchecks fail, as they did for `deepagents-code` 0.1.51, the manifest\npoints to a tag that does not yet exist. The fan-out detector currently\npasses that tag directly to `git diff`, which exits with `fatal: bad\nrevision` and prevents the watch from examining any other package.\n\nThe detector now verifies each baseline ref before diffing. `git\nrev-parse` return code 1 means the release tag is absent, so the\ncomponent is skipped with a warning and checked again on the next\nrelease-please run or hourly backstop. Any other git failure raises and\nmakes `main()` exit 2, preserving the advisory's fail-closed behavior.\nDiff failures for an existing tag also remain fatal.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `.github/scripts/tests/release/test_check_open_release_fanout.py` — 9\npassed, covering ref found, ref absent, operational lookup failure, and\nexisting-ref diff failure.\n- Full workflow-helper suite — 891 passed.\n- Ruff checks pass for the detector and its tests.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T06:01:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bebafaa0c8331af27665ac09461111ba8c75ad7f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92"}]},{"sha":"d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQyYjY2M2ZjYTI3N2Q1MTlhODgzMzViYzRmMjY4NTQyYzQxZjJkOTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T05:44:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T05:44:16Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): check rendered toast bounds (#5220)\n\nUnblocks the `deepagents-code` 0.1.51 release recovery after the second\nmanual release run timed out in\n`TestToastAnchoring::test_toasts_do_not_cover_the_chat_input`.\n\n---\n\nTextual lays out every toast in an overflowing `ToastRack`, including\noff-screen toasts, then clips the rack before painting it. When an\nunrelated startup toast makes the rack overflow, a toast's raw\n`region.bottom` can extend below the chat input even though its\ncompositor-clipped region does not render there. The previous hotfix\nwaited for every raw region to end at the chrome boundary, so that\ncondition could never converge on the Linux release runner.\n\nThe test now waits for and asserts the compositor-clipped toast bottoms.\nIt still requires both named test notifications to mount, checks the\ncomplete painted toast stack, and fails when `_anchor_toast_rack` is\ndisabled.\n\nFailed recovery run:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30606795001\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --python 3.11 --group test pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestToastAnchoring -q` — 4 passed.\n- Ruff lint and formatting checks pass via pre-commit.\n- Temporarily disabled `_anchor_toast_rack`; the target test failed as\nexpected.\n- The full local xdist run was interrupted before completion; PR CI will\nrun the release-equivalent suite.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"27c312edce302e2b9c5eba9566c9c27c83297ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/27c312edce302e2b9c5eba9566c9c27c83297ab4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbDYwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPsoQABUsmZXnX0kQhmXWHXkqoMB8\nMW2OYtMbnKq9H5WKgblUIRloyB1NxIGK1UT7Yq/BXgzF0tqqAcv5avBaJlSF8s4w\nIGtOiRllBq1YAQ8GNGsiuppn2iwQws4VOBVLPRSJGesncq7dOz+4C7cQXV+n6mML\nPGdFNbF5r+WfPjgP+JERzxw9LZNtQPasG88m9o+09Vf2mz5wYmO9bqPuA6v32tbo\nR877tffQ+YTy/S0++LmqgpVk8golzOGq60sjI5aMFuT/7fQ5hq76AiRo6IWLijkj\nS1zGC8LNAE+bDjcGewx+nAAAlnHB2ciB9eXHds1M4Al5XFUiUgRHvakDxfGwbxYl\nnd3Ck+DwzZ1NbI5VfNtXkcTYDIMpg9Mx7C+CHiPGJV4rYWSQFe42CcmREPqjaLYi\nLmTfddkHCswvsdhF7IB4Ha+YC7e+zFFEKADfKPKN3QjOGvtg42IDaOeOZ3kXpjIM\n5aXvo6+CJPuvAeY4v8k0FWkmwQoown2E7Pjesh7dLfO2uP8kT8Unmid7+sexz+aN\nrWM2p4N3ZL9tWeL8Yc9JX2EVjdEasPR3YbTS7wIJrhsIkTVSQ6tJUf7Igq3wFSbX\neF8azYX3XoTCkDuHWo68ZVP6MaG27ND+cruN2O+E/ICTZCxa0f/Kstt5m8j/Tc5B\n2iu2h4++W3K2/BK+73Zi\n=Clxu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 27c312edce302e2b9c5eba9566c9c27c83297ab4\nparent d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785476656 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785476656 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): check rendered toast bounds (#5220)\n\nUnblocks the `deepagents-code` 0.1.51 release recovery after the second\nmanual release run timed out in\n`TestToastAnchoring::test_toasts_do_not_cover_the_chat_input`.\n\n---\n\nTextual lays out every toast in an overflowing `ToastRack`, including\noff-screen toasts, then clips the rack before painting it. When an\nunrelated startup toast makes the rack overflow, a toast's raw\n`region.bottom` can extend below the chat input even though its\ncompositor-clipped region does not render there. The previous hotfix\nwaited for every raw region to end at the chrome boundary, so that\ncondition could never converge on the Linux release runner.\n\nThe test now waits for and asserts the compositor-clipped toast bottoms.\nIt still requires both named test notifications to mount, checks the\ncomplete painted toast stack, and fails when `_anchor_toast_rack` is\ndisabled.\n\nFailed recovery run:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30606795001\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --python 3.11 --group test pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestToastAnchoring -q` — 4 passed.\n- Ruff lint and formatting checks pass via pre-commit.\n- Temporarily disabled `_anchor_toast_rack`; the target test failed as\nexpected.\n- The full local xdist run was interrupted before completion; PR CI will\nrun the release-equivalent suite.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T05:44:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d2b663fca277d519a88335bc4f268542c41f2d92/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58"}]},{"sha":"d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ4MTUyMzg5ZDIwN2EyMDZmNDkzNjJlYzFiNzg0MWE2NmQ3ZWFhNTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T05:24:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T05:24:59Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): deflake toast anchoring test (#5217)\n\nA flaky unit test blocked the `deepagents-code` 0.1.51 release:\npre-release checks failed\n`TestToastAnchoring::test_toasts_do_not_cover_the_chat_input` with\n`assert 29 == 19`, so publishing and GitHub release creation were\nskipped. This makes the test deterministic so the release can be\ndispatched again.\n\n---\n\nThe test sends two notifications and immediately asserts exact toast\nlayout after one `pilot.pause()`. Under pytest-xdist load, the assertion\ncan run before those notifications are mounted and their rack layout is\ncurrent.\n\nThe test now waits for observable rendered state: both named\nnotifications must be mounted and the complete toast stack must end at\nthe top of the bottom chrome. The wait is bounded to five seconds.\nMatching the named notifications avoids returning early when startup has\nalready mounted an unrelated toast; checking the full stack still\nverifies that no displayed toast overlaps the chat input.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Python 3.11 (the release runner): exact formerly failing test passed\n20/20.\n- `uv run --python 3.11 --group test pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestToastAnchoring -q` — 4 passed.\n- Ruff lint and formatting checks pass.\n- Confirmed the test fails when `_anchor_toast_rack` is temporarily\ndisabled.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"6470a06a6c86380b26940a5a34b3d298a40118d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6470a06a6c86380b26940a5a34b3d298a40118d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbDGsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI28QADnTr1vLvnMd3+uyw4/+uTJx\nKTPqmxFx02Bn1GoFtufq5oe/XGsGF6hOVhhrLr8iAfEEk1Aihm0GoE4faUJALPW3\naezAwqOl1XaUFHMsreuwIxGd8LG3d9CI+F8TnQOTvlnwqoEk/seZAdaNU4qlcGsA\n1uev8V/tQqMkDlettNmk2iJ/PV9RagQmO1nHeNBxITcWYQnrdYavuAzTyrEc9tIZ\nTueIQOsZa/bMnAGoUEzzCH9dg8wHJwW4u3tt+wP5y54KRbp8CeK2N0E1gc0wrdLQ\nGOwebv/rtcA5fl6zXkgbn2p/i4aezdECpQ37es0dJ4JvRk2ugIF/YWP1fUHYIUa8\nzIci27slBvFpUAPoYz/15YNlSfIDpXcqNSYCDOJ6NDLQo9m1nBNJqqaeevDSOHXg\nDZFMsniVSpYqF6aGikz49um3XHMmYLmYPsUnyeEOkSp8NIu5J3uGM1qpPCT/bI+Q\ntmj/3y+8f3k5bUof6WRulgsJ62CdZKh1fnD99LNpb3XGdvINhPnRSqWaCu9u1SZU\nTosDGVLIxNHfmvkBKNWDYlVq/LLbxSxUJdyjt+dSWhI22Sw2d9A/Pilotfelk00A\nqYc+Jv5f53+BnIxTNgk1ulpyFm+zRd+RY5NLHTYZRwX8jeIHyzEnutzeafBptTC/\nlTLohmiCQexMB2uioVIS\n=S0St\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6470a06a6c86380b26940a5a34b3d298a40118d1\nparent 50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785475499 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785475499 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): deflake toast anchoring test (#5217)\n\nA flaky unit test blocked the `deepagents-code` 0.1.51 release:\npre-release checks failed\n`TestToastAnchoring::test_toasts_do_not_cover_the_chat_input` with\n`assert 29 == 19`, so publishing and GitHub release creation were\nskipped. This makes the test deterministic so the release can be\ndispatched again.\n\n---\n\nThe test sends two notifications and immediately asserts exact toast\nlayout after one `pilot.pause()`. Under pytest-xdist load, the assertion\ncan run before those notifications are mounted and their rack layout is\ncurrent.\n\nThe test now waits for observable rendered state: both named\nnotifications must be mounted and the complete toast stack must end at\nthe top of the bottom chrome. The wait is bounded to five seconds.\nMatching the named notifications avoids returning early when startup has\nalready mounted an unrelated toast; checking the full stack still\nverifies that no displayed toast overlaps the chat input.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Python 3.11 (the release runner): exact formerly failing test passed\n20/20.\n- `uv run --python 3.11 --group test pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_app.py::TestToastAnchoring -q` — 4 passed.\n- Ruff lint and formatting checks pass.\n- Confirmed the test fails when `_anchor_toast_rack` is temporarily\ndisabled.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T05:25:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d8152389d207a206f49362ec1b7841a66d7eaa58/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6"}]},{"sha":"50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUwZDdkMTAyOTFmZDJjNTIxMmI5MWQ4NDgzMjdjYjJiMDlmOWFkZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T04:54:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T04:54:41Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): mark editable SDK installs in `dcode_client_deepagents_version` (#5214)\n\nTrace metadata now reports editable `deepagents` installs as\n`X.Y.Z+editable` under `dcode_client_deepagents_version`, matching the\nencoding the SDK already uses for `lc_versions.deepagents`.\n\n---\n\nRunning `dcode` from a monorepo checkout produced a trace where\n`lc_versions` read `deepagents 0.7.1+editable` (stamped by the SDK) but\n`dcode_client_deepagents_version` read `0.7.1`. Same install, two\nencodings — which makes it look like the client and the graph are on\ndifferent builds.\n\nThe client-side resolver was reusing `_display_sdk_version`, the string\nbuilt for the human-facing `--version` / `/version` / `doctor` surfaces.\nThat string only appends the `editable` PEP 440 local segment for the\n\"workspace HEAD\" case, where the pin `deepagents-code` declares is newer\nthan the sibling SDK's own marker, because those surfaces render a\nseparate `(editable)` annotation next to the version. Trace metadata has\nno such annotation, so the marker has to live in the version string\nitself.\n\nTrace metadata now goes through its own resolver that appends the\nsegment for any editable SDK install. The human surfaces are unchanged\nand keep their unsuffixed version plus `(editable)` annotation; the\npin-ahead workspace HEAD case is also unchanged, since it already\ncarried the segment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/414781f9-ad36-05cc-386a-6cc13fc267d5)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6805e41e288f0e80d6ae712cf8c75e099100d9bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6805e41e288f0e80d6ae712cf8c75e099100d9bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbCqRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASVwQAIKDYGpXYetDi6Qs+PEdk7uP\naLTYvlBBDpgya141xmCzHAaLeGkqhQniydZkrmWJoirLMRNg07XwYMHPKd25SqT8\nrmrC6/UkPsyv3K9iMD8RjVv6JLq0COj7VO5YsXDHsOKc6kxASMu/6l5yDTB5diuL\nLvLzBy3ID1ljuPxK/4Mwc4UVUGDjoD2RH9fKA2P742h0Ch8Uj5fVHEYzrxaJiJFQ\n2b63DEbBO6PU1CTaUeXnbOpVlR54B3WOQ5ldaHR816lCXgDlWz1TvP+vjY9k7eLK\nIVsGIq9kTpgNSh4h5LltLOJMKEl2Y/WrgJpQBqNGdF+qgRfsIod1AoXFzXBnJLOK\njMQMtrw0WBkQnAO6i6yXvkBhyq1hsc2ZLaxRG/JhanpIxB/Bw/wBMtqSoylgKCbB\nFJCcwHy93Ad3030T27EtiitfKJ0NlELhHpclX28i0rOlfBNg7+3i1BByht266P5D\nlOQFQbV8SEvq50ncuqMvOzJB/iFajBsxSMp/egP9cU7iOJxyFm+h11TbMLjUgEW0\niS0Y3K7grXmXrY2RUXG6b7rbFcbE7uDEIp0KdS+kLaB7p9bsfEXrMCTgaz9ErnLo\nWhsmJizvpFNKb/HqI0WTVMbabNPuGGeZdAnpMJvK6NTg/28LwLZDpbuqypwI9cV7\n0V+UB2YxNAzCWvmFGLmW\n=2YQD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6805e41e288f0e80d6ae712cf8c75e099100d9bb\nparent 9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785473681 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785473681 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): mark editable SDK installs in `dcode_client_deepagents_version` (#5214)\n\nTrace metadata now reports editable `deepagents` installs as\n`X.Y.Z+editable` under `dcode_client_deepagents_version`, matching the\nencoding the SDK already uses for `lc_versions.deepagents`.\n\n---\n\nRunning `dcode` from a monorepo checkout produced a trace where\n`lc_versions` read `deepagents 0.7.1+editable` (stamped by the SDK) but\n`dcode_client_deepagents_version` read `0.7.1`. Same install, two\nencodings — which makes it look like the client and the graph are on\ndifferent builds.\n\nThe client-side resolver was reusing `_display_sdk_version`, the string\nbuilt for the human-facing `--version` / `/version` / `doctor` surfaces.\nThat string only appends the `editable` PEP 440 local segment for the\n\"workspace HEAD\" case, where the pin `deepagents-code` declares is newer\nthan the sibling SDK's own marker, because those surfaces render a\nseparate `(editable)` annotation next to the version. Trace metadata has\nno such annotation, so the marker has to live in the version string\nitself.\n\nTrace metadata now goes through its own resolver that appends the\nsegment for any editable SDK install. The human surfaces are unchanged\nand keep their unsuffixed version plus `(editable)` annotation; the\npin-ahead workspace HEAD case is also unchanged, since it already\ncarried the segment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/414781f9-ad36-05cc-386a-6cc13fc267d5)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T04:54:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/50d7d10291fd2c5212b91d848327cb2b09f9ade6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07"}]},{"sha":"9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlmNTgyZDVhMTcyM2NhODgxZTI4Y2QxODNhMGIzNGM5MTM0YjhmMDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-31T04:37:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T04:37:22Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.51 (#5200)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.51](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.50...deepagents-code==0.1.51)\n(2026-07-31)\n\n### Features\n\n- The status bar and usage view now show the running session cost.\n([#5036](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5036))\n- Removed redundant `shell` and `web_search` prompt guidance.\n([#5213](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5213))\n- After switching threads, Deep Agents now points back to the previous\nthread.\n([#5172](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5172))\n- Leaving `/mcp` with pending toggles now prompts you to reconnect.\n([#5211](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5211))\n- `dcode config get` now accepts configuration sections.\n([#5134](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5134))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Kept the `/goal` criteria prompt responsive.\n([#5142](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5142))\n- Improved goal handling so underspecified objectives can be resolved\nfrom conversation context.\n([#5201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5201))\n- Released the turn when an interrupted worker never starts.\n([#5196](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5196))\n- Hid timestamp footers together with their associated rows.\n([#5167](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5167))\n- Fixed editable SDK detection by scanning and correlating SDK locations\nmore accurately.\n([#5199](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5199))\n- Improved `doctor` output to explain why it may not have a\nlatest-version answer.\n([#5209](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5209))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6336c260308f0fd2daecfe0e0df64bfa21b75f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c6336c260308f0fd2daecfe0e0df64bfa21b75f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbCaCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJnwQAAtV+b2o8YeG/OPLMCuH01eo\n6Bg/gHePc53ZjUsF0ZsQdrMMnM7cVgO3V7lp4byobllKkEfAzEE65ObqeFid8q/T\nIZpihQZCXtzmBYRjkE/Cntag6cthYeVM1GUneMvcTFXxpnG0ux8Nnor4+bjKJSN/\nEWetSBtBdYMheY4LiuOjCR1ul8jAgLY7JEIsd8WejLIpLyTkM4wQOGWXuYI26zuv\nSwxOinyZl8spCVU52lHoueGRQ7gWmUHIYRFk3VENxy2eOXpE+Jsxu2mXT+c/BUip\nomh7PDyPiHgs9hDyWYU3JdsHiWwBLssr0k46xwRS4PtfcXOZ523pygB3eh5loweq\nOt33Au9cEUkIId6w/VKfPTtNqWTodl3JYQzV54F1ryunyLLjWVNbN0rplHbqkLYH\n9GRXqyrar4h6bfA5sSI4NndSB3fW9NBa9SuXS1u6BBfU1yGeuJmanNu7RaIDCdoc\nsJ8zxrq9i43ZM+seLDWBpM7piKYczUSibfrJMxSU21v7xKAzEG4Wt7FeX0fPx6oO\ns45Shucio6yF1IIn9KNdOQUlsJ+QXwHxiiORGn6fcucEPMx7F8EaeGMlYtX3lQcM\nXe43MhpSAzBi45D8j2IHlSmowfMMAmqeYvSS/83ZfVErKPbiuZKR2QM/wtqj4i1M\n20eI+4LWTDs+E7M8c7rY\n=rxay\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c6336c260308f0fd2daecfe0e0df64bfa21b75f5\nparent 539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785472642 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785472642 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.51 (#5200)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.51](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.50...deepagents-code==0.1.51)\n(2026-07-31)\n\n### Features\n\n- The status bar and usage view now show the running session cost.\n([#5036](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5036))\n- Removed redundant `shell` and `web_search` prompt guidance.\n([#5213](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5213))\n- After switching threads, Deep Agents now points back to the previous\nthread.\n([#5172](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5172))\n- Leaving `/mcp` with pending toggles now prompts you to reconnect.\n([#5211](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5211))\n- `dcode config get` now accepts configuration sections.\n([#5134](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5134))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Kept the `/goal` criteria prompt responsive.\n([#5142](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5142))\n- Improved goal handling so underspecified objectives can be resolved\nfrom conversation context.\n([#5201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5201))\n- Released the turn when an interrupted worker never starts.\n([#5196](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5196))\n- Hid timestamp footers together with their associated rows.\n([#5167](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5167))\n- Fixed editable SDK detection by scanning and correlating SDK locations\nmore accurately.\n([#5199](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5199))\n- Improved `doctor` output to explain why it may not have a\nlatest-version answer.\n([#5209](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5209))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T04:37:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9f582d5a1723ca881e28cd183a0b34c9134b8f07/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600"}]},{"sha":"539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUzOWQ0YTA0MzgwMTgyNDM4Y2E2M2JhNmI5MDJlYjkyMWRjOGE2MDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T04:25:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T04:25:15Z"},"message":"feat(code): running session cost in status bar and usage (#5036)\n\nCloses #4519\n\nDeep Agents Code now keeps a running estimated USD total for the active\nthread. The status bar shows it beside token usage, `/cost` and\n`/tokens` break it down on demand, and usage summaries include per-model\ncost. The total covers everything the thread spends — assistant turns,\nsubagents, offload/compaction, and Auto mode's classifier — and it is\nrestored on resume and thread switches.\n\n---\n\n## Where the number lives\n\nA thread's lifetime cost should be durable to support `--resume` and\nswitching between threads. Consequently, the graph owns it and the\nclient (e.g. TUI / headless CLI) can read it.\n\nConcretely, `_session_cost_usd` is a new channel on the agent's state\nschema (`CostState`, which extends `ResumeState`), which means it is\npersisted by the graph's checkpointer, in the same checkpoint as\n`messages`.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>FAQ: <code>CostState</code>, and why it extends\n<code>ResumeState</code></summary>\n>\n> `CostState` is the [state\nschema](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#schema)\n`CostTrackingMiddleware` declares — the agent's state plus one channel:\n>\n> ```python\n> class CostState(ResumeState):\n> _session_cost_usd: Annotated[NotRequired[float], PrivateStateAttr,\noperator.add]\n> ```\n>\n> **What `ResumeState` already holds.** It's the schema for facts that\nbelong to the thread as a whole rather than to any one message — the\nthings the TUI/client needs the moment you open a thread, before the\nagent runs again:\n>\n> - `_context_tokens` — how full the context window was after the last\nturn. This drives token readout — e.g., the display in the TUI's footer\nstatus bar, where the cost figure now also sits.\n> - `_model_spec` / `_model_params` — the model and settings the thread\nwas using, so `-r` resumes on _that_ model instead of whatever your\ncurrent [global\ndefault](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/config-file#default-and-recent-model)\nmight happen to be.\n> - `_goal_objective`, `_goal_rubric`, `_goal_status`,\n`_goal_status_note`, `_sticky_rubric`, and the pending-proposal fields —\nthe\n[goal](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/goals-and-rubrics)\nthe thread is working toward (if one is set) and where progress on said\ngoal stands.\n>\n> **Every field here is private, including the new one.** A graph has a\npublic interface: its input and output schemas say what callers may pass\nin and receive back (`messages` is the obvious example). None of the\nfields above belong in that interface, as they aren't things a caller\nsupplies or asks for — they're notes that dcode writes for itself so it\ncan pick the thread back up later.\n>\n> `PrivateStateAttr` omits a field from those public input/output\nschemas. It does **not** make the field ephemeral or unreadable: the\nchannel remains ordinary checkpointed state, is available to graph\nnodes, and is returned by `get_state`. Its writes can also appear as raw\ndeltas in the `updates` stream; the live status bar uses a dedicated\nabsolute-total event instead so the client does not have to reproduce\nthe reducer (details below).\n>\n> **These values are stored rather than recomputed**, because\nrecomputing them is expensive or impossible after the fact. Reopening a\nthread has to show the context gauge and the current model immediately.\nThe context number originally came from the last response's\n`usage_metadata` — the provider counted it for us. If it weren't saved,\nthe CLI would have to load the whole message history and count tokens\nitself to guess at it: slow, dependent on having a tokenizer that\nmatches the provider's, and still only an approximation of what was\nactually billed. Cost is the same shape of problem and worse —\nre-deriving it would mean re-pricing every message in the thread every\ntime you open it.\n>\n> **So why extend `ResumeState`?** Cost is the same kind of resumable\nthread fact, and pricing also needs the model information that\n`ResumeState` already carries. LangChain's `AIMessage` contract does not\nrequire a model identifier: `usage_metadata` standardizes token counts,\nwhile `response_metadata` is optional. Provider integrations commonly\ninclude a model name, but custom and third-party integrations are\nallowed to omit it. When a response does, pricing falls back to the\n`_model_spec` persisted for that turn.\n>\n> </details>\n\nRiding the checkpoint is a deliberate choice over an alternative where\nthe client prices a turn and then pushes the new total with\n`aupdate_state`. (That's a second round trip that can be interrupted —\ne.g. `Ctrl-C`, a crash, a dropped connection — *after* the messages have\nalready been committed.) Writing from inside the graph puts the cost in\nthe same commit as the response that incurred it. Importantly, it also\nkeeps an `UpdateState` run/span out of LangSmith traces if configured.\nRestoring is then a single `aget_state` read from the checkpoint.\n\nTwo things about the channel's declaration matter downstream:\n\n- **Additive.** Its reducer is `operator.add`, so a writer returns *only\nthe delta it just priced* — literally `{\"_session_cost_usd\": 0.02}`,\nnever a replacement total. If a thread starts a turn at $1.00,\n`after_model` contributes $0.02 and a later rubric-grading drain\ncontributes $0.005, the checkpoint ends at $1.025. Neither hook has to\nperform its own read-modify-write.\n- **Private.** It carries `PrivateStateAttr`, keeping cost out of the\ngraph's public input/output contract while leaving it checkpointed and\nreadable through `get_state`. Deep Agents also uses this marker to\nidentify state that must not cross the main-agent/subagent boundary.\n\nThe cumulative channel has one writer: the `CostTrackingMiddleware`\ninstance belonging to the thread's main agent. Subagents run the same\nmiddleware, but theirs is constructed with `nested=True`, which switches\nits pricing off — a subagent's spend is charged by its parent instead,\nas the next section explains.\n\nTo get every completed model call to that writer, the cost-tracking\nmodule installs one process-wide **Recorder**. The Recorder is an\nin-memory inbox for completed model calls, implemented as a LangChain\ncallback (`BaseCallbackHandler`). When a request finishes, it files the\nrequest's usage, model/provider metadata, and message ID under that\nthread. It does not calculate cost or write graph state; it only holds\nrecords until the main agent's middleware drains them.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph calls[\"every model call in the run\"]\n        direction TB\n        A[\"assistant\"]\n        B[\"subagent\"]\n        C[\"offload / summarization\"]\n        D[\"Auto mode classifier\"]\n        E[\"rubric grader\"]\n    end\n    calls --> REC[\"in-memory model-call recorder<br/>collects usage, keyed by thread\"]\n    REC --> MW[\"CostTrackingMiddleware<br/>drains, prices, adds the delta\"]\n    MW --> CK[(\"checkpoint<br/>_session_cost_usd\")]\n    MW -. \"stream event: absolute total\" .-> BAR[\"status bar and /cost\"]\n    CK -. \"resume, thread switch, end of turn\" .-> BAR\n```\n\nThe client is purely a reader; nothing outside the graph writes to the\nchannel.\n\n## Why collecting is split from pricing\n\nThe obvious place to price a request is `after_model`, but that hook\nonly ever sees the agent's own model node, and a large share of a\nthread's spend can happen somewhere else entirely:\n\n| Model call | Runs in |\n| --- | --- |\n| Assistant turn, [Auto\nmode](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4804) classifier |\nmodel node |\n| Offload /\n[summarization](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/context-engineering#summarization)\n| `before_model` (stock) or the model wrap chain (deepagents) |\n| Subagent turns | tool node, in a child graph |\n| `compact_conversation` | tool node |\n| [Rubric\ngrading](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/goals-and-rubrics)\n| `after_agent` |\n\nThe Recorder and the middleware have complementary access:\n\n- The Recorder sits at LangChain's callback layer, so it can observe\nmodel calls made by the main agent, a subagent, summarization, or\nanother direct invocation. But a callback is not a graph node and cannot\nreturn an update to `_session_cost_usd`.\n- `CostTrackingMiddleware` runs inside the main agent's graph, so its\nhooks can return an additive update that the checkpointer persists. But\nthose hooks do not run inside a child graph or around a bare side\ninvocation, so they cannot discover all spend on their own.\n\nThe in-memory queue bridges those two scopes. The callback places one\nrecord in the queue when a request completes; `CostTrackingMiddleware`\ndrains the current thread's records in `after_model` and `after_agent`,\nprices them, and returns their sum as one state update.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>Example: one turn with hidden model work</summary>\n> \n> Suppose a thread already sits at $1.00. Before the main response,\nsummarization spends $0.004; the main response then spends $0.020. The\nRecorder files both completions under the thread. `after_model` drains\nthose two records and writes `+0.024`, taking the checkpoint to $1.024.\n> \n> If rubric grading then spends $0.005 after the final model step,\n`after_agent` drains that later record and writes `+0.005`. The\ncommitted total is $1.029. A subagent call works the same way: its\nrecord waits in the shared thread queue until the parent's next drain.\n> \n> </details>\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>Why the main response is also checked in state</summary>\n> \n> Normally, a main-agent response with message ID `m1` produces a\nRecorder entry for `m1`. The middleware prices that entry, remembers\nthat `m1` was charged, and skips the copy of `m1` already present in\ngraph state.\n> \n> If a custom or third-party integration returns an `AIMessage` with\nusage metadata but no usable callback record was filed — for example,\nthe callback could not associate the request with a thread —\n`after_model` can still price that main response from state. Comparing\nmessage IDs lets the normal and fallback paths coexist without\ndouble-counting. This fallback is limited to the main response; hidden\ncalls are not in the parent's state and therefore still rely on the\nRecorder.\n> \n> </details>\n\n## How subagent spend is counted\n\nAn earlier version of this PR had subagents accumulate into their own\ncopy of the channel and merge the total back. That silently did nothing\nbecause Deep Agents intentionally treats `PrivateStateAttr` as\nagent-local state: `SubAgentMiddleware` discovers those keys and strips\nthem both when seeding a child and when merging its result. This\nprevents one agent's internal bookkeeping from leaking into another and\navoids parallel subagents racing to write private `LastValue` channels.\nA parent-visible aggregate would need a separate shared/public contract;\nfor cost, the thread-keyed recorder supplies that bridge without\nweakening private-state isolation.\n\nSince a subagent inherits its parent's thread ID, its completed model\ncalls land in the same in-memory recorder queue. The parent drains and\nprices those records on its next `after_model` or `after_agent` hook:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant P as Main agent\n    participant R as In-memory recorder\n    participant S as Subagent\n    participant C as Checkpoint\n    P->>R: assistant call usage\n    R-->>P: drain 1 record\n    P->>C: add priced delta\n    P->>S: task tool\n    S->>R: nested call usage\n    Note over S: Nested cost middleware does not<br/>price or accumulate spend\n    S-->>P: result\n    P->>R: next assistant call usage\n    R-->>P: drain nested + assistant records\n    P->>C: add priced delta\n```\n\n## Keeping the status bar live\n\nThe `updates` stream can expose the private channel's writes, but those\nwrites are reducer inputs such as `+0.02`, not the post-reducer lifetime\ntotal. Making the client accumulate them would create a second copy of\nthe graph's state machine, vulnerable to missed stream chunks. Instead,\nthe writer emits a small `custom` event carrying the **absolute** total\nand the client applies it with `set_cost`.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>How an absolute event recovers from a dropped\nupdate</summary>\n> \n> Suppose the client shows $1.00. The graph commits another $0.02 and\nemits `$1.02`, but that event is dropped. A later $0.005 charge emits\n`$1.025`. Because the payload is an absolute value, the client replaces\n$1.00 with $1.025 and is correct again; a delta-only stream would leave\nit permanently short by the missed $0.02. The end-of-turn checkpoint\nread provides another reconciliation point if the final event is the one\nthat disappears.\n> \n> </details>\n\nThe provisional number exists only to make the status bar react before\nthe graph reaches its next cost-tracking hook. These two client-side\nfields have different jobs:\n\n- `_session_cost_usd` is the latest absolute total received from the\ngraph. It is the durable value restored from the checkpoint.\n- `_provisional_cost_usd` is a temporary display estimate derived from\nusage on the message stream. It is never written to graph state.\n\nFor a request estimated at $0.02, the display moves through this\nsequence:\n\n| Moment | Durable total | Provisional | Status bar |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Before the request | $1.00 | $0.00 | $1.00 |\n| Usage arrives on the message stream | $1.00 | $0.02 | $1.02 |\n| The graph emits its new absolute total | $1.02 | $0.00 | $1.02 |\n\nThe last step replaces the durable total and clears the provisional\nbucket, so the same request is not shown twice. The displayed number\nstays steady at $1.02; only its source changes from an early estimate to\ncheckpointed state. On a completed turn, the final checkpoint read\nprovides the same reconciliation if the custom event was missed.\n\n`/cost`'s per-type and per-model rows remain client-side and stay\nlabeled “since this thread was loaded” — only the lifetime total above\nthem comes from the graph.\n\n## Pricing\n\nPricing stays in one place: `estimate_cost` is the only function that\ntouches canonical price data, currently through `genai-prices`. For each\nrequest it needs split input/output token counts, the model, and — when\nthe model name is available from more than one host — the provider.\nProvider names are normalized to the identifiers in the price catalog;\nif response metadata omits the model or provider, the checkpointed model\nspec is the fallback.\n\nHere are the main pricing paths.\n\n**Ordinary input and output.** Suppose a catalog entry charges $2 per\nmillion input tokens and $8 per million output tokens. A request with\n10,000 input tokens and 2,000 output tokens is estimated as:\n\n```text\ninput:  10,000 / 1,000,000 × $2 = $0.020\noutput:  2,000 / 1,000,000 × $8 = $0.016\ntotal:                              $0.036\n```\n\n(Those rates are illustrative; `genai-prices` supplies the actual\nmodel/provider rates.)\n\n**Provider-specific lookup.** The response's provider matters when the\nsame model family is sold through different hosts. For example,\nLangChain's `azure_openai` provider name is normalized to the catalog's\n`azure` identifier, while a direct OpenAI request uses `openai`. This\nprevents a recognizable model name from silently selecting the wrong\nhost's price.\n\n**Cached input.** LangChain's `input_tokens` is inclusive of cache reads\nand writes. If a response reports 1,000 input tokens with 600 cache-read\ntokens and 100 cache-write tokens, only 300 are ordinary input:\n\n```text\nordinary input: 1,000 - 600 - 100 = 300\ncache reads:                            600\ncache writes:                           100\n```\n\n`estimate_cost` passes all three buckets to `genai-prices`, which\napplies the ordinary-input, cache-read, and cache-write rates\nseparately. Output tokens are priced independently. If malformed\nprovider metadata says the cache buckets exceed the inclusive input\ncount, the tracker clamps them to the input total rather than creating a\nnegative ordinary-input count.\n\n**Anthropic cache TTLs.** When Anthropic reports its TTL breakdown,\nLangChain sets generic `cache_creation` to zero and exposes\n`ephemeral_5m_input_tokens` and `ephemeral_1h_input_tokens` instead. If\nthose fields contain 100 and 50 tokens, the tracker passes 150\ncache-write tokens rather than accidentally billing them as ordinary\ninput. `genai-prices` currently exposes one cache-write bucket, so the\ntwo TTL buckets share that catalog estimate.\n\nThe estimator declines to guess when the available data cannot support a\ndefensible calculation:\n\n- A response with only `total_tokens=1_200` is unpriceable because those\ntokens could be input, output, or a mixture, and the rates usually\ndiffer.\n- An unknown model has no canonical catalog rate to apply.\n- Subscription-style access such as the Codex provider is not equivalent\nto per-token API billing.\n- Malformed or non-finite usage/price data is ignored rather than\nallowed to fail the model turn.\n\nIn each case `estimate_cost` returns `None`; the request is omitted from\nthe dollar total while its token usage can still appear in `/tokens`.","tree":{"sha":"cd91603cce772a9ddec317c7a35be91f4525b0ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cd91603cce772a9ddec317c7a35be91f4525b0ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbCOrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/D4QAJP3T7bfcty6rfhlJzWVdJFR\nIrdZHVvVVcHsa1o4ebj2OM/OMQf/iszaSypM1iwcrgFlJEkD3S+/C94GubSbxE9z\nvAK0ZZh9x25oxe+6sWurv47ZTfIZt+621pdjO4rD2vzXZgxG9u1SOLpMit/ZnxiN\nIJh7oQ8LnMC4GJPVbAe2RyE7IgeyK5EOr7deoMdc1Gv/yCJTOUJtQJsWANiX8urb\njhUla4BdIM/xW/HDQeaHxNUbOlO0O9FTKQ3ux6+ddNJIOPxeU0P1X3ErYZk63E44\nkmrvnL/ixhE4dIoTLAduGIcgy3cEoLODsRvvZZ5JmyQ2aSs44Y1EjLRPnsHkYa9A\nXdoYWIs+N/adkHqGnUlE7PxLfLPvXTkM8qeL4EADcSyr+c47HC4xTellXC780VKN\nauIz8IqkwPFLVEeThEajOfZyi09sOHW2mH03Nkl2npgBH9vgyg7FgZzY/9JYLLGY\nqiZSUjfv/1zaOKMNSTytgHWR+g5ntcu0GnhhXH+28maPx+2ceKri9t1je/Id8wjs\nKwN9mNLXIuxVMcrbVus7NLMSL4icaxiaxnzKagZB7x+xB0K6JLmJ3znUiTZxKcXo\nG/eSCifgvZSFciNgofzUB5a8+IaTkv4NOQ1fH28owK2uzV39KfX0fm4u0hdXc9yY\nl2KhORZ+Rl7ScsNgJ9xO\n=ybAX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cd91603cce772a9ddec317c7a35be91f4525b0ec\nparent 53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785471915 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785471915 -0400\n\nfeat(code): running session cost in status bar and usage (#5036)\n\nCloses #4519\n\nDeep Agents Code now keeps a running estimated USD total for the active\nthread. The status bar shows it beside token usage, `/cost` and\n`/tokens` break it down on demand, and usage summaries include per-model\ncost. The total covers everything the thread spends — assistant turns,\nsubagents, offload/compaction, and Auto mode's classifier — and it is\nrestored on resume and thread switches.\n\n---\n\n## Where the number lives\n\nA thread's lifetime cost should be durable to support `--resume` and\nswitching between threads. Consequently, the graph owns it and the\nclient (e.g. TUI / headless CLI) can read it.\n\nConcretely, `_session_cost_usd` is a new channel on the agent's state\nschema (`CostState`, which extends `ResumeState`), which means it is\npersisted by the graph's checkpointer, in the same checkpoint as\n`messages`.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>FAQ: <code>CostState</code>, and why it extends\n<code>ResumeState</code></summary>\n>\n> `CostState` is the [state\nschema](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#schema)\n`CostTrackingMiddleware` declares — the agent's state plus one channel:\n>\n> ```python\n> class CostState(ResumeState):\n> _session_cost_usd: Annotated[NotRequired[float], PrivateStateAttr,\noperator.add]\n> ```\n>\n> **What `ResumeState` already holds.** It's the schema for facts that\nbelong to the thread as a whole rather than to any one message — the\nthings the TUI/client needs the moment you open a thread, before the\nagent runs again:\n>\n> - `_context_tokens` — how full the context window was after the last\nturn. This drives token readout — e.g., the display in the TUI's footer\nstatus bar, where the cost figure now also sits.\n> - `_model_spec` / `_model_params` — the model and settings the thread\nwas using, so `-r` resumes on _that_ model instead of whatever your\ncurrent [global\ndefault](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/config-file#default-and-recent-model)\nmight happen to be.\n> - `_goal_objective`, `_goal_rubric`, `_goal_status`,\n`_goal_status_note`, `_sticky_rubric`, and the pending-proposal fields —\nthe\n[goal](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/goals-and-rubrics)\nthe thread is working toward (if one is set) and where progress on said\ngoal stands.\n>\n> **Every field here is private, including the new one.** A graph has a\npublic interface: its input and output schemas say what callers may pass\nin and receive back (`messages` is the obvious example). None of the\nfields above belong in that interface, as they aren't things a caller\nsupplies or asks for — they're notes that dcode writes for itself so it\ncan pick the thread back up later.\n>\n> `PrivateStateAttr` omits a field from those public input/output\nschemas. It does **not** make the field ephemeral or unreadable: the\nchannel remains ordinary checkpointed state, is available to graph\nnodes, and is returned by `get_state`. Its writes can also appear as raw\ndeltas in the `updates` stream; the live status bar uses a dedicated\nabsolute-total event instead so the client does not have to reproduce\nthe reducer (details below).\n>\n> **These values are stored rather than recomputed**, because\nrecomputing them is expensive or impossible after the fact. Reopening a\nthread has to show the context gauge and the current model immediately.\nThe context number originally came from the last response's\n`usage_metadata` — the provider counted it for us. If it weren't saved,\nthe CLI would have to load the whole message history and count tokens\nitself to guess at it: slow, dependent on having a tokenizer that\nmatches the provider's, and still only an approximation of what was\nactually billed. Cost is the same shape of problem and worse —\nre-deriving it would mean re-pricing every message in the thread every\ntime you open it.\n>\n> **So why extend `ResumeState`?** Cost is the same kind of resumable\nthread fact, and pricing also needs the model information that\n`ResumeState` already carries. LangChain's `AIMessage` contract does not\nrequire a model identifier: `usage_metadata` standardizes token counts,\nwhile `response_metadata` is optional. Provider integrations commonly\ninclude a model name, but custom and third-party integrations are\nallowed to omit it. When a response does, pricing falls back to the\n`_model_spec` persisted for that turn.\n>\n> </details>\n\nRiding the checkpoint is a deliberate choice over an alternative where\nthe client prices a turn and then pushes the new total with\n`aupdate_state`. (That's a second round trip that can be interrupted —\ne.g. `Ctrl-C`, a crash, a dropped connection — *after* the messages have\nalready been committed.) Writing from inside the graph puts the cost in\nthe same commit as the response that incurred it. Importantly, it also\nkeeps an `UpdateState` run/span out of LangSmith traces if configured.\nRestoring is then a single `aget_state` read from the checkpoint.\n\nTwo things about the channel's declaration matter downstream:\n\n- **Additive.** Its reducer is `operator.add`, so a writer returns *only\nthe delta it just priced* — literally `{\"_session_cost_usd\": 0.02}`,\nnever a replacement total. If a thread starts a turn at $1.00,\n`after_model` contributes $0.02 and a later rubric-grading drain\ncontributes $0.005, the checkpoint ends at $1.025. Neither hook has to\nperform its own read-modify-write.\n- **Private.** It carries `PrivateStateAttr`, keeping cost out of the\ngraph's public input/output contract while leaving it checkpointed and\nreadable through `get_state`. Deep Agents also uses this marker to\nidentify state that must not cross the main-agent/subagent boundary.\n\nThe cumulative channel has one writer: the `CostTrackingMiddleware`\ninstance belonging to the thread's main agent. Subagents run the same\nmiddleware, but theirs is constructed with `nested=True`, which switches\nits pricing off — a subagent's spend is charged by its parent instead,\nas the next section explains.\n\nTo get every completed model call to that writer, the cost-tracking\nmodule installs one process-wide **Recorder**. The Recorder is an\nin-memory inbox for completed model calls, implemented as a LangChain\ncallback (`BaseCallbackHandler`). When a request finishes, it files the\nrequest's usage, model/provider metadata, and message ID under that\nthread. It does not calculate cost or write graph state; it only holds\nrecords until the main agent's middleware drains them.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph calls[\"every model call in the run\"]\n        direction TB\n        A[\"assistant\"]\n        B[\"subagent\"]\n        C[\"offload / summarization\"]\n        D[\"Auto mode classifier\"]\n        E[\"rubric grader\"]\n    end\n    calls --> REC[\"in-memory model-call recorder<br/>collects usage, keyed by thread\"]\n    REC --> MW[\"CostTrackingMiddleware<br/>drains, prices, adds the delta\"]\n    MW --> CK[(\"checkpoint<br/>_session_cost_usd\")]\n    MW -. \"stream event: absolute total\" .-> BAR[\"status bar and /cost\"]\n    CK -. \"resume, thread switch, end of turn\" .-> BAR\n```\n\nThe client is purely a reader; nothing outside the graph writes to the\nchannel.\n\n## Why collecting is split from pricing\n\nThe obvious place to price a request is `after_model`, but that hook\nonly ever sees the agent's own model node, and a large share of a\nthread's spend can happen somewhere else entirely:\n\n| Model call | Runs in |\n| --- | --- |\n| Assistant turn, [Auto\nmode](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/4804) classifier |\nmodel node |\n| Offload /\n[summarization](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/context-engineering#summarization)\n| `before_model` (stock) or the model wrap chain (deepagents) |\n| Subagent turns | tool node, in a child graph |\n| `compact_conversation` | tool node |\n| [Rubric\ngrading](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/code/goals-and-rubrics)\n| `after_agent` |\n\nThe Recorder and the middleware have complementary access:\n\n- The Recorder sits at LangChain's callback layer, so it can observe\nmodel calls made by the main agent, a subagent, summarization, or\nanother direct invocation. But a callback is not a graph node and cannot\nreturn an update to `_session_cost_usd`.\n- `CostTrackingMiddleware` runs inside the main agent's graph, so its\nhooks can return an additive update that the checkpointer persists. But\nthose hooks do not run inside a child graph or around a bare side\ninvocation, so they cannot discover all spend on their own.\n\nThe in-memory queue bridges those two scopes. The callback places one\nrecord in the queue when a request completes; `CostTrackingMiddleware`\ndrains the current thread's records in `after_model` and `after_agent`,\nprices them, and returns their sum as one state update.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>Example: one turn with hidden model work</summary>\n> \n> Suppose a thread already sits at $1.00. Before the main response,\nsummarization spends $0.004; the main response then spends $0.020. The\nRecorder files both completions under the thread. `after_model` drains\nthose two records and writes `+0.024`, taking the checkpoint to $1.024.\n> \n> If rubric grading then spends $0.005 after the final model step,\n`after_agent` drains that later record and writes `+0.005`. The\ncommitted total is $1.029. A subagent call works the same way: its\nrecord waits in the shared thread queue until the parent's next drain.\n> \n> </details>\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>Why the main response is also checked in state</summary>\n> \n> Normally, a main-agent response with message ID `m1` produces a\nRecorder entry for `m1`. The middleware prices that entry, remembers\nthat `m1` was charged, and skips the copy of `m1` already present in\ngraph state.\n> \n> If a custom or third-party integration returns an `AIMessage` with\nusage metadata but no usable callback record was filed — for example,\nthe callback could not associate the request with a thread —\n`after_model` can still price that main response from state. Comparing\nmessage IDs lets the normal and fallback paths coexist without\ndouble-counting. This fallback is limited to the main response; hidden\ncalls are not in the parent's state and therefore still rely on the\nRecorder.\n> \n> </details>\n\n## How subagent spend is counted\n\nAn earlier version of this PR had subagents accumulate into their own\ncopy of the channel and merge the total back. That silently did nothing\nbecause Deep Agents intentionally treats `PrivateStateAttr` as\nagent-local state: `SubAgentMiddleware` discovers those keys and strips\nthem both when seeding a child and when merging its result. This\nprevents one agent's internal bookkeeping from leaking into another and\navoids parallel subagents racing to write private `LastValue` channels.\nA parent-visible aggregate would need a separate shared/public contract;\nfor cost, the thread-keyed recorder supplies that bridge without\nweakening private-state isolation.\n\nSince a subagent inherits its parent's thread ID, its completed model\ncalls land in the same in-memory recorder queue. The parent drains and\nprices those records on its next `after_model` or `after_agent` hook:\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant P as Main agent\n    participant R as In-memory recorder\n    participant S as Subagent\n    participant C as Checkpoint\n    P->>R: assistant call usage\n    R-->>P: drain 1 record\n    P->>C: add priced delta\n    P->>S: task tool\n    S->>R: nested call usage\n    Note over S: Nested cost middleware does not<br/>price or accumulate spend\n    S-->>P: result\n    P->>R: next assistant call usage\n    R-->>P: drain nested + assistant records\n    P->>C: add priced delta\n```\n\n## Keeping the status bar live\n\nThe `updates` stream can expose the private channel's writes, but those\nwrites are reducer inputs such as `+0.02`, not the post-reducer lifetime\ntotal. Making the client accumulate them would create a second copy of\nthe graph's state machine, vulnerable to missed stream chunks. Instead,\nthe writer emits a small `custom` event carrying the **absolute** total\nand the client applies it with `set_cost`.\n\n> <details>\n> <summary>How an absolute event recovers from a dropped\nupdate</summary>\n> \n> Suppose the client shows $1.00. The graph commits another $0.02 and\nemits `$1.02`, but that event is dropped. A later $0.005 charge emits\n`$1.025`. Because the payload is an absolute value, the client replaces\n$1.00 with $1.025 and is correct again; a delta-only stream would leave\nit permanently short by the missed $0.02. The end-of-turn checkpoint\nread provides another reconciliation point if the final event is the one\nthat disappears.\n> \n> </details>\n\nThe provisional number exists only to make the status bar react before\nthe graph reaches its next cost-tracking hook. These two client-side\nfields have different jobs:\n\n- `_session_cost_usd` is the latest absolute total received from the\ngraph. It is the durable value restored from the checkpoint.\n- `_provisional_cost_usd` is a temporary display estimate derived from\nusage on the message stream. It is never written to graph state.\n\nFor a request estimated at $0.02, the display moves through this\nsequence:\n\n| Moment | Durable total | Provisional | Status bar |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Before the request | $1.00 | $0.00 | $1.00 |\n| Usage arrives on the message stream | $1.00 | $0.02 | $1.02 |\n| The graph emits its new absolute total | $1.02 | $0.00 | $1.02 |\n\nThe last step replaces the durable total and clears the provisional\nbucket, so the same request is not shown twice. The displayed number\nstays steady at $1.02; only its source changes from an early estimate to\ncheckpointed state. On a completed turn, the final checkpoint read\nprovides the same reconciliation if the custom event was missed.\n\n`/cost`'s per-type and per-model rows remain client-side and stay\nlabeled “since this thread was loaded” — only the lifetime total above\nthem comes from the graph.\n\n## Pricing\n\nPricing stays in one place: `estimate_cost` is the only function that\ntouches canonical price data, currently through `genai-prices`. For each\nrequest it needs split input/output token counts, the model, and — when\nthe model name is available from more than one host — the provider.\nProvider names are normalized to the identifiers in the price catalog;\nif response metadata omits the model or provider, the checkpointed model\nspec is the fallback.\n\nHere are the main pricing paths.\n\n**Ordinary input and output.** Suppose a catalog entry charges $2 per\nmillion input tokens and $8 per million output tokens. A request with\n10,000 input tokens and 2,000 output tokens is estimated as:\n\n```text\ninput:  10,000 / 1,000,000 × $2 = $0.020\noutput:  2,000 / 1,000,000 × $8 = $0.016\ntotal:                              $0.036\n```\n\n(Those rates are illustrative; `genai-prices` supplies the actual\nmodel/provider rates.)\n\n**Provider-specific lookup.** The response's provider matters when the\nsame model family is sold through different hosts. For example,\nLangChain's `azure_openai` provider name is normalized to the catalog's\n`azure` identifier, while a direct OpenAI request uses `openai`. This\nprevents a recognizable model name from silently selecting the wrong\nhost's price.\n\n**Cached input.** LangChain's `input_tokens` is inclusive of cache reads\nand writes. If a response reports 1,000 input tokens with 600 cache-read\ntokens and 100 cache-write tokens, only 300 are ordinary input:\n\n```text\nordinary input: 1,000 - 600 - 100 = 300\ncache reads:                            600\ncache writes:                           100\n```\n\n`estimate_cost` passes all three buckets to `genai-prices`, which\napplies the ordinary-input, cache-read, and cache-write rates\nseparately. Output tokens are priced independently. If malformed\nprovider metadata says the cache buckets exceed the inclusive input\ncount, the tracker clamps them to the input total rather than creating a\nnegative ordinary-input count.\n\n**Anthropic cache TTLs.** When Anthropic reports its TTL breakdown,\nLangChain sets generic `cache_creation` to zero and exposes\n`ephemeral_5m_input_tokens` and `ephemeral_1h_input_tokens` instead. If\nthose fields contain 100 and 50 tokens, the tracker passes 150\ncache-write tokens rather than accidentally billing them as ordinary\ninput. `genai-prices` currently exposes one cache-write bucket, so the\ntwo TTL buckets share that catalog estimate.\n\nThe estimator declines to guess when the available data cannot support a\ndefensible calculation:\n\n- A response with only `total_tokens=1_200` is unpriceable because those\ntokens could be input, output, or a mixture, and the rates usually\ndiffer.\n- An unknown model has no canonical catalog rate to apply.\n- Subscription-style access such as the Codex provider is not equivalent\nto per-token API billing.\n- Malformed or non-finite usage/price data is ignored rather than\nallowed to fail the model turn.\n\nIn each case `estimate_cost` returns `None`; the request is omitted from\nthe dollar total while its token usage can still appear in `/tokens`.","verified_at":"2026-07-31T04:25:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/539d4a04380182438ca63ba6b902eb921dc8a600/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc"}]},{"sha":"53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUzZDFmYjgwY2JkNDNmOTgzNzgyOTc1ZDU0MGZhYzM0YTExYzRjY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T02:44:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T02:44:29Z"},"message":"feat(code): prompt to reconnect when leaving `/mcp` with pending toggles (#5211)\n\n`/mcp`: closing the viewer after disabling/enabling servers now offers\nto reconnect so the change takes effect.\n\n---\n\n`F2` disable/enable toggles in the `/mcp` viewer only take effect after\na server restart, but closing the viewer with Esc left them silently\nunapplied unless the user remembered `Ctrl+R`. Closing the viewer after\na toggle now schedules a `MCPDisableReconnectPromptScreen` action modal:\nEnter reconnects via the same detached-task path as `Ctrl+R`, Esc defers\nwith a reminder toast.\n\nThe prompt is scoped to toggles that are actually still pending, so it\nstays quiet on a plain close, on a toggle that was undone, and on a\npending login (that flow has its own post-login modal). If another modal\nalready owns the screen by the time it fires, it degrades to a toast\npointing at `/mcp reconnect` rather than stacking on top and stealing\nEnter/Esc. Toggles are persisted to `config.toml` either way, so they\napply on next launch even when the reconnect never happens.\n\nBoth prompts in `mcp_reconnect.py` now share a `_ReconnectPromptScreen`\nbase holding the bindings, layout, styling, and the reconnect/defer\ndismissal contract, following the existing `update_confirm.py` pattern.\nSubclasses supply only their title and body copy, so the two dialogs\ncannot drift apart visually or behaviorally.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/47e3ff8c-9f5c-f8a3-15cc-6476a4a187de)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ee2719dc076aff64d3ef06c4caf5a584eb240bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9ee2719dc076aff64d3ef06c4caf5a584eb240bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbAwNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVd4QACHPQtVo/3Uk2g5fUigLEKsJ\nDfcZveQDg9pR1H7RLZbZZqQEAcwfj25QIpnTifwpAlWZzmUDaLSFFraJdPH+fIz6\nyFl527QNG90LGdJm9No6IE2soeNaJ4gsqP+xUtWkT1sQf1AaxUIU58j6RPWfAzUh\nAcqtcUQa5zceeoL5fp7/9+/vo2zlCne/Hqf81Bu2/roVINHk1TP3vk82NP5N6xCZ\nU3RRqC94Aoz0MACRfKYCE+INQCE26u9xKzbhchYNuJNkOVphJHT+dUef33mp79BJ\nIp1ORvlWQTyLWoy1VjpHJkI9aTjpvnDuvUOl55e4RoT0nPEruT0/aB4Hklj60NQR\n3q5TAnFbFtPjAjdSBqK0fnTK43nX3scwrVk8KX40zwGCjse+QYL6DRO0Cb7RePci\nsPJES3S2UeSzeZ8Mh9O+5liJ7NgUbuydEGKqOvEvu5G100uiTlw5/pKTb/EPe4RP\nsD+tAx5gZCogZZhnM4S73g+vpMYA37GMwl0hgICvcOlRhpPGub+aF+qQ8t7f0s78\nvIc5JxZRcw/h7ybq8hEkstXAU1OJlGMVefW0jl0GHbsWR9rIlw45HhFkTwRY84Jt\n+rivkdNeF9nx57i2tpul/zVGvS4c+pgIME9LyRkBExK0cvFntzyUqteZ8AfVwtqH\neEs8CG3/8TIWXMFgp8yr\n=9VCP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ee2719dc076aff64d3ef06c4caf5a584eb240bf\nparent 4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785465869 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785465869 -0400\n\nfeat(code): prompt to reconnect when leaving `/mcp` with pending toggles (#5211)\n\n`/mcp`: closing the viewer after disabling/enabling servers now offers\nto reconnect so the change takes effect.\n\n---\n\n`F2` disable/enable toggles in the `/mcp` viewer only take effect after\na server restart, but closing the viewer with Esc left them silently\nunapplied unless the user remembered `Ctrl+R`. Closing the viewer after\na toggle now schedules a `MCPDisableReconnectPromptScreen` action modal:\nEnter reconnects via the same detached-task path as `Ctrl+R`, Esc defers\nwith a reminder toast.\n\nThe prompt is scoped to toggles that are actually still pending, so it\nstays quiet on a plain close, on a toggle that was undone, and on a\npending login (that flow has its own post-login modal). If another modal\nalready owns the screen by the time it fires, it degrades to a toast\npointing at `/mcp reconnect` rather than stacking on top and stealing\nEnter/Esc. Toggles are persisted to `config.toml` either way, so they\napply on next launch even when the reconnect never happens.\n\nBoth prompts in `mcp_reconnect.py` now share a `_ReconnectPromptScreen`\nbase holding the bindings, layout, styling, and the reconnect/defer\ndismissal contract, following the existing `update_confirm.py` pattern.\nSubclasses supply only their title and body copy, so the two dialogs\ncannot drift apart visually or behaviorally.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/47e3ff8c-9f5c-f8a3-15cc-6476a4a187de)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T02:44:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/53d1fb80cbd43f983782975d540fac34a11c4ccc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c"}]},{"sha":"4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1MDdmOWYxOTg1ZjI5ZTlkNGFmNzU3NzI5M2RhNjRlYzEyYjEzMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T02:32:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T02:32:10Z"},"message":"feat(code): point back to the previous thread after a switch (#5172)\n\nThe REPL now shows a `Previous thread: <id> (Resume with /threads -r)`\nhint after switching threads, matching `/clear`.\n\n---\n\nSwitching threads mid-session (`/threads`, `/threads -r`) replaced the\ntranscript with no way back — the outgoing thread's ID scrolled out of\nreach, unlike `/clear`, which already mounts a `Previous thread: <id>\n(Resume with /threads -r)` hint. The `/clear` logic is extracted into\n`_mount_previous_thread_hint` and reused by the switch path, mounted\ndirectly under the `Resumed thread: <id>` note. Threads with no\ncheckpoint row (i.e. the previous thread was empty) still get no hint,\nsince `-r` can't resume them.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/728d8c08-22a3-c584-6101-365edb6fbfe2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4da62b525d7a94da783fa9626bce1edad0a425f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4da62b525d7a94da783fa9626bce1edad0a425f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbAkqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAnQQABzEEDdTs6JhN8EJilvod0Jg\nEiSkBpXIOFJMxb7uQLt90fGjyLOC+2SW3y2Z05XOstJbMgtZ3+0BdRhxbDYAaKjI\nZP5cNhHmKcH68DOMgnpUH4WUmamQnLTeoya2niWQ2VkQ0ErZDEllKnWQEXIYwkNc\nBH3KPoXkgilubrzkBM7U3raG5qHyj/UVppq+WjcoVcAQLhEkRE64+pSCm9G7vFLA\nXtfSPDrw56G0Im2clUiE26ZQTO4xc78+nBYFyfOJ92ZMxWQzFOTBTxwJFTfOUAVo\n666uQFaHCjKgi86lBEqLWI1VAS9ZpZdCVFMf6e6hVy0x4XKxgq1LcwKTsT5AaiRh\nqdGAT3/KcKwYGEFh+4JZajO39Rk3Yir45k2c/UwhQDv+G+BjlgjItgKLVgz1nDx1\nUYZAu5hb3qK8/hAeIVO9y5hh4ez8An3x9qpPU8ZSlY5GYxYW691QaligPt9Mj6Gv\nd59ZcNDGfM6vN7HJ56oFu9rm2dJRbc5rnfUGwDXPgoV4UdzLEOAla00d6cn/KBiW\nyPdKy8Br1MMU05TpiOMEAyHLwJPPLm/WJNz1nezIAeVkowRomRtH/8TFEmbG8H12\nj7oY8Dvt14eQW0yi/Xx6w83c0uE4FLYyvrOqaSh4LWlnrGp+8tCKPXmzxsUoDmSt\nMYd8HvNGcCL7Q2lNyUs8\n=QXJY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4da62b525d7a94da783fa9626bce1edad0a425f4\nparent 6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785465130 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785465130 -0400\n\nfeat(code): point back to the previous thread after a switch (#5172)\n\nThe REPL now shows a `Previous thread: <id> (Resume with /threads -r)`\nhint after switching threads, matching `/clear`.\n\n---\n\nSwitching threads mid-session (`/threads`, `/threads -r`) replaced the\ntranscript with no way back — the outgoing thread's ID scrolled out of\nreach, unlike `/clear`, which already mounts a `Previous thread: <id>\n(Resume with /threads -r)` hint. The `/clear` logic is extracted into\n`_mount_previous_thread_hint` and reused by the switch path, mounted\ndirectly under the `Resumed thread: <id>` note. Threads with no\ncheckpoint row (i.e. the previous thread was empty) still get no hint,\nsince `-r` can't resume them.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/728d8c08-22a3-c584-6101-365edb6fbfe2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T02:32:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4507f9f1985f29e9d4af7577293da64ec12b131c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff"}]},{"sha":"6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYzMDVmZGJmOGQ5NGQwNjExOTNhOTA4NzE1ZjJjNjI5ODkzYjQ3ZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T00:33:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T00:33:46Z"},"message":"feat(code): drop redundant `shell` and `web_search` prompt guidance (#5213)\n\nTrims two subsections from the `## Tool Usage` section of the\n`deepagents-code` system prompt.\n\n---\n\nThe `### shell` subsection repeated guidance the `execute` tool already\ncarries in its own model-facing description (quoting paths with spaces,\navoiding `cd` in favor of absolute paths), and its suggestion to inspect\nverbose output with `head`/`tail`/`grep` directly contradicted that\ndescription, which tells the model to prefer `read_file`. Static,\nper-tool advice belongs with the tool, not duplicated in the prompt\nwhere the two copies can drift.\n\nThe `### web_search` subsection was a one-line stub fully subsumed by\nthe dedicated web-search section later in the same file.\n\nRetained in `## Tool Usage`: the dynamic filesystem-guidance placeholder\n(conditional on the filesystem tool allowlist, so it cannot live in a\nstatic tool description) and the parallel tool-call guidance plus the\nparallel-fanout schema-error recovery note, which describe cross-tool\norchestration that no single tool description covers and that is not\nreliably injected for non-Anthropic models.\n\nThe system-prompt smoke-test snapshot is regenerated accordingly.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f28cbb41-5b4f-31c7-6ec1-5268ecca4864)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"acfabcee519d2fbeb9d2b416cbecd04e8ae8ca64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/acfabcee519d2fbeb9d2b416cbecd04e8ae8ca64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa+1qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ6EQAHI25DMgH11MO5xq3OI1vv7H\nM3WHbblZ9qCISqTsRl5CGrUGYKSc4KlPU7zkOTnqCRXtJq3Wdyrb+bjFqu3whP+D\nqmuaCdxjs5b0iHjNMmsSiCsysy36kvuMdV8MVa1p7cv8ktr6NoQ/rxDWhFJRFerk\nhyLHE9zMp1qQLjYOE437csUomHNEN5VSznuF4Se0fAEpTw25NZNEselQtKBqjpCN\nCb6hqKiJtwXPqN20YTlRgLXaqhAHh+PJFuMIQc2cY+Pf6Y4NRr+3DPsCjyYjuvhH\nSJTVTV+5brKcoUNHoXqFgSI4hfcH0ZSSb5U/21p1rNhAWDekzrUoS7LLWNg49dk1\nIH7s+ZwZQ9BuVWGo76Vz//Ao3NDpQDLts9NP6Rh4pHJy7BAn0lGNKM7hZSQeNP1X\nVL2nBEmSwspMJGUSjkH3jWVoGfHSA6TsmKKRt3Ah+e6UXwCbn0VqbEkO3GCl6cl4\nOUsWcLqIcu3StqJjadHibvDrRlaAc7N5F918NND01d1AZyJiwknBG+rHEd+Wufkq\nDQacJtUU2EG17r7OQjfmP8kqFn5qHSNx/Ax6kIzUiepsiKZSvRX/7Ha6+d60MOma\nOlzE05/du9T+pi3/QlYzvyB2cppZVkBeJ4cX5mJZeJXKdWWuFXNh6tNKevB95LU6\njoCIPxiSIvj5KissdXYy\n=PNm+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree acfabcee519d2fbeb9d2b416cbecd04e8ae8ca64\nparent ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785458026 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785458026 -0400\n\nfeat(code): drop redundant `shell` and `web_search` prompt guidance (#5213)\n\nTrims two subsections from the `## Tool Usage` section of the\n`deepagents-code` system prompt.\n\n---\n\nThe `### shell` subsection repeated guidance the `execute` tool already\ncarries in its own model-facing description (quoting paths with spaces,\navoiding `cd` in favor of absolute paths), and its suggestion to inspect\nverbose output with `head`/`tail`/`grep` directly contradicted that\ndescription, which tells the model to prefer `read_file`. Static,\nper-tool advice belongs with the tool, not duplicated in the prompt\nwhere the two copies can drift.\n\nThe `### web_search` subsection was a one-line stub fully subsumed by\nthe dedicated web-search section later in the same file.\n\nRetained in `## Tool Usage`: the dynamic filesystem-guidance placeholder\n(conditional on the filesystem tool allowlist, so it cannot live in a\nstatic tool description) and the parallel tool-call guidance plus the\nparallel-fanout schema-error recovery note, which describe cross-tool\norchestration that no single tool description covers and that is not\nreliably injected for non-Anthropic models.\n\nThe system-prompt smoke-test snapshot is regenerated accordingly.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f28cbb41-5b4f-31c7-6ec1-5268ecca4864)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T00:33:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6305fdbf8d94d061193a908715f2c629893b47ff/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9"}]},{"sha":"ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVmM2UwNzg3OTVlMDFiODMzNDE1MTA4MWQwMjZkNmE4ODI2OGQ1YTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-31T00:09:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-31T00:09:54Z"},"message":"fix(code): explain why `doctor` has no latest-version answer (#5209)\n\n`dcode doctor` now says *why* it has no latest-version answer — editable\ninstall, update checks disabled, a stale cache, or no check ever\ncompleted — instead of the blanket `unknown (no recent check)`.\n\n---\n\nThe `Updates` section could render this, which reads as a contradiction:\n\n```txt\nUpdates ✓\n├ Update checks: enabled\n├ Auto-updates: disabled (editable install)\n├ Latest version: unknown (no recent check)\n└ Last checked: 3d ago\n```\n\nBoth rows read the same `checked_at` stamp, but\n`get_cached_update_available` applies the 24h cache TTL while the `Last\nchecked` row does not, and that TTL is invisible in the output. The\nunderlying situation is also worth surfacing: an editable install never\ncontacts PyPI at all (startup auto-update, the in-app background worker,\nand the update command all bail early), so a stamp on disk was written\nby another install sharing the state directory — or, for a regular\ninstall, by a check that has since started failing, since a failed fetch\nleaves the stamp untouched.\n\n`_format_latest_version` now names the cause: `not checked (editable\ninstall)`, `not checked (checks disabled)`, `unknown (cache stale)`, or\n`unknown (never checked)`. A cached answer is still reported whenever\none exists.\n\nRows are deliberately *not* omitted when they are inert. `doctor` output\nis meant to be pasted into bug reports and compared line by line between\na working and a broken machine, so the same four labels always render\nand the `--json` item labels stay stable; the configured `[update]`\nvalues remain visible even on an editable install, where they are\nexactly what a triager asks about. No new helper and no TTL arithmetic\nin `doctor`: a rejected cached answer plus a recorded stamp already\ndistinguishes stale from never checked. Both rows now share a single\nstamp read, so they cannot straddle a concurrent cache refresh and\ndisagree.\n\nFreshness is read separately rather than inferred, via a new\n`is_update_cache_fresh` in the update-check module: a cache can be\ncurrent and still hold no usable answer (only pre-release pins were\nrecorded, or a pre-release install meets a stable-only payload), which\nreports as `unknown (cache incomplete)` so the row never claims an\nexpiry that did not happen. The helper takes the already-read stamp so\nthe file is still read once.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ec7edc1e-d575-f700-e725-0addbcb2a412)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d44fe4390dc2c6a6362d6e2e4bc64c30288e384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3d44fe4390dc2c6a6362d6e2e4bc64c30288e384"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa+fSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAerUQAK5BXJ28y3HVVUlOr1BLnW27\nm0Vz4obj5E5w45oNlVqcXUnCbZ5GzGzb0LTJ3PyDRKBLR6LKw8voiPFVU2PPxLAr\nYHGx0C2lxFOKjCRa/8FUJJ2ziazPAwNErAlcAgVRkBsLs2STHC2lNOPq/VvJmiiF\nzAnrqaXp+nXuiz5wYQ2xb6Zu3DXZDJqPtasbNBoDCqiWrX09zwthH+pZ1aYIvcfH\nRFW4i7V21P9yt+cARfpsOQPjq1ZrGQwsQWuivvN2MXfr5PGWm8sw1XAPr3fwcycz\n38zcTBhF/GeAvy9NPTGk9PvyDxv+Zr7UrCkZ4UmKLd8lF1fMgbdnMbE8wGD/We4C\niuzCzbffKsP/s2LE6r0m+pa7VKkpOvK/11P79z01B6k4Zojx4OwMoorGNm4g08qP\njcQdWHrl4XZYiUiGxB8OlRQfG+ZtGxuUijCQKfYO/ZHx574FP6dGek/wlqgsIeTa\n+9nDcx/OZ9gSjj5DJrAitQ2QriyCCPtwofU2fkiI76v50yI4CY5fKvLHkL0TWx8V\nNV7yyVBlvj9Je8SABsjT5Hu1VHF7s1xZ7W2EBRdq63QOe/V6uqSxqHvziPtdK3ic\n30SGytN2lNgy4sE15uW/ptI3y3YyZMm9CD/HEy7jjRqlga192Sfq0IofyHZmbUBq\nRRiwt05FhEdbF+h+Tx9Q\n=3oeT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3d44fe4390dc2c6a6362d6e2e4bc64c30288e384\nparent 9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785456594 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785456594 -0400\n\nfix(code): explain why `doctor` has no latest-version answer (#5209)\n\n`dcode doctor` now says *why* it has no latest-version answer — editable\ninstall, update checks disabled, a stale cache, or no check ever\ncompleted — instead of the blanket `unknown (no recent check)`.\n\n---\n\nThe `Updates` section could render this, which reads as a contradiction:\n\n```txt\nUpdates ✓\n├ Update checks: enabled\n├ Auto-updates: disabled (editable install)\n├ Latest version: unknown (no recent check)\n└ Last checked: 3d ago\n```\n\nBoth rows read the same `checked_at` stamp, but\n`get_cached_update_available` applies the 24h cache TTL while the `Last\nchecked` row does not, and that TTL is invisible in the output. The\nunderlying situation is also worth surfacing: an editable install never\ncontacts PyPI at all (startup auto-update, the in-app background worker,\nand the update command all bail early), so a stamp on disk was written\nby another install sharing the state directory — or, for a regular\ninstall, by a check that has since started failing, since a failed fetch\nleaves the stamp untouched.\n\n`_format_latest_version` now names the cause: `not checked (editable\ninstall)`, `not checked (checks disabled)`, `unknown (cache stale)`, or\n`unknown (never checked)`. A cached answer is still reported whenever\none exists.\n\nRows are deliberately *not* omitted when they are inert. `doctor` output\nis meant to be pasted into bug reports and compared line by line between\na working and a broken machine, so the same four labels always render\nand the `--json` item labels stay stable; the configured `[update]`\nvalues remain visible even on an editable install, where they are\nexactly what a triager asks about. No new helper and no TTL arithmetic\nin `doctor`: a rejected cached answer plus a recorded stamp already\ndistinguishes stale from never checked. Both rows now share a single\nstamp read, so they cannot straddle a concurrent cache refresh and\ndisagree.\n\nFreshness is read separately rather than inferred, via a new\n`is_update_cache_fresh` in the update-check module: a cache can be\ncurrent and still hold no usable answer (only pre-release pins were\nrecorded, or a pre-release install meets a stable-only payload), which\nreports as `unknown (cache incomplete)` so the row never claims an\nexpiry that did not happen. The helper takes the already-read stamp so\nthe file is still read once.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ec7edc1e-d575-f700-e725-0addbcb2a412)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-31T00:09:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ef3e078795e01b8334151081d026d6a88268d5a9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af"}]},{"sha":"9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhZjQzN2IyZjZhZTlmYTAyMmMzN2MxZjkwNTJkMjNlN2ZjYTYxYWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T23:52:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T23:52:54Z"},"message":"test(infra): de-flake release-notes git history helpers (#5212)\n\nCI hit `subprocess.CalledProcessError ... 'commit', '-m', 'fix(example):\ngenerated 77'] returned non-zero exit status 128` in\n`test_git_log_limits_large_history`, with no way to tell *why* git\nfailed.\n\n---\n\nThe release-notes helper tests build synthetic histories by shelling out\nto git three times per commit. The truncation test created 101 commits\nthat way, so one transient git failure anywhere in the loop fails the\nwhole job. `_commit_many` now writes a batch of commits with a single\n`git fast-import` process, removing ~300 subprocess spawns from that\ntest alone (plus ~150 across the byte-budget and contributor-cap tests)\nand cutting its runtime from ~2s to ~0.6s.\n\nTwo supporting changes make the remaining git usage safer to debug and\nless racy:\n\n- `_git` no longer relies on `check=True`. `str(CalledProcessError)`\nreports only argv and the exit status, which is precisely why the\noriginal failure was undiagnosable; the helper now raises with git's own\n`fatal:` line and both output streams, matching the pattern already used\nfor the Node helper tests.\n- Temporary repositories set `gc.auto=0` and `maintenance.auto=false`,\nso `git commit` never forks background maintenance that can hold the\nrepository locks while the next command runs.\n\nThe underlying `fatal:` line was never captured, so this reduces the\nexposed surface by two orders of magnitude *and* guarantees the next\noccurrence names its own cause instead of a bare exit code.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/598a0622-925d-f68a-006d-66cf035c9cdb)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a0cfb798d9f68bf09f94ffbc79eabf4ce3fad7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5a0cfb798d9f68bf09f94ffbc79eabf4ce3fad7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa+PWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFF4QAGtchW8/gnuojMGoPJbYc4rF\nv/zoQtfg4Qg8XQMb9KopcV4JuHbxIMU5IvPx1sfxrz8dIIUm+CizmGmjB/63iBQA\nrWF//I61gAs4KmKRQM6NqPBAnZ7VYLgSrVnqbZ7Sr5PTulB5D7Bqvwvp2AQhc1a9\nkSZGxHwfQJYFQldbxDiwtyvLEe1AQMJLTdGTEMgU7kioZ/TS6Y1VLHyjwcfdfti1\nsbM78Cu/oPIMNLwmwrBeQ+IlnhHex6A/CExHH3XTNHmMiqemMTK1iArelRFrczU3\n+IssEf6oPKAkovQCw9GVl4JYzZMMCkn1nt8o1GPRVCJ/xXB9SUWMlY66paoDv80J\nkXp9uXq1+Pvhk4XWMESC3+ZLSbGegNiHzapo6EJJe/jD33+9P1H5r9OVvRBzYMzJ\n5B2BZwdCn6BFuURkkrOM5TDhK2yclBSm0mS5cWau9wARmDIRmYzLsru8AioMp4Cf\ngG3FswbQisrziZL7sEC1EeTNr1cLcjp6tqkr/ezdMdl9xshnOkJgAc/HBt+HYde+\nGmFatdFDy/e5kBItyMvd2MYO5eCcfMt/+cNko0kc8gxGoRd7riov2zXVuk4fcEKB\n/yZJMYptyXZ0RffUa+jhanphOKOVuSiHoJNle3wCJEe3qs4tSicR0UxojoEC3zqs\nWb3Ku2PuBiyuakQ2kFYz\n=hobs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5a0cfb798d9f68bf09f94ffbc79eabf4ce3fad7e\nparent 263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785455574 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785455574 -0400\n\ntest(infra): de-flake release-notes git history helpers (#5212)\n\nCI hit `subprocess.CalledProcessError ... 'commit', '-m', 'fix(example):\ngenerated 77'] returned non-zero exit status 128` in\n`test_git_log_limits_large_history`, with no way to tell *why* git\nfailed.\n\n---\n\nThe release-notes helper tests build synthetic histories by shelling out\nto git three times per commit. The truncation test created 101 commits\nthat way, so one transient git failure anywhere in the loop fails the\nwhole job. `_commit_many` now writes a batch of commits with a single\n`git fast-import` process, removing ~300 subprocess spawns from that\ntest alone (plus ~150 across the byte-budget and contributor-cap tests)\nand cutting its runtime from ~2s to ~0.6s.\n\nTwo supporting changes make the remaining git usage safer to debug and\nless racy:\n\n- `_git` no longer relies on `check=True`. `str(CalledProcessError)`\nreports only argv and the exit status, which is precisely why the\noriginal failure was undiagnosable; the helper now raises with git's own\n`fatal:` line and both output streams, matching the pattern already used\nfor the Node helper tests.\n- Temporary repositories set `gc.auto=0` and `maintenance.auto=false`,\nso `git commit` never forks background maintenance that can hold the\nrepository locks while the next command runs.\n\nThe underlying `fatal:` line was never captured, so this reduces the\nexposed surface by two orders of magnitude *and* guarantees the next\noccurrence names its own cause instead of a bare exit code.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/598a0622-925d-f68a-006d-66cf035c9cdb)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T23:52:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9af437b2f6ae9fa022c37c1f9052d23e7fca61af/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a"}]},{"sha":"263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI2M2RkNzJiMWIwM2VjZWU2ZGZiOWQxMmJjZWIwMWI2MjU5YjY5OGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T21:10:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T21:10:55Z"},"message":"build(repo): parameterize coverage flags in Makefile test targets (#5208)\n\nThe release workflow's `Run unit tests` step was disabling coverage\nthrough two compounding mechanisms: `COV_ARGS=` blanked the flag for\npackages that parameterize it (`cli`, `code`), while\n`PYTEST_EXTRA=\"--no-cov\"` leaned on pytest-cov's escape hatch to\nintercept the packages that hardcode `--cov` in their Makefile recipe\n(`deepagents`, `acp`, `talon`, `quickjs`). That coupling is fragile — it\nsilently depends on pytest-cov being installed and on every recipe\ntolerating an empty variable.\n\nThis moves the four hardcoded recipes onto the same `COV_ARGS ?=`\npattern `cli` and `code` already used, so `make test COV_ARGS=` now\ndisables coverage identically across every package. The release step\ndrops `--no-cov` accordingly. Packages that collect no coverage\n(`evals`, `daytona`, `modal`, `runloop`, `vercel`) are untouched —\n`COV_ARGS=` is already a no-op for them.\n\nVerified via `make --dry-run` that each edited package emits `--cov` by\ndefault and a cov-free command under `COV_ARGS=`. CI's reusable\n`_test.yml` (`make test` on the coverage leg, `make test COV_ARGS=`\nelsewhere) is unchanged and now behaves uniformly for the\npreviously-hardcoded packages too.\n\nAlso syncs `libs/acp/uv.lock` to the `deepagents` 0.7.1 release version\n— a pending lockfile update the acp pre-commit hook regenerates on any\ncommit touching `libs/acp/` (the 0.7.1 release PR's `update-lockfiles`\njob did not refresh it).","tree":{"sha":"19e89314cfae5540e772311870e296c08275a422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/19e89314cfae5540e772311870e296c08275a422"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa73fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhf0QAAhmqtY3s4cWPdaaxPogVYoP\ncNPedNXFVLfDK3Rc+UCQR3RcYJ/16ZujlZHMDBMj6KtwSCjQu5Ogn5LDok5mZSlX\nNnfIzMMEEiimp0uRxrS7RtNKtEezx7ZryUynQ/k7WjSgJgnzBKT9AfeH3Y6eqyOB\nwbLYNwdG+mJFSxpJzquwwan3BKzNZ7VD5/uBnMZigecYP2x7L0B7vJ/aCPLZRUj0\n//CveLMdN2ixSnFWUlsN9LvMdkKiTeuFhstphLYYEQsLHXeAbwmeyOAzMrRZoAVH\ni/wm7hvz65n58+NdLqFJakwXfMbSaLwGkaNc51voGz+tXPAewJ3SIoGkWguHMRcl\nJrDdrzOScEh/DoQz+8wFrN9Q++lnG7Vu82wV8JhfSNIkc5IT9fhrEALLqq9XEI6/\nXJssouRJcoJ/xPRKkX2ecczFJFFJR4ZN8Ma40fMHpiemy5m0ETDCMPB2N/rpN+I7\nw0a88Oz+RYOcRGLMNFDWi3+PFDztnUTVRQneNlDJEAMtUR3TpD+TioeIVSLy1D/E\nYBaDxS8Q3fOcxpX2TzC2YACC3aamMvwkyLRGi0JXLhacdHFb7lML1IwN6yfnspWB\nRpi1LOp/gJ7NKH72HxamzRGBsQEpBoyqQJSo07GwBMzZh5rSrCm3cpAORcvPwxr8\nPGFKw5Kn/HN9UJUAYnnk\n=bgVS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 19e89314cfae5540e772311870e296c08275a422\nparent 26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785445855 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785445855 -0400\n\nbuild(repo): parameterize coverage flags in Makefile test targets (#5208)\n\nThe release workflow's `Run unit tests` step was disabling coverage\nthrough two compounding mechanisms: `COV_ARGS=` blanked the flag for\npackages that parameterize it (`cli`, `code`), while\n`PYTEST_EXTRA=\"--no-cov\"` leaned on pytest-cov's escape hatch to\nintercept the packages that hardcode `--cov` in their Makefile recipe\n(`deepagents`, `acp`, `talon`, `quickjs`). That coupling is fragile — it\nsilently depends on pytest-cov being installed and on every recipe\ntolerating an empty variable.\n\nThis moves the four hardcoded recipes onto the same `COV_ARGS ?=`\npattern `cli` and `code` already used, so `make test COV_ARGS=` now\ndisables coverage identically across every package. The release step\ndrops `--no-cov` accordingly. Packages that collect no coverage\n(`evals`, `daytona`, `modal`, `runloop`, `vercel`) are untouched —\n`COV_ARGS=` is already a no-op for them.\n\nVerified via `make --dry-run` that each edited package emits `--cov` by\ndefault and a cov-free command under `COV_ARGS=`. CI's reusable\n`_test.yml` (`make test` on the coverage leg, `make test COV_ARGS=`\nelsewhere) is unchanged and now behaves uniformly for the\npreviously-hardcoded packages too.\n\nAlso syncs `libs/acp/uv.lock` to the `deepagents` 0.7.1 release version\n— a pending lockfile update the acp pre-commit hook regenerates on any\ncommit touching `libs/acp/` (the 0.7.1 release PR's `update-lockfiles`\njob did not refresh it).","verified_at":"2026-07-30T21:10:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/263dd72b1b03ecee6dfb9d12bceb01b6259b698a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511"}]},{"sha":"26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI2NTU3YzM4MWIxNzQ5M2IyY2Y4Njk4YWE2ODdiYzk4MDFmYmQ1MTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T21:04:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T21:04:46Z"},"message":"feat(infra): local rebuild path for GitHub release notes (#5187)\n\nExtract the release-notes job's inline bash body-construction steps into\na shared Python script (.github/scripts/release/build_release_notes.py)\nso maintainers can rebuild the production-shaped GitHub release body\nlocally when the CI notes job fails or produces an empty body after\npublish.\n\nThe script mirrors the CI behavior exactly: changelog extraction,\ncontributor shoutouts, collapsible package-scoped git log, size budget\nand truncation, pre-release banner, and branch provenance annotation. It\nsupports --offline mode for degraded environments and --github-output\nfor CI use.\n\n---\n\nWire release.yml to call the shared script from the release-notes job,\nreplacing the five inline bash steps (resolve-refs, generate-git-log,\nresolve-releaser, generate-release-body, finalize-release-body) with a\nsingle step. The release-body output still flows to mark-release, and\npublish remains independent of notes success.\n\nUpdate tests: add comprehensive unit tests for the shared script in\ntest_build_release_notes.py (46 tests covering version detection,\nchangelog extraction, git log generation, tag resolution, body assembly,\nand size budgets), and slim test_release_git_log.py to cover only the\nsteps that remain inline (setup job's resolve-sha).\n\nDocument the recovery path in RELEASING.md: rebuild body locally with\nthe script, apply with gh release edit --notes-file, verify with gh\nrelease view. Cross-link the existing pre-release enrichment guidance.","tree":{"sha":"455317cba29a959900260144e111af30bc5f2347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/455317cba29a959900260144e111af30bc5f2347"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa7xuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY1MQAJW1oXziQlFIKsNzlTTKMaJI\nb+PqHPtbNZVxRIsr/EnSyqR8ID4DNXWfSzoWGPL/n+10T+r7BUwpqwI5d52Bpj3T\ntgPVvlgTAMQfBxkFz4dKCQg5X0NXuBPCiWtdWAEf/TPZ7lhINTug+cI0fk+DHsyo\nBi3JtDRk+PVVaUyF0jeRHrN1JFs9y2U/I6Yxh2TFLmmMEglt13l/UVYCP1Hr2vPB\n5uwlHR7quTIxCVHjIgba7mLvN3ktgNeE+4QVgkDe9B5JtgOoXjBnO/hYcmCBhN6F\nhqhPh+stgZSVV5H+1Uv4VmSba6xCfm0dYE/Xr5YUkx6I1oGvnykGGNfrhsBmpDBn\n/mQQkALtsX014Xib2X3nKDZq2mAzTrrwl7UBEGO+TAnq8OmbxQBY05e5qm2flzvf\n3EgDGzth7l6JULSdzj8vyB14cDgjJl5Sf3qX/fPQFB7kZjIoyjqjeaJbenSkm/Vu\n4kcrV+iDDplP2Aal+4EnwKEo66XmvYxRqLrMLdSi0fgZnPTcjs1MGVAvFSPW6Vvy\nmFJiv+LCG/ih0RsbykgQcbnM8P4fpilBTkMllZDTSNJVhHluKCTvouO2PeYCIwEL\nM5FmlinEk2yzptTYC2wInamDzpIf3muPbLfIip2iQgD2JVLbTdOxtU+f07ue21fd\nUUZRfUbq/6M305kUEF5x\n=Q8P7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 455317cba29a959900260144e111af30bc5f2347\nparent 6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785445486 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785445486 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): local rebuild path for GitHub release notes (#5187)\n\nExtract the release-notes job's inline bash body-construction steps into\na shared Python script (.github/scripts/release/build_release_notes.py)\nso maintainers can rebuild the production-shaped GitHub release body\nlocally when the CI notes job fails or produces an empty body after\npublish.\n\nThe script mirrors the CI behavior exactly: changelog extraction,\ncontributor shoutouts, collapsible package-scoped git log, size budget\nand truncation, pre-release banner, and branch provenance annotation. It\nsupports --offline mode for degraded environments and --github-output\nfor CI use.\n\n---\n\nWire release.yml to call the shared script from the release-notes job,\nreplacing the five inline bash steps (resolve-refs, generate-git-log,\nresolve-releaser, generate-release-body, finalize-release-body) with a\nsingle step. The release-body output still flows to mark-release, and\npublish remains independent of notes success.\n\nUpdate tests: add comprehensive unit tests for the shared script in\ntest_build_release_notes.py (46 tests covering version detection,\nchangelog extraction, git log generation, tag resolution, body assembly,\nand size budgets), and slim test_release_git_log.py to cover only the\nsteps that remain inline (setup job's resolve-sha).\n\nDocument the recovery path in RELEASING.md: rebuild body locally with\nthe script, apply with gh release edit --notes-file, verify with gh\nrelease view. Cross-link the existing pre-release enrichment guidance.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T21:04:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/26557c381b17493b2cf8698aa687bc9801fbd511/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61