":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3"}]},{"sha":"6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZkYmJiZDE4YjFkZTc1MzEwZDEzZWJmZjBkZDk2Y2EzOTcxZWVjZTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T20:59:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T20:59:13Z"},"message":"chore(code): pin deepagents==0.7.1 (#5207)\n\nBump the `deepagents` SDK pin in `deepagents-code` from `==0.7.0` to\n`==0.7.1` so the next dcode release ships the latest SDK patch release.\n\nLockfile updated via `uv lock`; only the `deepagents` entry changed.","tree":{"sha":"b9c6745a0201985cf6c54a3c6ab67d9cbdd01f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b9c6745a0201985cf6c54a3c6ab67d9cbdd01f66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa7shCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwvgQAKJK0L7s0M20HXLo/2rfwFmX\nous+jv0TmDBLOlLJlW/UoIikpnDjwhCLDSMM3UbIUWwiIdXv986C9MeGjCNEtEsO\nDcUzB1CDfgUXNkg3pCS+VwJcEPQ4W4p+QU0RhRzb/SazuSbgYi9piuzNn3PR5hzq\nS5UjhAboF9AfnJj76Hv7VNe/+dOMIo94cr4y4R70EcmJBumfUfI2fnYClVd7RVqA\nacCrPp4LtsO4q0bH5l5q9dMW/8cAL8HSe4AevGRwy/T6rrNy8/c3ru80sKi0IkBI\ndsmB3RezoKEt8HIJParaxCo36jnbFFUDCwibqjj8osuohx1Y9TRX4ez7XCvBBQaY\nFlsItXAy7viDB5WHkoSebtgwQ8Fg7BtoCqYYIzmxiDYMGcmpFODKx5cdAVKmCIvr\nQHADpRDpFINqhquTVNM49X25oScmJa+4DpPcLWsnF7AWcIp64L0PZQEizRNemeES\nGbOW7z7yVNWyPnyUAJxyLrJUlznRLmiEaa02GnDpYxW7EyBtMCTCN7r1skG8wJ5L\nCsjPkPLjLjhqEsebol5ZsR8ZnG8Ce5LjiAjATRN4czDgg9rdQSOusvlUf6uZREZg\nrJUUngTHyQ6Rdf4fHb8AtUPF8yS+4dH0uqVCJfilewYLuypbQeasvpC0sOAAb0Ey\nGRV/QmhD/KfxSp9Edq/h\n=FFSL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9c6745a0201985cf6c54a3c6ab67d9cbdd01f66\nparent 875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785445153 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785445153 -0400\n\nchore(code): pin deepagents==0.7.1 (#5207)\n\nBump the `deepagents` SDK pin in `deepagents-code` from `==0.7.0` to\n`==0.7.1` so the next dcode release ships the latest SDK patch release.\n\nLockfile updated via `uv lock`; only the `deepagents` entry changed.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T20:59:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6dbbbd18b1de75310d13ebff0dd96ca3971eece3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3"}]},{"sha":"875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg3NTgzNjU0N2YxNDMxNDhmM2JhMTE1ZWJkZDk2OGE1MTk5M2E4ZTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T20:52:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T20:52:49Z"},"message":"fix(infra): run `update-`lockfiles after skipped `trigger-releases` (#5206)\n\nRelease PRs opened or updated by release-please get their `uv.lock`\nfiles regenerated again. The `update-lockfiles` job was silently\nskipping on every push to `main` — the workflow showed green while\nrelease PR lockfiles went stale and the \"🔒 Check Lockfiles\" workflow\nfailed on them — because #5161 put the legitimately-skipped\n`trigger-releases` job in its upstream `needs` chain and the job's bare\n`if:` kept GitHub Actions' implicit `success()` gate. #5169 fixed this\nfor the `release-please` job; this applies the same gating to\n`update-lockfiles` (and audits the remaining downstream jobs).\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n`update-lockfiles` needs `release-please`, which (after #5161)\ntransitively needs `trigger-releases` via `guard-pending-release`. On\nordinary pushes to `main`, `trigger-releases` is skipped — and without a\nstatus-check function in the job's `if:`, Actions' implicit `success()`\ngate on the whole `needs` chain fails closed. The job was skipped with\nan all-green workflow; observed on release PR #5170, where lockfiles had\nto be regenerated by hand.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `update-lockfiles`: `!cancelled()` plus explicit `result == 'success'`\nchecks on every dependency in the chain (`guard-empty-commit`,\n`detect-release-commit`, `guard-pending-release`, `release-please`),\nkeeping the existing `prs != '[]' && prs != ''` requirement. Fail-closed\nsemantics preserved: a crashed guard or unset `prs` still blocks the\njob. `trigger-releases` is deliberately not re-checked — on release\ncommits, `release-please` succeeding already implies the guard saw the\ndispatch succeed.\n- `dispatch-release-notes-check`: audit found its `always()` gate\nalready survived the skipped-`trigger-releases` case, but would also run\nafter a cancelled workflow or red guardians. Added `!cancelled()` and\nthe same hand-checked ancestor results; `update-lockfiles` stays a\nsequencing-only need whose own failure does not block the dispatch.\n- `guard-empty-commit`, `detect-release-commit`, and `trigger-releases`\nneed no changes — their `needs` chains never contain a\nlegitimately-skipped job.\n\nTests pin the new truth tables for both jobs, mirroring the style #5169\nused for `release-please`, and `_evaluate` now handles `always()`.","tree":{"sha":"4dd0a69fb591d4d37d5d49b7b59cf481b087392f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4dd0a69fb591d4d37d5d49b7b59cf481b087392f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa7mhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFBgQAALT7kpUOnUZXwyppBMgNhz3\njkqgnchQQ7bNaTvgZ5XAHaXAigHNWh3zdwA52m3CrrNL8fbuYDoZvcmjrsNvORu7\n/548NNuOxuCiJ3k3EZ69omrHy2Mp8nCA1lw5z+bkzOV2REBVJOLhcfY82G2UuJz7\nhuy2SOG3JvJJ+t63+NTANZ223qhl85ih+gVSHLditpFaBTUyU/hYSRQUT/mbmWrE\nG0DtvgMPGEpjfBoMC+QLeQdUHhC5a0630EvR2E2sz2X3FRu5k17k8vGsbhiiyBWB\nmbKq0eSqF707hFgkqkpqH5ax8WpzswXXIC678K8pkvgB+oAEksbszYHQKDPcBZbj\nbSlwB1kcNhJZcU/Tp0SDxuVgAYmK7rogF5obmVj5AijkYQso5j1joiesCgS2i36v\nks5YLlSdNbMVXuN2Vbm21Ci8tmuyD/34YFx77NI32FE1N6I5ryJB09D6KPri23YR\n5SYGtP04I0noEXAmf+75rbu9TU82V15gJUEG9RD2pBiNHdI2oiKWrX4/YbbX3bkH\nHvYqtOyXHavOQjvEaRWCcVfSjDoy3T7Lk/CWjpKwh3nPUxkumuMKQB8tKKQGd7w6\nDBX6edoze/GPQdbsHCnMlmLmtsO1KD54zbAH9BMnko75krLKQehVdt4Gh4OnrOhr\n8VHhg+8DWJdCuaBA/9Sk\n=ngCJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4dd0a69fb591d4d37d5d49b7b59cf481b087392f\nparent 0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785444769 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785444769 -0400\n\nfix(infra): run `update-`lockfiles after skipped `trigger-releases` (#5206)\n\nRelease PRs opened or updated by release-please get their `uv.lock`\nfiles regenerated again. The `update-lockfiles` job was silently\nskipping on every push to `main` — the workflow showed green while\nrelease PR lockfiles went stale and the \"🔒 Check Lockfiles\" workflow\nfailed on them — because #5161 put the legitimately-skipped\n`trigger-releases` job in its upstream `needs` chain and the job's bare\n`if:` kept GitHub Actions' implicit `success()` gate. #5169 fixed this\nfor the `release-please` job; this applies the same gating to\n`update-lockfiles` (and audits the remaining downstream jobs).\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n`update-lockfiles` needs `release-please`, which (after #5161)\ntransitively needs `trigger-releases` via `guard-pending-release`. On\nordinary pushes to `main`, `trigger-releases` is skipped — and without a\nstatus-check function in the job's `if:`, Actions' implicit `success()`\ngate on the whole `needs` chain fails closed. The job was skipped with\nan all-green workflow; observed on release PR #5170, where lockfiles had\nto be regenerated by hand.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `update-lockfiles`: `!cancelled()` plus explicit `result == 'success'`\nchecks on every dependency in the chain (`guard-empty-commit`,\n`detect-release-commit`, `guard-pending-release`, `release-please`),\nkeeping the existing `prs != '[]' && prs != ''` requirement. Fail-closed\nsemantics preserved: a crashed guard or unset `prs` still blocks the\njob. `trigger-releases` is deliberately not re-checked — on release\ncommits, `release-please` succeeding already implies the guard saw the\ndispatch succeed.\n- `dispatch-release-notes-check`: audit found its `always()` gate\nalready survived the skipped-`trigger-releases` case, but would also run\nafter a cancelled workflow or red guardians. Added `!cancelled()` and\nthe same hand-checked ancestor results; `update-lockfiles` stays a\nsequencing-only need whose own failure does not block the dispatch.\n- `guard-empty-commit`, `detect-release-commit`, and `trigger-releases`\nneed no changes — their `needs` chains never contain a\nlegitimately-skipped job.\n\nTests pin the new truth tables for both jobs, mirroring the style #5169\nused for `release-please`, and `_evaluate` now handles `always()`.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T20:52:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/875836547f143148f3ba115ebdd968a51993a8e3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398"}]},{"sha":"0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBkMzhlYjJkZjM5YjA2NTJkNmYyYWQ5MmU4ZDE0YWU1ZWRjNzgzOTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-30T20:31:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T20:31:50Z"},"message":"release(deepagents): 0.7.1 (#5170)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.7.1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.7.0...deepagents==0.7.1)\n(2026-07-30)\n\n### Features\n\n- Mark editable installs in `lc_versions.deepagents`\n([#5158](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5158))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Return an empty read for degenerate `read_file` windows\n([#5184](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5184))\n- Warn instead of silently skipping unresolved state schemas\n([#5166](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5166))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e961cd09a645328fdad85c8705c3701d55ecb088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e961cd09a645328fdad85c8705c3701d55ecb088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa7S2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqjMQAKSZp8DfSyPLMlFJUqdXRf1O\npQvNP/Xh9EdyWCgBEBrL/8lrcyHxJOPXIr+xzTRwsVokEtZIAVPMCGwLCG9ESPbB\n+v9/0eOvRc4YQsy6uuJQcmY+YJbdnuEl0yTwGU3KlLWM1VhD/GzCxsMXtlvhrRKe\nXwEDS6fkkmtwgPFIkgtVqNGZBWAOIGvtBknaEC6Yfq/YS0TyXCJTiPvuaLi7htro\nasgt3Ucg8upSOoj3npRR7euyByojro6PPBsc8YYw6fHn6Iqke7XiphGP/nz1JDEG\n5JfiIOjS4SOsCsJO5JdQBwdVdSG2vx5xLijyNVYNJEuGeT61vuLaPutDKg8mwAcY\nWjyTSxfw87zThanOdRrSslwb9I+JQpnYfiR1PPsGwmfIYInXcy6KBHhHC9huLTNw\nDplcrBZmmDe9MKDNF+6KOSL5MnJgZYQCjWIvTJAdyERvFL6mppHcm0pjTSyxt+Ii\nYtOR1lU5o4Uxme8AqDI7keGqdNjyX6jyoF3v7fkcZXVQ/jWTz4Q4DCt+D/Gzp0fz\nbM6jWyf7REzii+V1OWW6o41nFCnY16gzs2wMfZ7AEiatyzXOgKWoZVuV6ow3c2/O\n8IjNBFskhchobQN1r+S+U/G5As6solrBcI+iYBIyBks1J/OfMlrtzzfPb/Sfp/2/\ni3/4QM8AtcPnQQ4SEB2U\n=JR78\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e961cd09a645328fdad85c8705c3701d55ecb088\nparent a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785443510 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785443510 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents): 0.7.1 (#5170)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.7.1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.7.0...deepagents==0.7.1)\n(2026-07-30)\n\n### Features\n\n- Mark editable installs in `lc_versions.deepagents`\n([#5158](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5158))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- Return an empty read for degenerate `read_file` windows\n([#5184](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5184))\n- Warn instead of silently skipping unresolved state schemas\n([#5166](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5166))\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T20:31:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0d38eb2df39b0652d6f2ad92e8d14ae5edc78398/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599"}]},{"sha":"a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE0YzE2MDViZDVkNDAzODcxOGVhZDNiNTVhZjYxN2Q2ZWUyZTk1OTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T19:38:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T19:38:14Z"},"message":"chore(deps): sync lockfiles after SDK packaging dep addition (#5204)\n\nRegenerates the per-package `uv.lock` files after `packaging` (>=23.2)\nwas added as a runtime dependency of the `deepagents` SDK.\n\n---\n\nTwo lockfile-only categories of change, no source edits:\n\n- Every package/example lockfile that depends on the local `deepagents`\nSDK now records `packaging` in the SDK's `dependencies` /\n`requires-dist` entries, matching the SDK's `pyproject.toml`.\n- The `evals` and `talon` lockfiles pick up the `deepagents-code` 0.1.49\n→ 0.1.50 version stamp from the latest release.\n\nThis is the standard post-release lockfile sync so the \"check lockfiles\nare up-to-date\" pre-commit hook stays green on `main`.","tree":{"sha":"3e09c1c0878df6c4736e82f653b043b36e48f26d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3e09c1c0878df6c4736e82f653b043b36e48f26d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa6gmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATDsQAAfQ7pu2m0aGbgB11Le/fw+v\n0h+7cNrYdq9/tbcfGGjCmwNDqlijs1PwyTHX2pQwKHeUXy+6rxcrdEZ8xXklBSPs\ns58UxD8Lh8A2j3O6JA/QU9RxUCSwfKMnwUBHEbgw4vB4zO6+S2KajjDpD1gQVnmb\nxrfSFmLNSEkJzcK4xGYj+/itfdaLrrQRyoPCgmYEovIw9ov2H5XsVczhz3QxRiwe\n5J5qmK6utk7M0phI4iZaDP7msipBLqQyfhYoU0X0wi/BSP7uN24UcTAd3EBlo77X\n9VteBE+H/qApLNagfztaPB5rHhMDB6vdejZht5I1MT3JhfPZbU7eRLMXPf7XCcnq\nWfPA3IFq3iBzggLub4SiTVmVw+/uM9gGTsw4wydC86eBrDWk4ChhJ4SSp7FllLwV\n6X8h3X0xiHHNgqnzMsvTiYkVPtET4Klkyc2vKjSBEpseNCmkpRpwk8PyCpusZ0hA\nLhm0snTo4z9B9P2RhNMn5isa/wuHjuFoTpzOlXjzL21V058lRReoNqaP0TYew355\nZJX7MAk7RSEct+sFrfWA9e33F2RL1FHNTJTFGCI622n4T8K8ULjIx7PbOsWQ5g3t\ncvpbFSe/QY5R9b+DPD5MIBAUdY8SRWnbGyo1hh06qL/a3GAaiGvCul3n8zLD32M5\nUeSVjxbudEIKKW1waQcB\n=kd8P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e09c1c0878df6c4736e82f653b043b36e48f26d\nparent a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785440294 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785440294 -0400\n\nchore(deps): sync lockfiles after SDK packaging dep addition (#5204)\n\nRegenerates the per-package `uv.lock` files after `packaging` (>=23.2)\nwas added as a runtime dependency of the `deepagents` SDK.\n\n---\n\nTwo lockfile-only categories of change, no source edits:\n\n- Every package/example lockfile that depends on the local `deepagents`\nSDK now records `packaging` in the SDK's `dependencies` /\n`requires-dist` entries, matching the SDK's `pyproject.toml`.\n- The `evals` and `talon` lockfiles pick up the `deepagents-code` 0.1.49\n→ 0.1.50 version stamp from the latest release.\n\nThis is the standard post-release lockfile sync so the \"check lockfiles\nare up-to-date\" pre-commit hook stays green on `main`.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T19:38:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4c1605bd5d4038718ead3b55af617d6ee2e9599/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d"}]},{"sha":"a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEzZTM3OTg1OTk3MDVhZmQyZDBhM2ZjZTgxMTZkZjYxZjIyYTU1MWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexander Olsen","email":"aolsenjazz@gmail.com","date":"2026-07-30T19:33:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T19:33:57Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide timestamp footers with the rows they belong to (#5167)\n\nTimestamp footers now hide and reappear with the message row they belong\nto.\n\n---\n\nTimestamp footers (`/timestamps`) are sibling widgets trailing each\nmessage in the transcript, so hiding a message row left its footer\nbehind — a stray timestamp floating over nothing. Three paths did this:\n\n- Collapsing a run of tool calls into a step summary hid the tool rows\nand any folded diffs, but not their footers.\n- An approval prompt replacing a tool row hid the row, but not its\nfooter.\n- A summary whose tools all failed removed itself while a folded diff\nwas still attached, stranding that diff and its footer hidden with no\nsummary left to expand them.\n\nFooters are now tracked as accessories of the collapsible they trail,\nand hidden via a marker class rather than by assigning `display`. That\ndistinction is load-bearing: an inline `display` permanently outranks\nthe CSS cascade, so assigning it would strand a footer against the\nuser's `/timestamps` preference for the rest of the session. With a\nclass, the preference survives the fold and reasserts itself on expand.\n\nGroup collapse and approval keep separate marker classes on purpose — a\nfooter can be hidden for both reasons at once, and releasing one must\nnot reveal it while the other still applies.\n\nThe constructor, `add_member`, and `add_collapsible` all register\nthrough a single `_attach_accessories` entry point, so a group's\naccessory map and a tool's own approval linkage cannot drift apart\ndepending on which path folded a row. Every summary releases what it\nstill holds before removing itself, and the mount-failure path rolls\nback everything it may have applied rather than only the `-grouped`\nclass.\n\nFooters are attributed to an owner by their derived DOM id rather than\nposition alone, so an unanticipated transcript shape leaves a footer\nalone instead of folding it into a neighbouring group.\n\n### Testing\n\nCovers the `/timestamps` preference toggled against a collapsed group, a\ngroupable diff folding its own footer, footer release when a failed tool\nis ejected, release when a summary removes itself, the approval\nhide/restore round trip, and footer attribution across run boundaries.\n\nEach of these was checked by mutation — reverting the corresponding\nbehaviour fails the test that covers it. `11368` unit tests pass; `ruff`\nand `ty` are clean.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3ef61997-48ee-568e-ccba-3fcf318db5f0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"58e1934678cb556f810f192b61793e3d91a0aaa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/58e1934678cb556f810f192b61793e3d91a0aaa8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa6clCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhvIQAICzRi8Zx2qev9muCWW/1Nze\n0C8W+TCVcAOqMNeRo2Uzg7JfTPv7y9q6riRSjZs2ziJuvJPIlBdpHi+NfUzKc11+\nD+mXRF1ya+8rnTJ/CxkimMT6XbKPr64TNhVB6l2DpZcdygbpTPNprnJ7s3uXcz2r\njWctGKSrJSMBqMEsRwVrX7GyymL/IdIeN8BM1v5AB/Ua1NnzIkpK5UYR59ACDG/F\npVRNvJhjFoN2BTWmYFfqDy9QNvLLAow5f5nJd3eFzWm5GcCV1kt+w/7EbO2IeE7H\njYlwYUeKe4B64WqKDxNtSSkcxRsnt15rGpI80rXGUwgeuKcV3/6N5/IuSlr6kp1u\nA5VTzK5eIoBrbB+w+iuShURehzRtshleglVs1sJ1vEErBByTB/6qqIKFOvPoqlBl\ntWRe/NW4JB3UaFqB9NYNpS00k2V2KhQcMnAgdsYg82g2k+KiS9hj0Nuv/GnH9Il4\n993VE1velBUA0pJY0bmJYVSOzJcrArtW65HPx7+AA3LtW7putmwprY1E/Sipl+/Y\nkhZvh0oB6j21gZCdNee7yCQRZBrCSfhj/KqE1hfWsMdnwllhEteKM/BJ9jBWNovU\n7fspgCBPjVLnnD+QwhsWYfW52WcfhK61Q+8x7Q0zeTkb45yc6od8zYomOmKIbqvp\nVAwGrYsE8Dum2hMX2Or+\n=q/Mm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 58e1934678cb556f810f192b61793e3d91a0aaa8\nparent 42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767\nauthor Alexander Olsen <aolsenjazz@gmail.com> 1785440037 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785440037 -0400\n\nfix(code): hide timestamp footers with the rows they belong to (#5167)\n\nTimestamp footers now hide and reappear with the message row they belong\nto.\n\n---\n\nTimestamp footers (`/timestamps`) are sibling widgets trailing each\nmessage in the transcript, so hiding a message row left its footer\nbehind — a stray timestamp floating over nothing. Three paths did this:\n\n- Collapsing a run of tool calls into a step summary hid the tool rows\nand any folded diffs, but not their footers.\n- An approval prompt replacing a tool row hid the row, but not its\nfooter.\n- A summary whose tools all failed removed itself while a folded diff\nwas still attached, stranding that diff and its footer hidden with no\nsummary left to expand them.\n\nFooters are now tracked as accessories of the collapsible they trail,\nand hidden via a marker class rather than by assigning `display`. That\ndistinction is load-bearing: an inline `display` permanently outranks\nthe CSS cascade, so assigning it would strand a footer against the\nuser's `/timestamps` preference for the rest of the session. With a\nclass, the preference survives the fold and reasserts itself on expand.\n\nGroup collapse and approval keep separate marker classes on purpose — a\nfooter can be hidden for both reasons at once, and releasing one must\nnot reveal it while the other still applies.\n\nThe constructor, `add_member`, and `add_collapsible` all register\nthrough a single `_attach_accessories` entry point, so a group's\naccessory map and a tool's own approval linkage cannot drift apart\ndepending on which path folded a row. Every summary releases what it\nstill holds before removing itself, and the mount-failure path rolls\nback everything it may have applied rather than only the `-grouped`\nclass.\n\nFooters are attributed to an owner by their derived DOM id rather than\nposition alone, so an unanticipated transcript shape leaves a footer\nalone instead of folding it into a neighbouring group.\n\n### Testing\n\nCovers the `/timestamps` preference toggled against a collapsed group, a\ngroupable diff folding its own footer, footer release when a failed tool\nis ejected, release when a summary removes itself, the approval\nhide/restore round trip, and footer attribution across run boundaries.\n\nEach of these was checked by mutation — reverting the corresponding\nbehaviour fails the test that covers it. `11368` unit tests pass; `ruff`\nand `ty` are clean.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3ef61997-48ee-568e-ccba-3fcf318db5f0)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Olsen <13665641+aolsenjazz@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T19:33:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3e3798599705afd2d0a3fce8116df61f22a551d/comments","author":{"login":"aolsenjazz","id":13665641,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjY1NjQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13665641?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz","html_url":"https://github.com/aolsenjazz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aolsenjazz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767"}]},{"sha":"42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQyZTAxYTk1ODViZTg4NDdhZmY2Yjk3ZTUyMGQ3Yjg0ZGU5MjI3Njc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T19:20:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T19:20:58Z"},"message":"fix(code): release the turn when an interrupted worker never starts (#5196)\n\nPressing `Esc` to interrupt the agent could leave the session\npermanently stuck, unable to accept any new work.\n\n## What users saw\n\nYou interrupt a turn, then try to send a follow-up message. Instead of\ngoing to the agent, it shows up dimmed — queued behind a turn that\nalready ended and will never finish. From there:\n\n- `Esc` just pops the text back into the input box (\"Queued message\nmoved to input\"), and re-submitting queues it again.\n- `/force-clear` doesn't help.\n- The only way out is relaunching the TUI.\n\n## Why it happened\n\nThe session tracks whether the agent is busy with a single flag. While\nthat flag is set, typed messages are queued instead of sent. Only one\npiece of code clears it: the cleanup that runs when a turn finishes.\n\nThe bug is that a turn can end without ever reaching its cleanup. Three\nways that happened:\n\n- **The turn was cancelled before it started running.** Textual marks a\nbackground worker as `RUNNING` the moment it's created, before its code\nactually begins. Interrupting inside that window throws the whole turn\naway without running any of it — including the cleanup — while the\nworker still looks alive from the outside. Later interrupts just\nre-cancel something already dead.\n- **Turn setup ran outside the block cleanup is attached to.**\n`_run_agent_task` had two early-return guard clauses, and it persisted\ngoal/rubric state before entering its `try`. A rejected turn, or an\ninterrupt landing during that setup, skipped cleanup entirely.\n- **The busy flag was set before a worker existed.** `_send_to_agent`\nsets it first so the UI reacts immediately, then does some `await`ed\nsetup before starting the worker. Bailing out during that setup left the\nsession busy with no worker at all.\n\n## The fix\n\nMake it explicit who is responsible for releasing the flag in each case:\n\n- Turn setup moves inside the `try` whose `finally` does the cleanup, so\nany early exit still releases the turn.\n- `_send_to_agent` releases the flag itself when it never got as far as\nstarting a worker.\n- A new `_agent_turn_started` marker lets the interrupt paths tell\n\"cancelled before it ran\" apart from a live turn, and release it\ndirectly.\n\nA message queued behind an abandoned turn is now drained rather than\nstranded.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038692df-2613-b315-330e-00ce0e0d82a2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"80fb68a3a52f1d3e5dcd1a7f4446833a2fd41c67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/80fb68a3a52f1d3e5dcd1a7f4446833a2fd41c67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa6QaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwTIQAJJQ79nW9I6mGXMCuKSrs0m1\ndbn8+aqdAMm71QOg9FuH8SawKEK95nLB68lz9OGLlpwRUKjt0V07YuSPQ6HzzvVn\ncvw/gP3jTZABM8oXy6Umsba3grsltDxKNrcxy8RtJLvimFKRpwSZFeVffGbgTHbT\nOnrdvqazgnVctK6ARjt/lH5bRm6nvLRAQNLmmar2dnqghzJvlLvxDk/zzmDgxStI\np6n3K75NaI1eUct3XX1C0DGf9mYFbpq2mm8aMKQ+pbTY0yLE1saXhq9CCobxyu8u\nCTj8B49GAPw9YskAsed74vSwS72sRQ10wwU4EYFT1E1dvcDbCCvEuknMczlmRL2H\n11BAPaDypQQ56voSqB3eriAEecL4qLCaunN304et4hdiGwp7hyCvJLYPq3iZUQyi\nwpk2FHMESiQSgGMG7UFnhszQwTu6mxdvz88JfhB6qjZqUqdJVKFe+YIO9YoHYRlH\nVZZX/QEOil+pNovpqX9M0oVZUz0eamvvK2SyyqzSNI2oWW2ke6QD6uJuEg0IMztA\nxm99DUI91OrrUN+ZeGD8Bmw72Alt7GWM7acVEMsj33UuMKsgATygeOeltAGg6GzB\nN03GzpEGbMbHSNtQJnSan9qtfCY1iJJ8NGKs/FCujtjOR9AkGXgHlMiFsTSRzYlO\nQK7uGYP6e6f4wXI13hsu\n=ckei\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 80fb68a3a52f1d3e5dcd1a7f4446833a2fd41c67\nparent 6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785439258 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785439258 -0400\n\nfix(code): release the turn when an interrupted worker never starts (#5196)\n\nPressing `Esc` to interrupt the agent could leave the session\npermanently stuck, unable to accept any new work.\n\n## What users saw\n\nYou interrupt a turn, then try to send a follow-up message. Instead of\ngoing to the agent, it shows up dimmed — queued behind a turn that\nalready ended and will never finish. From there:\n\n- `Esc` just pops the text back into the input box (\"Queued message\nmoved to input\"), and re-submitting queues it again.\n- `/force-clear` doesn't help.\n- The only way out is relaunching the TUI.\n\n## Why it happened\n\nThe session tracks whether the agent is busy with a single flag. While\nthat flag is set, typed messages are queued instead of sent. Only one\npiece of code clears it: the cleanup that runs when a turn finishes.\n\nThe bug is that a turn can end without ever reaching its cleanup. Three\nways that happened:\n\n- **The turn was cancelled before it started running.** Textual marks a\nbackground worker as `RUNNING` the moment it's created, before its code\nactually begins. Interrupting inside that window throws the whole turn\naway without running any of it — including the cleanup — while the\nworker still looks alive from the outside. Later interrupts just\nre-cancel something already dead.\n- **Turn setup ran outside the block cleanup is attached to.**\n`_run_agent_task` had two early-return guard clauses, and it persisted\ngoal/rubric state before entering its `try`. A rejected turn, or an\ninterrupt landing during that setup, skipped cleanup entirely.\n- **The busy flag was set before a worker existed.** `_send_to_agent`\nsets it first so the UI reacts immediately, then does some `await`ed\nsetup before starting the worker. Bailing out during that setup left the\nsession busy with no worker at all.\n\n## The fix\n\nMake it explicit who is responsible for releasing the flag in each case:\n\n- Turn setup moves inside the `try` whose `finally` does the cleanup, so\nany early exit still releases the turn.\n- `_send_to_agent` releases the flag itself when it never got as far as\nstarting a worker.\n- A new `_agent_turn_started` marker lets the interrupt paths tell\n\"cancelled before it ran\" apart from a live turn, and release it\ndirectly.\n\nA message queued behind an abandoned turn is now drained rather than\nstranded.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/038692df-2613-b315-330e-00ce0e0d82a2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T19:20:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/42e01a9585be8847aff6b97e520d7b84de922767/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703"}]},{"sha":"6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZiZjNiNjg0NDFlMDRlOWUyNTg4M2E0ZjkxZTZiOGQwZDZjMTU3MDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T18:56:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T18:56:41Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): empty read for degenerate `read_file` windows (#5184)\n\nCloses #5180\n\n`read_file` no longer fails when a model asks for a window that contains\nno lines: a `limit` of zero or less now returns an empty read, and a\nnegative `offset` starts from the first line, matching pre-0.7 behavior.\n\n---\n\n0.7 added pagination metadata to read results, and `ReadResult`\nvalidates that metadata at construction — a line range has to run\nforward and the resume offset has to point at the first un-shown line,\nso a backend can never hand the agent an offset that silently skips\nsource lines. That strictness is deliberate and stays; the bug is that\nthe code paths *producing* those ranges never clamped degenerate tool\narguments, so `limit=0` or `offset=-1` reached the constructor and\nraised instead of reading nothing.\n\nEach read path now floors the requested bounds through one shared helper\nand returns empty content when no lines were asked for — no line range\nto describe, which is how empty files already behave.\n`FilesystemBackend` also drops its own copy of the slicing logic and\nreuses `slice_read_response`, the same helper the state and store\nbackends already use, so local reads and in-memory reads can no longer\ndisagree. The sandbox read runs as a script inside the sandbox and can't\nimport that helper, so it clamps when the command is built and\nshort-circuits a non-positive `limit` on the sandbox side, after the\nnot-found, directory, and binary checks so real failures still take\npriority.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b90d509c-c8fd-c0f2-ed5a-c783be1314ed)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d60f100d395964acf2fcbe52b193e6c2b2e6a7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8d60f100d395964acf2fcbe52b193e6c2b2e6a7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa55pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAYgQAGcsnlgYcD5464Wwqx3FCg/W\n1uzGG0rBA2cTQXzaaY38MYti+SNhBxU8j2VzCweEQO12e48kcPk+wQy0TS8Vd/Li\nZyB/sE1+EYIYVuKJD/vALYNkRLkKPEXOdMR+urNpcYDaEpQZODBbjHKMiJ+7vGxA\np0awRz1o2oc3x/AEB7EMnJyp+Ip4zxEY0rmR/8JvoWS3ZXh0MVRRD6xIwY7VT+sQ\nkikDAMfkHCuju5VqI8+U1sVzN1oZ/A5WW1N1IM+T8O0dYdeAmRBAJIbyzs84VyQs\nQnvdQYBhW7pdHPbf55EyFFQFNr6A2x2cYB+LUfD1rpZwAo+6HDjMq8qujfteK9DS\naLiChHaDxCpHG+DCewneMIhDr2xxrE9aTLyNLjx8563rMAZIU90dO8V45TclAR+F\nR/XBPDlCkIPPLXi78051DQrtomWpvXnmtzJzZmvgViZ862bNpyvXTpK2B3O1Z05m\nAqp37NbIMPbe9oRjkm0RDCmHDRpiagO3ey5CHsEBiNJNb/t+KTcoxdy3TAANl88R\nSHLSVrsT/A9oLGyiV/InlNohPVOn6hhv8fXA1ez0q+MCb8HoGFeAjJNc2vvNMtuz\nR25GUL5JjwmJOIHk7f+NXVqjBvrpfBM5/k4wk97AsHFB3geNNdim1kS7xjVRskGU\nQArA6nEag5QpGJkyk9Q/\n=wmYe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d60f100d395964acf2fcbe52b193e6c2b2e6a7b\nparent 6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785437801 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785437801 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): empty read for degenerate `read_file` windows (#5184)\n\nCloses #5180\n\n`read_file` no longer fails when a model asks for a window that contains\nno lines: a `limit` of zero or less now returns an empty read, and a\nnegative `offset` starts from the first line, matching pre-0.7 behavior.\n\n---\n\n0.7 added pagination metadata to read results, and `ReadResult`\nvalidates that metadata at construction — a line range has to run\nforward and the resume offset has to point at the first un-shown line,\nso a backend can never hand the agent an offset that silently skips\nsource lines. That strictness is deliberate and stays; the bug is that\nthe code paths *producing* those ranges never clamped degenerate tool\narguments, so `limit=0` or `offset=-1` reached the constructor and\nraised instead of reading nothing.\n\nEach read path now floors the requested bounds through one shared helper\nand returns empty content when no lines were asked for — no line range\nto describe, which is how empty files already behave.\n`FilesystemBackend` also drops its own copy of the slicing logic and\nreuses `slice_read_response`, the same helper the state and store\nbackends already use, so local reads and in-memory reads can no longer\ndisagree. The sandbox read runs as a script inside the sandbox and can't\nimport that helper, so it clamps when the command is built and\nshort-circuits a non-positive `limit` on the sandbox side, after the\nnot-found, directory, and binary checks so real failures still take\npriority.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b90d509c-c8fd-c0f2-ed5a-c783be1314ed)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T18:56:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6bf3b68441e04e9e25883a4f91e6b8d0d6c15703/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98"}]},{"sha":"6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZmOWVhNmE5NDNkYWJlNmMwNTU3NjZhNDNhMjA0ZGI2ZjRkOTVjOTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T18:48:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T18:48:54Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep the `/goal` criteria prompt responsive (#5142)\n\nRelated #5086, #5127\n\n`/goal <objective>` and `/goal amend <feedback>` no longer freeze the\nterminal the first time Auto mode asks how to handle generated goal\ncriteria — Enter and Esc now resolve that prompt.\n\n---\n\nSlash commands are dispatched from the App's `on_chat_input_submitted`\nhandler, which is awaited inline on the Textual message pump. The\n`/goal` create and amend branches awaited the one-time \"How should Auto\nmode handle goal criteria?\" modal in that chain, so the pump stayed\nblocked for as long as the modal was open. The modal therefore never\nreceived the Enter/Esc key events it needs to resolve, and because the\nmodal watchdog is ten minutes, the app looked permanently frozen — not\neven the quit binding got through, so users had to kill the terminal.\n\nThis is the same failure #5086 fixed for the post-install restart prompt\nand #5127 fixes for the `/update` and `/install --package` prompts. Only\nthe first Auto-mode `/goal` in a fresh install is affected: once the\npreference is answered (or set in `config.toml` /\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_GOAL_AUTO_ACCEPT_CRITERIA`) no modal opens and the flow\nnever blocks. Launching with `dcode --goal ...` was already fine,\nbecause the startup sequence runs off the pump.\n\nNotes for review:\n\n- The shared tail of both branches moves into `_start_goal_proposal`,\nwhich detaches the flow **only** when the preference prompt is actually\nowed; otherwise it stays inline, so ordinary `/goal` behavior and its\nqueue interaction are unchanged. The proposal coroutine is now built by\na callable so a preflight failure cannot strand it un-awaited.\n- Because the handler returns while the prompt is up, a second `/goal`\n(an external caller, or a queue drain) is refused with a toast instead\nof stacking a modal over an unanswered one, and app teardown cancels a\nflow still parked on the prompt.\n- Fail-closed behavior is unchanged: a timed-out or unmountable prompt\nstill persists \"review before applying\" and records the one-time marker.\n- Tests submit through the real `ChatInput.Submitted` path and press a\nkey; both regression tests wedge the app (pump blocked until the pytest\ntimeout) against the previous code. If #5127 lands first, this detach\ncould be folded into its `_schedule_off_message_pump` helper.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b0872246-9522-6d5b-8f18-aff84ee46dfb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d38e199629e43e7d5406eb92c3a9796021ca11ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d38e199629e43e7d5406eb92c3a9796021ca11ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa5yWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3+QQAHZk96CaH0fsaoK5fsD/YHBj\nTywl5MV03CG9MIpv417BanqbHXkYGzc7NokIi1k2Csb1g7uTXwDLzOnSMV0ZNCqz\nmeUyGCfNwwDGyBT0ydfRxM/+YjpHmo8Gwqch8v8/eCmpB5wWylfuHljcJNWEn/Cz\niD9F/b40F7bn1Pa743awy2/TORKeJASKXIzGyatXNX2giDmMAgU0stdR6r+itOdl\nut+is5D3G2thChH7fX7UCuEDqkAutzSMnqe8aXzqmtNAkvjraR6r7iPhgnX3Qzg4\nhS5r55Q16ouD2SIEiok4AL24Mw3HrEYxnUldxLKQCTDW3poE94MSrdkIxapWoMeY\n3kZLm04JA90DOAHv1tB27NwRWWsR+WdGBNtKEcYzzmoHj0BFKMx+HOB4u3375d0y\nuZtR0kYqu90UUpwyx/j+Bi7MMnDx0IZHHPOkMnx+l0gC73vJ3LuO+su4xdm8W4ZD\nSyj3lE7mHfjvr6QNyC2AloNepa/SeqS21krkoWRSZOcgwTq+ZiT/tO21TciH5A7B\nWMvTvs6bA6lxpJyIDgiOJl5wbgBb+Cl16Qe4mQxb8gSeORNc+G6U8fqIMOw/RjPf\nbHTfuoI32Acl1LlFRqHVXAGZsxLwqUzrvmyBG8S8f8rVYoPJvMAyRFWmdLnOJGua\nP/qJi88hMvHiy9XFBrEz\n=i+uH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d38e199629e43e7d5406eb92c3a9796021ca11ed\nparent 8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785437334 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785437334 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep the `/goal` criteria prompt responsive (#5142)\n\nRelated #5086, #5127\n\n`/goal <objective>` and `/goal amend <feedback>` no longer freeze the\nterminal the first time Auto mode asks how to handle generated goal\ncriteria — Enter and Esc now resolve that prompt.\n\n---\n\nSlash commands are dispatched from the App's `on_chat_input_submitted`\nhandler, which is awaited inline on the Textual message pump. The\n`/goal` create and amend branches awaited the one-time \"How should Auto\nmode handle goal criteria?\" modal in that chain, so the pump stayed\nblocked for as long as the modal was open. The modal therefore never\nreceived the Enter/Esc key events it needs to resolve, and because the\nmodal watchdog is ten minutes, the app looked permanently frozen — not\neven the quit binding got through, so users had to kill the terminal.\n\nThis is the same failure #5086 fixed for the post-install restart prompt\nand #5127 fixes for the `/update` and `/install --package` prompts. Only\nthe first Auto-mode `/goal` in a fresh install is affected: once the\npreference is answered (or set in `config.toml` /\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_GOAL_AUTO_ACCEPT_CRITERIA`) no modal opens and the flow\nnever blocks. Launching with `dcode --goal ...` was already fine,\nbecause the startup sequence runs off the pump.\n\nNotes for review:\n\n- The shared tail of both branches moves into `_start_goal_proposal`,\nwhich detaches the flow **only** when the preference prompt is actually\nowed; otherwise it stays inline, so ordinary `/goal` behavior and its\nqueue interaction are unchanged. The proposal coroutine is now built by\na callable so a preflight failure cannot strand it un-awaited.\n- Because the handler returns while the prompt is up, a second `/goal`\n(an external caller, or a queue drain) is refused with a toast instead\nof stacking a modal over an unanswered one, and app teardown cancels a\nflow still parked on the prompt.\n- Fail-closed behavior is unchanged: a timed-out or unmountable prompt\nstill persists \"review before applying\" and records the one-time marker.\n- Tests submit through the real `ChatInput.Submitted` path and press a\nkey; both regression tests wedge the app (pump blocked until the pytest\ntimeout) against the previous code. If #5127 lands first, this detach\ncould be folded into its `_schedule_off_message_pump` helper.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b0872246-9522-6d5b-8f18-aff84ee46dfb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T18:48:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6f9ea6a943dabe6c055766a43a204db6f4d95c98/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58"}]},{"sha":"8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhmZGI5YzMwNmZkOWE1YjUzNjhlYjA2NWIxMDBjYmZlOGM4Y2JjNTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T18:15:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T18:15:58Z"},"message":"fix(code): resolve underspecified goal objectives from conversation context (#5201)\n\nGoal criteria for underspecified objectives like \"do it\" or \"fix it\" now\nresolve what the objective refers to from conversation context instead\nof producing circular criteria that only restate the objective (e.g.\n\"the requested work is completed as specified\").\n\n---\n\nWhen a goal objective is deictic — a bare imperative or a pointer to\nearlier discussion — the criteria drafter previously had no guidance on\nhow to handle it, and the conversation-context wrapper actively told it\nnot to infer anything from context. The result was criteria that\nasserted completion in the abstract, which a grader cannot evaluate.\n\nThis change adds explicit guidance to the goal/rubric system prompt:\nresolving the referent of an underspecified objective is not \"inventing\nrequirements\", and the drafter should write criteria for the resolved\nwork, naming the concrete files, commands, behavior, or deliverables\ninvolved. Context that discusses work the objective does not ask for\nstill stays out of the criteria — the explicit goal operation remains\nthe scope boundary. If the referent genuinely cannot be determined, the\ndrafter falls back to the most specific criteria the available context\nsupports rather than a tautology.","tree":{"sha":"7cc604e31acc264ae6d13ff0a8013b339ec9d3d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7cc604e31acc264ae6d13ff0a8013b339ec9d3d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa5TeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAht8QAAZZA8DWI05QNAlsNmBaQt9G\neBk6IBOCj9LVod6nuLtvILAuAggMAGXKBIQyCp01lJbkmzI2fyI2VYrR6gmANRhH\nf98JdiaVgW11oV+FC1oYtsQgiWZne7jJFp6euUcPbhieGvTOp4DCEBd8dXJdv/GI\nqg0xGcacRcZnWYyhSfhy66AkTQTufdYZ6bFt4Qzceo1TErfBU4RaQLDE1dBkuqIU\nJePZ3qAyI6WJ52dVqTMBhPb+9FHQ/mdwr4fcqKHc+zMZQE8Hj25eubrGY31vmpNK\nJwFKlxwTqpCuaKdq8v1l5aHtiCU/tbzNLVFjnumCY7IrAT3G+tCi/GFgCFGpFzeP\nqVzUWDrqgsx4Zw5ARe/rADwl+utODF6m/WLRbgXjEN1FrMtMk9ChFIkyHDXZpz3j\nghrOVhmquMg9LCM7kEWLvW9TBxzmmJ+bNZXYQbwK2Kq49cRvwk4WFNB0Qa+fyXs4\nKKMztwgdyZ55tWwLCOQzj9+5lMjZeExltbWEUbPDlvD7ilIeGrJC0/mlKWc7GyAz\nWt68ugQO32cY5enB3+3YyjkoJ9hLiX+zDbf+SCqUYnKoAbBcQeJNycZOYvhdDK/N\nZTX3r1nTv7Lp1x3xgo4HfwE6nSYPPjFHkRFoGoOYZkhE8u6N5DAoezxGG0nTdNPN\nIKnEGQ0/fZHF+X4HQMP9\n=U4Po\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7cc604e31acc264ae6d13ff0a8013b339ec9d3d3\nparent 874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785435358 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785435358 -0400\n\nfix(code): resolve underspecified goal objectives from conversation context (#5201)\n\nGoal criteria for underspecified objectives like \"do it\" or \"fix it\" now\nresolve what the objective refers to from conversation context instead\nof producing circular criteria that only restate the objective (e.g.\n\"the requested work is completed as specified\").\n\n---\n\nWhen a goal objective is deictic — a bare imperative or a pointer to\nearlier discussion — the criteria drafter previously had no guidance on\nhow to handle it, and the conversation-context wrapper actively told it\nnot to infer anything from context. The result was criteria that\nasserted completion in the abstract, which a grader cannot evaluate.\n\nThis change adds explicit guidance to the goal/rubric system prompt:\nresolving the referent of an underspecified objective is not \"inventing\nrequirements\", and the drafter should write criteria for the resolved\nwork, naming the concrete files, commands, behavior, or deliverables\ninvolved. Context that discusses work the objective does not ask for\nstill stays out of the criteria — the explicit goal operation remains\nthe scope boundary. If the referent genuinely cannot be determined, the\ndrafter falls back to the most specific criteria the available context\nsupports rather than a tautology.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T18:15:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8fdb9c306fd9a5b5368eb065b100cbfe8c8cbc58/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2"}]},{"sha":"874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg3NGExMzdmN2JmNjk0ZjY0N2Y2ZjFkY2JjZjU2M2VhZTU1ODllZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T18:15:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T18:15:23Z"},"message":"feat(code): `dcode config get` accepts sections (#5134)\n\n`dcode config get credentials` (and any other config section) now prints\nevery option in that section instead of failing with `unknown option`.\n\n---\n\nInspecting one area of the config surface previously required knowing\neach exact key, because `config get` only accepted a full dotted key. It\nnow also accepts a section: the dotted key prefix shared by its options\n(`credentials`, `display`, `models`, ...), with an optional trailing\ndot, matched case-insensitively. Key prefixes are the only section\nnamespace — display group titles as printed by bare `dcode config`\n(`Credentials`, `Tools`, `Updates`) are not accepted, because a heading\nand the same word as a prefix can name different option sets (`Models`\nthe heading holds 2 options; the `models.*` prefix holds 4, two of which\nrender under the `Tools` heading). One namespace keeps a section\nunambiguous; the trade-off is that headings whose members share no\nprefix (`Tools`, which mixes `shell.*`, `skills.*`, `memory.*`,\n`events.*`, ...) are not reachable as sections. Prefix matching itself\nis case-insensitive, so `get Models` still returns the full `models.*`\nset even though that is also the heading's spelling.\n\nMatching is strict and predictable, resolved by `_select_options`:\n\n1. exact option key → the existing single-option path, unchanged\n2. else a key prefix → every key under that prefix\n3. else the existing unknown-option error (exit `1`)\n\nTruncated guesses (`credential`) and partial leaves (`credentials.open`)\nremain hard errors; no fuzzy or glob matching was added.\n\nSection rendering delegates to the grouped table, verbose view, and JSON\nrow builder that bare `config` already uses, so source resolution and\ncredential redaction are not duplicated — credentials still report\nset/not-set only. Section JSON is always a list (even for a one-option\nsection) so callers can distinguish it from the single-key object, whose\npayload is untouched. `--verbose`/`--all` and `--json` work on either\nside of `get`; the `get` subparser suppresses its own defaults so a flag\nset on the parent `config` parser survives argparse's namespace merge.\n\nA new helper `options_with_key_prefix` was added to the config manifest;\nit is additive.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Unit tests cover exact-key text/JSON shapes staying unchanged,\n`credentials` / `credentials.` / `CREDENTIALS` selecting the same\noptions, sections spanning group headings (`models` includes keys filed\nunder `Tools`), group titles being rejected (`Credentials`, `Tools`,\n`Updates` → exit `1`), one-option sections, verbose catalog fields, and\nrejection of `credential` / `credentials.open` / `nope` with exit `1`.\n- Verified by hand: `dcode config get credentials`, `... credentials\n--json`, `... credentials --verbose`, `... display`, `...\ncredentials.openai --json`, plus the failing cases and bare `dcode\nconfig get`.\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"be7f753348a914e71d8b498f135202976b025606","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/be7f753348a914e71d8b498f135202976b025606"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa5S7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAincQAHVX+BRuuKvda9QjjeXxN+u/\nPaPX7xak21MtJf7xU8Uc9o5gQpOzoyj88Qw08WRczPLeZrlMoafv+Kf7D+AVf0k5\nVLXTAMmetl1XqvYa2LzxaGw7K3ToU8Psgh+g/JKnh1ISSaCNOdfjYU+lAXADNTiw\nQeWHwEZgtUIe9oaNT1J+/9+f6okyPQZJ3SAIR/5FBTS8bqNZqPrWydM2TlHVxkwc\n3ANoF1GuhI0B8BuofB9EqEGEWNi50YC7avcR9NJIz4lUuIdmujXTbcnry4ZXs6Zg\nXwqmbjFmmIvQB6+0yLFqdLUzXCxf/CuEc3Tdn5el3T1rsbvbc8L8/3e/mpxNih36\na/z/9pZ0j26ih9j2sYTVoJxysVj41nZlpTmxUOMCOwLz3vkYhMJc4DIlU7um/AZH\nP6fpePoAWXNPJfKnTzhQDhBf66ouTqWhiSiP/Bbrxm5+40qLW57KE9QUsNHIgPCo\nOJnbpprA2HSyMOiq9iY0D7RGksOXcXBhuDBBg/ibzYGf9XtSa2n48E6t5na5g6QQ\nb8HiPuAgf/lmLvH5k5jOCl5Xf2GOoMNTWwno+0tjUZevjLmRAa8J7XhRRj0UDxUy\n+QrBwceFJZWsNcG+w6e7oj++BPNWKidbRuoXjLamOcOXNGc36qyyeSfv5Bb9OPjb\noBY4poL3glJb5Rr9L20P\n=/7+4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree be7f753348a914e71d8b498f135202976b025606\nparent 4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785435323 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785435323 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `dcode config get` accepts sections (#5134)\n\n`dcode config get credentials` (and any other config section) now prints\nevery option in that section instead of failing with `unknown option`.\n\n---\n\nInspecting one area of the config surface previously required knowing\neach exact key, because `config get` only accepted a full dotted key. It\nnow also accepts a section: the dotted key prefix shared by its options\n(`credentials`, `display`, `models`, ...), with an optional trailing\ndot, matched case-insensitively. Key prefixes are the only section\nnamespace — display group titles as printed by bare `dcode config`\n(`Credentials`, `Tools`, `Updates`) are not accepted, because a heading\nand the same word as a prefix can name different option sets (`Models`\nthe heading holds 2 options; the `models.*` prefix holds 4, two of which\nrender under the `Tools` heading). One namespace keeps a section\nunambiguous; the trade-off is that headings whose members share no\nprefix (`Tools`, which mixes `shell.*`, `skills.*`, `memory.*`,\n`events.*`, ...) are not reachable as sections. Prefix matching itself\nis case-insensitive, so `get Models` still returns the full `models.*`\nset even though that is also the heading's spelling.\n\nMatching is strict and predictable, resolved by `_select_options`:\n\n1. exact option key → the existing single-option path, unchanged\n2. else a key prefix → every key under that prefix\n3. else the existing unknown-option error (exit `1`)\n\nTruncated guesses (`credential`) and partial leaves (`credentials.open`)\nremain hard errors; no fuzzy or glob matching was added.\n\nSection rendering delegates to the grouped table, verbose view, and JSON\nrow builder that bare `config` already uses, so source resolution and\ncredential redaction are not duplicated — credentials still report\nset/not-set only. Section JSON is always a list (even for a one-option\nsection) so callers can distinguish it from the single-key object, whose\npayload is untouched. `--verbose`/`--all` and `--json` work on either\nside of `get`; the `get` subparser suppresses its own defaults so a flag\nset on the parent `config` parser survives argparse's namespace merge.\n\nA new helper `options_with_key_prefix` was added to the config manifest;\nit is additive.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Unit tests cover exact-key text/JSON shapes staying unchanged,\n`credentials` / `credentials.` / `CREDENTIALS` selecting the same\noptions, sections spanning group headings (`models` includes keys filed\nunder `Tools`), group titles being rejected (`Credentials`, `Tools`,\n`Updates` → exit `1`), one-option sections, verbose catalog fields, and\nrejection of `credential` / `credentials.open` / `nope` with exit `1`.\n- Verified by hand: `dcode config get credentials`, `... credentials\n--json`, `... credentials --verbose`, `... display`, `...\ncredentials.openai --json`, plus the failing cases and bare `dcode\nconfig get`.\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T18:15:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/874a137f7bf694f647f6f1dcbcf563eae5589ef2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1"}]},{"sha":"4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2OTNlZTc3NDc3MWM1OTM2ZmZhMTc4MzM5NmFhNGUyMTI2MjExYjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T17:59:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:59:14Z"},"message":"fix(code): correct editable SDK detection to scan and correlate (#5199)\n\n`dcode` now detects an editable `deepagents` SDK install the same way\nthe SDK itself does, so the two stop disagreeing about the same\ninstallation. A trace that previously showed `lc_versions.deepagents =\n\"0.7.0+editable\"` alongside `dcode_client_deepagents_version = \"0.7.0\"`\nfor one install now reports the editable source version on both.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n`_editable_sdk_source_root` answered \"is the installed `deepagents`\neditable, and where is its source?\" with a single\n`importlib.metadata.distribution(\"deepagents\")` lookup and no\ncorrelation against the running package. The SDK's\n`_is_editable_install` does more, and both extra steps guard real\nerrors:\n\n- **Scan every matching distribution instead of one lookup.**\n`setuptools` leaves a gitignored `deepagents.egg-info/` in the source\ntree after any local build, and the cwd is on `sys.path` for `-c`, `-m`,\nand the REPL — so from a checkout that directory is found *first* and\ncarries no `direct_url.json`. The single-lookup form concluded \"not\neditable\" and never consulted the real editable install in\nsite-packages. In that scenario dcode fell back to package metadata for\nthe version while the SDK stamped `+editable`; after this change dcode\ncorrectly reads the version from the checkout's `_version.py`.\n- **Correlate the record with the running package.** An environment can\nhold several `deepagents` records — a wheel earlier on `sys.path` plus\nan unrelated editable checkout later on it. Crediting the wrong one\nlabels a published install as a workspace build.\n\n## What changed\n\ndcode's `_editable_sdk_source_root` now scans every installed\n`deepagents` distribution for a PEP 610 `dir_info.editable: true` record\nand credits it only when its source root contains the package\n`find_spec` would import, mirroring the SDK's logic. The correlation\nanchor is located with `importlib.util.find_spec` rather than an\n`import`, so the existing \"SDK version lookup must not import the SDK\"\ninvariant (`test_dcode_client_deepagents_version_does_not_import_sdk`)\nstill holds. Per-distribution metadata failures are contained so one\nunreadable record cannot abort the scan early; the `distributions()`\nbackstop also swallows `RecursionError` so pathological metadata cannot\nmake the answer depend on iteration order.\n\n**dcode keeps its own copy rather than importing the SDK helper.** The\nSDK's scan lives in the private `_is_editable_install`, which only\nexists in releases newer than dcode's exact `deepagents==0.7.0` pin —\ndelegating would gate this fix on an SDK release and a pin bump, and add\nanother private-SDK coupling. The mirrored tests in\n`test_extras_info.py` keep the two implementations honest.\n\nThe editability tests were reworked to patch the new seams\n(`distributions`, `_running_sdk_package_root`) instead of handing a\nfabricated `direct_url.json` payload to a `distribution()` mock. Some\nexpectations changed for correctness reasons, not just mocking reasons:\nthe egg-info-shadowing case now resolves the editable source version\ninstead of falling back to metadata.\n\n## Behavior change to call out\n\nThis is not pure cleanup. In the egg-info-shadowing scenario dcode\npreviously concluded \"not editable\" and reported the metadata version;\nit now concludes \"editable\" and reports the checkout's source version.\nThat is the intended fix — developer environments will see their SDK\nversion reported as the live source version (matching the SDK's own\ntrace entry) rather than stale install metadata.","tree":{"sha":"965594322fb6d1c566fd2d21bc99a09d73119b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/965594322fb6d1c566fd2d21bc99a09d73119b90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa5DyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhScQAKuKB1ha25UVlZy+VXsSK/wd\ne6pQE0Tetl4ZYfwUdmaxTcGyTCLdv8Rr5ql6Vv8Iv5KnXr9BUdVisYiCOcCauIDa\ngdJoHxjBhOk4JN3nF5ey0ynZ1DzoFtXAp4d8kVYH4Pr7so9oAnXf4cVuP/luhS45\nXHXItjcpbGINVKjTSBs1PnECdILmHh/dXnCMBnmE33BonSFxGAT18qNDAC4ZIfit\nEfBRUSj0pzioPL3AFpBH12d6WIX/a4Wlu1qI2+uAJZe0l7fZ1IPgJaLl1cqKTH5S\nBDEFHFva+jTL6bT2JP1fWDSrUXbllXJJFjCmaoY8r4oWjH9qd8lm3B+NayeA5COV\ngaA7E2NHKF2p7/K5BG3P52LdoxYKVbTbwnSfq4T2VF/0L839P5La06elj9LKEInG\nUmiHAbx8PgEdSdNu5+426X15W9S+YIm2N3y7olVAvmduOxr5Glxih0yW+vRkDXq5\nkkAK4sfSdGCsg6mAMgXGJWn4xn7IbybNMg6UbqXaRAHVey4iHprfrKh/44WK8egC\n5I+9fZ6feq24Yonu5gR8JjpJR948SPGr3gm3QWLotQjdBlA9Nnc5/rH6/Svhrr/y\np+wTqgWWLq4SliojUzKNVK5W65jHiW1hP09XHFQ0zY9kFjiXqCGigF5yPpv8/8eN\nvQDnj1Vhg+ddLWMD3VUL\n=vsWY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 965594322fb6d1c566fd2d21bc99a09d73119b90\nparent 032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785434354 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785434354 -0400\n\nfix(code): correct editable SDK detection to scan and correlate (#5199)\n\n`dcode` now detects an editable `deepagents` SDK install the same way\nthe SDK itself does, so the two stop disagreeing about the same\ninstallation. A trace that previously showed `lc_versions.deepagents =\n\"0.7.0+editable\"` alongside `dcode_client_deepagents_version = \"0.7.0\"`\nfor one install now reports the editable source version on both.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n`_editable_sdk_source_root` answered \"is the installed `deepagents`\neditable, and where is its source?\" with a single\n`importlib.metadata.distribution(\"deepagents\")` lookup and no\ncorrelation against the running package. The SDK's\n`_is_editable_install` does more, and both extra steps guard real\nerrors:\n\n- **Scan every matching distribution instead of one lookup.**\n`setuptools` leaves a gitignored `deepagents.egg-info/` in the source\ntree after any local build, and the cwd is on `sys.path` for `-c`, `-m`,\nand the REPL — so from a checkout that directory is found *first* and\ncarries no `direct_url.json`. The single-lookup form concluded \"not\neditable\" and never consulted the real editable install in\nsite-packages. In that scenario dcode fell back to package metadata for\nthe version while the SDK stamped `+editable`; after this change dcode\ncorrectly reads the version from the checkout's `_version.py`.\n- **Correlate the record with the running package.** An environment can\nhold several `deepagents` records — a wheel earlier on `sys.path` plus\nan unrelated editable checkout later on it. Crediting the wrong one\nlabels a published install as a workspace build.\n\n## What changed\n\ndcode's `_editable_sdk_source_root` now scans every installed\n`deepagents` distribution for a PEP 610 `dir_info.editable: true` record\nand credits it only when its source root contains the package\n`find_spec` would import, mirroring the SDK's logic. The correlation\nanchor is located with `importlib.util.find_spec` rather than an\n`import`, so the existing \"SDK version lookup must not import the SDK\"\ninvariant (`test_dcode_client_deepagents_version_does_not_import_sdk`)\nstill holds. Per-distribution metadata failures are contained so one\nunreadable record cannot abort the scan early; the `distributions()`\nbackstop also swallows `RecursionError` so pathological metadata cannot\nmake the answer depend on iteration order.\n\n**dcode keeps its own copy rather than importing the SDK helper.** The\nSDK's scan lives in the private `_is_editable_install`, which only\nexists in releases newer than dcode's exact `deepagents==0.7.0` pin —\ndelegating would gate this fix on an SDK release and a pin bump, and add\nanother private-SDK coupling. The mirrored tests in\n`test_extras_info.py` keep the two implementations honest.\n\nThe editability tests were reworked to patch the new seams\n(`distributions`, `_running_sdk_package_root`) instead of handing a\nfabricated `direct_url.json` payload to a `distribution()` mock. Some\nexpectations changed for correctness reasons, not just mocking reasons:\nthe egg-info-shadowing case now resolves the editable source version\ninstead of falling back to metadata.\n\n## Behavior change to call out\n\nThis is not pure cleanup. In the egg-info-shadowing scenario dcode\npreviously concluded \"not editable\" and reported the metadata version;\nit now concludes \"editable\" and reports the checkout's source version.\nThat is the intended fix — developer environments will see their SDK\nversion reported as the live source version (matching the SDK's own\ntrace entry) rather than stale install metadata.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T17:59:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4693ee774771c5936ffa1783396aa4e2126211b1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2"}]},{"sha":"032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAzMmVlMTBhZWJlODdmMDNmYTI5ZWI1OTM3YmI3YzRmN2IzMjlhYjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T17:54:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:54:10Z"},"message":"test(code): stop unit tests from tripping the socket guard (#5197)\n\nThe unit suite runs under `--disable-socket`, and pytest-socket emits a\n`UserWarning` from `SocketBlockedError.__init__` itself — so a blocked\nsocket attempt warns even when the calling code catches the error and\ndegrades gracefully. That produced hundreds of `A test tried to use\nsocket.getaddrinfo` / `socket.socket` warnings per run, which is exactly\nthe noise that hides a genuinely new warning.\n\nTwo paths were reaching the guard:\n\n- **Managed ripgrep install.** `_ensure_managed_ripgrep` runs on app\nmount, and with no current `rg` on `PATH` (the norm on CI and in\ncontainers) it downloads a release from GitHub in a worker thread. The\nfailure is swallowed, but every blocked DNS lookup warns, and the\n\"auto-install failed\" toast it posts is stray state for tests that\nassert on toast layout or the notification registry. An autouse fixture\nnow sets the existing production opt-out env var so the install\nshort-circuits before any network work — the same approach already used\nfor the startup update check. Tests that exercise the installer already\nclear that variable themselves.\n- **`ChatOpenAI` construction.** langchain-openai probes a throwaway\nsocket to filter unsupported TCP keepalive options on every\nconstruction. The reasoning-effort integration test now passes explicit\nempty socket options, matching what the Codex-model tests already do.\n\nTest-only; no production behavior changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/160421ef-a69f-9f10-986a-9833c6e9ad39)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"37f34b17a9275c46a23956c257b22d2cb4592ab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/37f34b17a9275c46a23956c257b22d2cb4592ab9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa4/CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGFcQAFvywaamc+t/bCUmW/5cL0i5\nOc6F5a8ijkWfM0K6SEZFAsnVHEhKIiyx0z5Noxic1inirn4TeB7SUH5qF8xM44NS\nzzoL10+yP+jfi2dCQWOhMn81a6YdQvA2JAAKksKD9Z/d4znhL+KDnDeWvvb2Opsd\nUuQ+nk4k8IcsEVPo4WWwU1ueGGkk0lK0pW+tbNZ5Z1kyFihEV8C7l+zALynrZWP+\nGmJMdXHO2DY9QMJT2WzjQPVukbxEHok5EBwfRbcECL/kA9NV+WnA+cbgPmyJvZot\na+zVTDmX0AL0ZuB98ire5hACnhqZgqDTpDngCj5z6ud6R1NHmqKStzkJHtIvtK7U\ntoZgYjzzFOstI9hIn7NPuwZ01J/tm4MsSe+frgi0iHUPGMztlkdEjEyNPt6sPTGg\nRVWvNrDWEojZ6UBB1DX761b+2cJcdEHFNZTk2y/TCTEPFDVs6imj4I8JWntvpsxy\nidLbj2kvpZUIjqmHT13o85WR9XHya1mSRtznncw9SzotxT9egAnZHc4+V/OXkaAG\nSzSp2U1VzbOwUptJP2bbCtKL6ZU81SuBjnvRcqXvfa5onzPLzQYr3TV+vKH1bsmN\nUwum1K4mzGbnNZAOgeIDdeNRE86+mT38xMQp4sl9sTv2DM8Y2aXGPJQIbP0BURGd\noP5Bj7uPtHoRAX2bulJ8\n=p7JL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 37f34b17a9275c46a23956c257b22d2cb4592ab9\nparent 4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785434050 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785434050 -0400\n\ntest(code): stop unit tests from tripping the socket guard (#5197)\n\nThe unit suite runs under `--disable-socket`, and pytest-socket emits a\n`UserWarning` from `SocketBlockedError.__init__` itself — so a blocked\nsocket attempt warns even when the calling code catches the error and\ndegrades gracefully. That produced hundreds of `A test tried to use\nsocket.getaddrinfo` / `socket.socket` warnings per run, which is exactly\nthe noise that hides a genuinely new warning.\n\nTwo paths were reaching the guard:\n\n- **Managed ripgrep install.** `_ensure_managed_ripgrep` runs on app\nmount, and with no current `rg` on `PATH` (the norm on CI and in\ncontainers) it downloads a release from GitHub in a worker thread. The\nfailure is swallowed, but every blocked DNS lookup warns, and the\n\"auto-install failed\" toast it posts is stray state for tests that\nassert on toast layout or the notification registry. An autouse fixture\nnow sets the existing production opt-out env var so the install\nshort-circuits before any network work — the same approach already used\nfor the startup update check. Tests that exercise the installer already\nclear that variable themselves.\n- **`ChatOpenAI` construction.** langchain-openai probes a throwaway\nsocket to filter unsupported TCP keepalive options on every\nconstruction. The reasoning-effort integration test now passes explicit\nempty socket options, matching what the Codex-model tests already do.\n\nTest-only; no production behavior changes.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/160421ef-a69f-9f10-986a-9833c6e9ad39)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T17:54:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/032ee10aebe87f03fa29eb5937bb7c4f7b329ab2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9"}]},{"sha":"4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjMzkzZWFhYTgzMDlkOWFlODBlMzQwNTA0MGM3NGNmZGJmYTIzYTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T17:21:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:21:15Z"},"message":"chore(deps): declare `packaging` in sdk and align editable suffix (#5165)\n\nDeclares `packaging` as an SDK dependency and unifies how editable\ninstalls are marked in `lc_versions`.\n\n---\n\n`deepagents/_version.py` imports `packaging.version`, but `packaging`\nwas absent from the SDK's `dependencies`. It resolves today only\ntransitively via `langchain-core` and `langsmith` — both of which\nrequire it unconditionally — so there is no current breakage. But\nnothing in the SDK's own metadata pins it, and `deepagents/__init__.py`\nimports `_version` unconditionally, so a future `langchain-core`\ndropping `packaging` would break `import deepagents` outright.\n`libs/code` already declares it explicitly.\n\nThe second change aligns dcode's editable marker with the SDK's. The SDK\nstamps `lc_versions[\"deepagents\"]` with a PEP 440 local segment\n(`0.7.0+editable`), while `_format_lc_version` used a parenthesized\nsuffix (`0.8.0 (editable)`). LangChain merges nested metadata\ndictionaries, so both keys land in the same `lc_versions` dict — a\nsingle dcode trace showed two encodings for one concept:\n\n```json\n\"lc_versions\": {\"deepagents\": \"0.7.0+editable\", \"deepagents-code\": \"0.8.0 (editable)\"}\n```\n\nThe local segment is the better of the two: parseable, PEP 440-valid,\nand already what `dcode_client_deepagents_version` reports.\n`_format_lc_version` now delegates to the SDK helper rather than keeping\na third copy of the formatting rule, imported lazily to respect the\ndocumented constraint that `packaging` stay off `config`'s module-import\npath.\n\nBoth lockfiles pick up the new `requires-dist` entry.\n\n## Behavior change\n\nThis changes emitted trace metadata for editable dcode installs from\n`X.Y.Z (editable)` to `X.Y.Z+editable`. Any saved LangSmith view or\nquery filtering on the ` (editable)` spelling needs updating. Only\neditable installs are affected; published installs still report the bare\nrelease version.","tree":{"sha":"5a1b05d17f99537d1c76286ca35157b00ff93724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5a1b05d17f99537d1c76286ca35157b00ff93724"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa4gLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeo4QAHMNCcgolBTUZw+t6FYwejFM\n2dfYl0oabsiBsTORWxW2CW41TfmCxDN2KDyC93tCcUyMj4k1bk5dHCJFtEmQYy5H\nGegVRU4uwL+BmJ8A0UuedwvaNc+rLcfs4LLFoFrUFVNUjaPrJyhB+bdbFz+pEC57\ngn2fdIyV3sMHtbgQ1YLc2BzZbmBuJDIxfjde3GSFqQb476vWfsZGNK9XPTnP91Sy\n04BrtSRyvMm/qyK74b0o46RzhQjWpqq3qgt+7w3/Cm2/0I+dPQl778zdVJdEnrnF\ngMoUYXHfBNbCFqZRJkEc7oQdVQB+v4WcKmViqBq2qVEbMCGaZMF9+hwChmB9EvcJ\n4u5avnJJsOGXy90D4V94YGIBpmL/c9CbD4JycG/WoSPqn5iCDp0dWBtI6YKeeSer\nITliNDH+Km3Dwwr+152flUn5noGgE3K40c7vQvNjZyAhs+KmQsIj4OaJ2gmW9T/f\nVTLpiHerGiasRMbzKYDqwfzyHWSvUYl1oHEO5JGduqW4azZM3iOvkCkqxx1qTfu2\ntcPok0x83FQsg1OxQ/gGxVTxZIhvg98LrknvCp3w3uz+UTV1InehNrDJs7PvBw/N\nY/7wFnUh74bD1pIZfxXkIHwFHipYh0+LR70nmEVpAKh6f0jzaUIu4im1NDNTOHaT\njsQhLstjD0IRi65iqJB6\n=EFOY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5a1b05d17f99537d1c76286ca35157b00ff93724\nparent bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785432075 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785432075 -0400\n\nchore(deps): declare `packaging` in sdk and align editable suffix (#5165)\n\nDeclares `packaging` as an SDK dependency and unifies how editable\ninstalls are marked in `lc_versions`.\n\n---\n\n`deepagents/_version.py` imports `packaging.version`, but `packaging`\nwas absent from the SDK's `dependencies`. It resolves today only\ntransitively via `langchain-core` and `langsmith` — both of which\nrequire it unconditionally — so there is no current breakage. But\nnothing in the SDK's own metadata pins it, and `deepagents/__init__.py`\nimports `_version` unconditionally, so a future `langchain-core`\ndropping `packaging` would break `import deepagents` outright.\n`libs/code` already declares it explicitly.\n\nThe second change aligns dcode's editable marker with the SDK's. The SDK\nstamps `lc_versions[\"deepagents\"]` with a PEP 440 local segment\n(`0.7.0+editable`), while `_format_lc_version` used a parenthesized\nsuffix (`0.8.0 (editable)`). LangChain merges nested metadata\ndictionaries, so both keys land in the same `lc_versions` dict — a\nsingle dcode trace showed two encodings for one concept:\n\n```json\n\"lc_versions\": {\"deepagents\": \"0.7.0+editable\", \"deepagents-code\": \"0.8.0 (editable)\"}\n```\n\nThe local segment is the better of the two: parseable, PEP 440-valid,\nand already what `dcode_client_deepagents_version` reports.\n`_format_lc_version` now delegates to the SDK helper rather than keeping\na third copy of the formatting rule, imported lazily to respect the\ndocumented constraint that `packaging` stay off `config`'s module-import\npath.\n\nBoth lockfiles pick up the new `requires-dist` entry.\n\n## Behavior change\n\nThis changes emitted trace metadata for editable dcode installs from\n`X.Y.Z (editable)` to `X.Y.Z+editable`. Any saved LangSmith view or\nquery filtering on the ` (editable)` spelling needs updating. Only\neditable installs are affected; published installs still report the bare\nrelease version.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T17:21:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c393eaaa8309d9ae80e3405040c74cfdbfa23a9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc"}]},{"sha":"bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJmZDlmMWZlNmQ0OGIzNjI2MTBkZGFmNTc4ZmVlMGYyZTA2NDU4YmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T17:15:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:15:29Z"},"message":"chore(infra): clarify that release-notes edits are optional (#5193)\n\nClarify in the curated release-notes draft comment that editing the\nnotes is optional.\n\n---\n\nThe draft comment posted on release PRs previously read \"Review and edit\nthe release notes between the content markers below.\" Adding \"as needed\"\nmakes it clear maintainers don't have to change anything when the\ngenerated notes are already fine, rather than implying an edit is always\nexpected.","tree":{"sha":"1ccdb35768e29d79d5fb74c5a9c364e98fb98903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1ccdb35768e29d79d5fb74c5a9c364e98fb98903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa4axCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr6YQAAyMkYkOUiui+KcR+KT/eSL8\n5yyvDBZTZijwuXjmnctrw34Dn1BPUdWM9bTGAf8+s4msJWVmLwwovvmnHSb9IMZ2\nKl6aR3d6EYdvVMNxDX6SBGJdkuZ2RFAvY6oVclJBWpV4HltwwbEgdvovoq1iagDn\nsXXjqOQs0NdaIwQZADCvVNzVkaRQVsF9RkLyaBkCtZhE2yDedXhzQbngd4Ztf+9c\nkaLsr9otCq9ga2ul8xr2LUdiGlRr2Vols5RdphY/FEQ7iE+fvTID3uAXZnw/cn+m\nCotrwN8zyrbXJzbhOGq40vVIIGXCGVoJ6Zsuv24tKOkYDX9AH7Da3utvhgZkZxPG\nEqcMc0RO7H9YTsGL6yow0uGplr7FyxVnGnWe726z97QhlvrvsleVM2pncCIrpEpk\nri9fAW64GmzG5k0kbpSVfeUA5F/Z0oJtLQ8JYtx/IXFsRz5JOkZjJTZcZmfFRk5C\nLwFj2qSHVhu9KwbX+hzgXNZKXaek6sh69TBZrfSjog7SLVzqhROGyuJoItlxLaHE\nlquR8yM4p63LRQX77pfMlKjHrSzewvE7DX3Gyo+5QIb6LusnxDvBxHxlfbVQgPD6\n8MAm5xo40LSCBJW0yw6482ulM4flAMDsQCFXjwhR/CSIRKYOZhRrUMvyLm3/qAC5\n4SEsIQ9U7yrUcq51Vz/c\n=k5R8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1ccdb35768e29d79d5fb74c5a9c364e98fb98903\nparent 63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785431729 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785431729 -0400\n\nchore(infra): clarify that release-notes edits are optional (#5193)\n\nClarify in the curated release-notes draft comment that editing the\nnotes is optional.\n\n---\n\nThe draft comment posted on release PRs previously read \"Review and edit\nthe release notes between the content markers below.\" Adding \"as needed\"\nmakes it clear maintainers don't have to change anything when the\ngenerated notes are already fine, rather than implying an edit is always\nexpected.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T17:15:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bfd9f1fe6d48b362610ddaf578fee0f2e06458bc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96"}]},{"sha":"63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYzYWRiOTY0NTY4N2IyNzEwYjNhOGFkZjFlZTkyYzY1M2RkMzdiOTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:13:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T17:13:39Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.50 (#5102)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.50](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.49...deepagents-code==0.1.50)\n(2026-07-30)\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Added project hooks workspace trust and expanded Hooks v2 support with\nclient and server lifecycle events plus runtime feedback\n([#5105](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5105),\n[#5104](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5104),\n[#4997](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4997),\n[#5045](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5045)).\n- Added an option to mute the “YOLO is active” toast\n([#5103](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5103)).\n- Made the splash screen `thread` ID clickable to copy it\n([#5173](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5173)).\n- Show `ask_user` answers directly on the answered tool row\n([#5100](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5100)).\n- Show a toast when submitting an empty required `ask_user` answer\n([#5095](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5095)).\n- Added thread message counts to the Debug Console\n([#5117](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5117)).\n\n### Fixes and improvements\n\n- Gated Hooks v2 behind `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` and improved hook\nresume stability across identity and Command tool results\n([#5146](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5146),\n[#5176](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5176)).\n- Kept server hook state out of task results\n([#5164](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5164)).\n- Stopped duplicate Auto transcript events during interrupt replay\n([#5157](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5157)).\n- Kept `/update` and `/install --package` prompts responsive\n([#5127](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5127)).\n- Refreshed the `/threads` cache after each turn\n([#5174](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5174)).\n- Anchored toasts above the chat input and added a toast when media is\ndropped into a free-text question\n([#5101](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5101),\n[#5099](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5099)).\n- Improved thread status message styling and links\n([#5118](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5118)).\n- Made resume hints echo the launched command name\n([#5119](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5119)).\n- Scoped selection copy to the clicked screen\n([#5140](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5140)).\n- Ignored mouse hits on detached widgets\n([#5114](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5114)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"38f82834e65f30ea420b1f70d2ffdf44ec1f0abf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/38f82834e65f30ea420b1f70d2ffdf44ec1f0abf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa4ZDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM7sQABWJVzVwTzZ9+7aydkqwkzuF\nClrrPrJFWxWLYAPK6PqDpxV1VIMPHD3otCO5Yo4SgD79dcHdCeNwzssM6WWbGpue\n1PrxOlJLgBR7FPAHXevUt4jjobGzVu9i4Y8XExbyoQZCaM0EGK7KewHuaknTrOIv\nkYXmkerIebTxSzxRpx1nm5MD4LO/D0EgNaVgMDhuE+gdwqsFHu+FZlE0m1+QLHeu\nL77hDe58lLtZWih+fiIBWzNy2s5YlJUOK3KXJ/UW7CnHchrSaZHnNzlZipWzcR48\nBvhxRejWKn4Z0g6uJGocn4v52dk8cvD/C48lELM/8LHK6JAeDwTtLI+9zNCslMbn\nf+L4SMLJZpH6dPLGIks9HAvrteJb9AxtkOo0RWq6OihxV4nI2PPc0AKJccPmC4Tw\n4eh5ViP3s2NwQjO40pY+rI++oLiNBebkH4sfsNZAOe8PFwkgzXuahnXkUm/tKIAP\nj2dP32yLKuuO7WoZkoHZzcLR6L2Uisfks7B/8reb2MKmbBOe5Gc+QVJO3/SKdtok\n9JQb8nLaAXSWBh/Y2v6N+kDvzdMDNWYOnPq380FaoCNn0/5Mp6qoFskeBRSqwWk4\naemjjrNaJAcZgzKdzkQLUfGJ+m56t4RSy/4fn2ItErrIBAppBSKJ9F/Daq7sqLcM\nkOMSctYtSsMum0o+CoQW\n=bNen\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38f82834e65f30ea420b1f70d2ffdf44ec1f0abf\nparent 08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785431619 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785431619 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.50 (#5102)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.50](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.49...deepagents-code==0.1.50)\n(2026-07-30)\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Added project hooks workspace trust and expanded Hooks v2 support with\nclient and server lifecycle events plus runtime feedback\n([#5105](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5105),\n[#5104](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5104),\n[#4997](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4997),\n[#5045](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5045)).\n- Added an option to mute the “YOLO is active” toast\n([#5103](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5103)).\n- Made the splash screen `thread` ID clickable to copy it\n([#5173](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5173)).\n- Show `ask_user` answers directly on the answered tool row\n([#5100](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5100)).\n- Show a toast when submitting an empty required `ask_user` answer\n([#5095](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5095)).\n- Added thread message counts to the Debug Console\n([#5117](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5117)).\n\n### Fixes and improvements\n\n- Gated Hooks v2 behind `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` and improved hook\nresume stability across identity and Command tool results\n([#5146](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5146),\n[#5176](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5176)).\n- Kept server hook state out of task results\n([#5164](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5164)).\n- Stopped duplicate Auto transcript events during interrupt replay\n([#5157](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5157)).\n- Kept `/update` and `/install --package` prompts responsive\n([#5127](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5127)).\n- Refreshed the `/threads` cache after each turn\n([#5174](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5174)).\n- Anchored toasts above the chat input and added a toast when media is\ndropped into a free-text question\n([#5101](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5101),\n[#5099](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5099)).\n- Improved thread status message styling and links\n([#5118](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5118)).\n- Made resume hints echo the launched command name\n([#5119](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5119)).\n- Scoped selection copy to the clicked screen\n([#5140](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5140)).\n- Ignored mouse hits on detached widgets\n([#5114](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5114)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T17:13:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63adb9645687b2710b3a8adf1ee92c653dd37b96/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c"}]},{"sha":"08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA4ZTZlOGJhOGQ4ZWE2MjlkNzg5NzY1NDJhMDYxYTJhY2FiMWZhOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T16:36:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T16:36:24Z"},"message":"fix(code): stabilize hook resumes across identity and Command tool results (#5176)\n\nServer-owned hooks now survive resume, so `PostToolUse`,\n`SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, and `Stop` can complete a turn —\nincluding for `Command`-returning tools like `task`.\n\n---\n\nTwo defects aborted server-owned hook resumes:\n\n1. `_invocation_id` hashed `run_id`, which changes on every\n`Command(resume=...)`, so the id the client echoed back never matched\nthe one the server re-derived. Fixed by swapping `run_id` for\n`prompt_id`, which is per-turn but stable across every resume within\nthat turn.\n2. `PostToolUseEvent.result` was typed as a live `Command |\nToolMessage`, and client re-validation of a dumped `Command` raised\n`KeyError: 'tool_call_id'`. Fixed by projecting the tool return through\n`to_wire_tool_result` into `JsonValue` before building the interrupt.\n\n`PreToolUse` was unaffected by (1) because its outcome is replayed from\nstate rather than re-invoked, and (2) only hit `Command`-returning tools\n— so `task` failed where `execute` worked.\n\nKeeping a per-turn value in the identity matters:\n`HookFulfillmentLedger` caches completed responses by `(snapshot_id,\ninvocation_id)`, so if two turns reusing a tool-call id derived the same\nid, the later one would replay the earlier allow/block without running\nits hook.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\nVerified non-interactively with handlers for every event:\n`SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` for Bash\nand `task`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, and `SessionEnd`\nall fire, and the turn completes without error.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"a7b03d8cc76d5dbe1686f9132cafe6e4a99f40a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a7b03d8cc76d5dbe1686f9132cafe6e4a99f40a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa32ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXgkQAGOFtEpRgqMOq4aPkRiGGceK\n7CEOHcZOOTHGOuXW2DCYa7p+C57hQivdtLtR6VBwZGvufg61HWX1ZJFmBHygK4K+\n9N4F+EG0Jm15QEFTMEmPXsGXu+QQ13Z2YOXblNW2dsObDE8J9upvGPtYMvtzXQhl\nPXzxJCE7xAUHX9xNU+PnccF7JR9ZjKGp4P5TKGkD45MYGBaoeBDdhKq+alupTYDb\nrFmMG9zBqnn7ItSz0Blgv0BHOS6a9Hf2z03kEIvG091EaH0nuzNt8PKbjQu1LdWX\nFcQb5Y5oAt0Rnp6ldkjhb5pW8wp3UOw2k4xstCfGQ/7OgQ8nK4bcwLAYgXJrdqyO\n+cM8M9xGx46DWjzm+n8MyhvqMxGE/YLEBcK2zZnyIi72WLrNa25ophcMjU1h6UPL\n13vbGB/ySkEfiX/Jfq0Z4AkVX6UzDb9MqBpeU7v1mZOa+zcW5dNQ+/epR+OZyxPN\n6bGMxSzE+Sm6ULcOKrJigKlMsAZU9HIAxtF9EHouh6p2/Nue75REy906gv3XwFJX\nrp3WdUXpxsdVeAjjzhdXH4XQjYnNz+cu9jHz3JLpPrV9lrN5SJzw0utFGUBkmfyw\nZkNhibgn/EMd1zptQ2oF6o1hDl4evRCsFWAzocEAkoeNdTLqjyQA2W7riYGmTRTF\nl99Rnh+iFZEKmGSamACW\n=YvnZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7b03d8cc76d5dbe1686f9132cafe6e4a99f40a3\nparent ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785429384 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785429384 +0000\n\nfix(code): stabilize hook resumes across identity and Command tool results (#5176)\n\nServer-owned hooks now survive resume, so `PostToolUse`,\n`SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, and `Stop` can complete a turn —\nincluding for `Command`-returning tools like `task`.\n\n---\n\nTwo defects aborted server-owned hook resumes:\n\n1. `_invocation_id` hashed `run_id`, which changes on every\n`Command(resume=...)`, so the id the client echoed back never matched\nthe one the server re-derived. Fixed by swapping `run_id` for\n`prompt_id`, which is per-turn but stable across every resume within\nthat turn.\n2. `PostToolUseEvent.result` was typed as a live `Command |\nToolMessage`, and client re-validation of a dumped `Command` raised\n`KeyError: 'tool_call_id'`. Fixed by projecting the tool return through\n`to_wire_tool_result` into `JsonValue` before building the interrupt.\n\n`PreToolUse` was unaffected by (1) because its outcome is replayed from\nstate rather than re-invoked, and (2) only hit `Command`-returning tools\n— so `task` failed where `execute` worked.\n\nKeeping a per-turn value in the identity matters:\n`HookFulfillmentLedger` caches completed responses by `(snapshot_id,\ninvocation_id)`, so if two turns reusing a tool-call id derived the same\nid, the later one would replay the earlier allow/block without running\nits hook.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\nVerified non-interactively with handlers for every event:\n`SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` for Bash\nand `task`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, and `SessionEnd`\nall fire, and the turn completes without error.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T16:36:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/08e6e8ba8d8ea629d78976542a061a2acab1fa9c/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a"}]},{"sha":"ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVlN2FjM2Q0Nzk4MGU0MDM3NDAzYmZlYTFhMTNiN2I1MWUwNmZiNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T16:06:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T16:06:22Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): mark editable installs in `lc_versions.deepagents` (#5158)\n\nEditable installs of `deepagents` report `lc_versions.deepagents` with a\nPEP 440 local segment — `0.7.0+editable` — so LangSmith traces\ndistinguish a workspace checkout from a published wheel. Published\ninstalls are unaffected.\n\n`create_deep_agent` stamped the hard-coded `__version__`, so both looked\nidentical in traces.\n\n## How detection works\n\n`_is_editable_install()` looks for an installed distribution named\n`deepagents` whose PEP 610 `direct_url.json` marks it editable, and\ncredits it only when its recorded source root contains the module being\nimported.\n\nBoth halves matter, and they guard opposite errors:\n\n- **Scanning all distributions**, rather than one\n`importlib.metadata.distribution()` lookup, avoids a false negative.\n`setuptools` leaves a gitignored `deepagents.egg-info/` in the source\ntree, and the cwd is on `sys.path` for `-c`, `-m`, and the REPL — so\nfrom a checkout that directory is found first, and it has no\n`direct_url.json`. A single lookup therefore reports \"not editable\" for\na genuinely editable install.\n- **Correlating with the running module** avoids a false positive. An\nenvironment can hold several `deepagents` records, such as a wheel plus\nan unrelated editable checkout. Only one supplies the imported code;\ncrediting the other would label a published install as a workspace\nbuild.\n\nMetadata failures are contained per distribution, so a single unreadable\nor corrupt distribution can neither end the scan early nor propagate out\nof `create_deep_agent`. Anything unreadable, unparseable, or unlocatable\nreports the plain release version.\n\nThe result is cached — install layout is fixed for the life of the\nprocess, and this runs on every `create_deep_agent()` call.","tree":{"sha":"03ea97df2635c6955a0c54da77b57bc69404d5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/03ea97df2635c6955a0c54da77b57bc69404d5b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa3Z+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI2cQAH4OAI2OY5/J17TahUgWKexO\nJHt1ExBHWwZYwGJctCLzV3shuFFHUUhLXppxH0RBecYSxtFRrHdOFKeeYvdYPzoA\nbXiqOrFT7TsyKNwRpDgXmhf2R1vEySWNeIkauW4pb9HsTM6xKG6y+h+xAeTLEN5M\nlsSoqs7/QzVCkRDR/wGe++posdwnwRTSB28LfgVaZSgaUbJdizds+m2J4yaKX4Tc\nHm/W5jlAxm5EgNFNQlhZms3SMrig7LqB770Nj8VEwC+HVJTZRQCIZ/URjDSIvmWS\nLD58hKlzBxo3VFpnRIxFdj1Ni+9PNqDoFuJlMbS7SvQsZ5+d2odZrf2Xi7lTlZW8\nQhgrOUiLKTlNRUB2r+vjJyjH+M1EM3zh5zi8Yk2vkABkd1VO/0ORvwHeRTbABLh1\n3CdUHn1+rWeQC5q6YsgtrkBq0AN7QOM9WOUkw1to+kWjsKncT5b2RgmRmqi0rllY\nfwCVDgAXf8F2W3NxUX0FFAiRrrtssCxuUEs9HXFWOPFxLTMt6O2qex+Ogs24Py3T\nmrz2tBp7R0ATbTa2FNW37ki/rlZvx+iBTZzrEo5z2J7fgt9tnkt5WWusho8cjGfQ\nxNuOhBfcSS8SbWTOWTgVx/WK44GUXoDFzXxeiAmMul06MvjwJLKyGZ25gXd3hogY\nAxyl6uFn8JAar3F3FQof\n=n37t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 03ea97df2635c6955a0c54da77b57bc69404d5b6\nparent 5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785427582 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785427582 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): mark editable installs in `lc_versions.deepagents` (#5158)\n\nEditable installs of `deepagents` report `lc_versions.deepagents` with a\nPEP 440 local segment — `0.7.0+editable` — so LangSmith traces\ndistinguish a workspace checkout from a published wheel. Published\ninstalls are unaffected.\n\n`create_deep_agent` stamped the hard-coded `__version__`, so both looked\nidentical in traces.\n\n## How detection works\n\n`_is_editable_install()` looks for an installed distribution named\n`deepagents` whose PEP 610 `direct_url.json` marks it editable, and\ncredits it only when its recorded source root contains the module being\nimported.\n\nBoth halves matter, and they guard opposite errors:\n\n- **Scanning all distributions**, rather than one\n`importlib.metadata.distribution()` lookup, avoids a false negative.\n`setuptools` leaves a gitignored `deepagents.egg-info/` in the source\ntree, and the cwd is on `sys.path` for `-c`, `-m`, and the REPL — so\nfrom a checkout that directory is found first, and it has no\n`direct_url.json`. A single lookup therefore reports \"not editable\" for\na genuinely editable install.\n- **Correlating with the running module** avoids a false positive. An\nenvironment can hold several `deepagents` records, such as a wheel plus\nan unrelated editable checkout. Only one supplies the imported code;\ncrediting the other would label a published install as a workspace\nbuild.\n\nMetadata failures are contained per distribution, so a single unreadable\nor corrupt distribution can neither end the scan early nor propagate out\nof `create_deep_agent`. Anything unreadable, unparseable, or unlocatable\nreports the plain release version.\n\nThe result is cached — install layout is fixed for the life of the\nprocess, and this runs on every `create_deep_agent()` call.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T16:06:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ee7ac3d47980e4037403bfea1a13b7b51e06fb4a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d"}]},{"sha":"5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU3MjY4NzJjZDVlZmVjOTM2N2FlMmNlNjc4YWE3MTgzYWY3NDMzNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T15:32:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T15:32:20Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep `/update` and `/install --package` prompts responsive (#5127)\n\nRelated #5086\n\nThree confirmation prompts froze the terminal instead of taking an\nanswer: the `/update` dependency-refresh prompt, the `/update --deps`\napp-update prompt, and the `/install <pkg> --package` prompt. Enter and\nEsc did nothing, the quit key did nothing, and the only way out was\nkilling the terminal. They work now.\n\n## Why it happened\n\nTextual delivers keypresses on a single loop, and slash commands are\nhandled on that same loop. These three commands sat there waiting for\nthe user to answer the prompt — so the loop was blocked waiting for a\nkeypress that it was itself responsible for delivering. The prompt could\nnever resolve. Its internal timeout is ten minutes, so the app looked\npermanently dead rather than slow.\n\n#5086 fixed this same deadlock for the post-install restart prompt.\nThese three prompts were missed.\n\n## The fix\n\n`_schedule_off_message_pump` runs the prompt, and whatever depends on\nthe answer, as a separate task. The command handler returns right away,\nthe loop is free, and keypresses reach the prompt. Two blocks of code\nmoved so they could be reached from the new task:\n`_handle_update_command`'s upgrade tail became `_perform_app_upgrade`,\nand the `--package` install body became `_perform_package_install`.\n\n## What that broke\n\nBlocking the loop was also doing two useful things by accident. Both are\nnow done deliberately, and this is most of the diff.\n\n**It prevented two installs at once.** `/install` and `/update` both run\n`uv tool install --reinstall` against the same environment, and each\nrebuilds that environment from what is already recorded in it. Run two\nat once and both read the old state first, so whichever finishes last\nsilently discards the other's package. Only one install or update can\nnow be in progress at a time; a second command waits in the queue rather\nthan starting alongside.\n\n**It kept failures visible.** Code in a separate task is outside the\ncommand handler's error handling, so a crash would only reach a log file\nthe user never sees — leaving `Installing package '<pkg>'...` on screen\nas the last word, with nothing actually running. Each prompt now reports\nits own failures on screen.\n\nThere is also a new case to handle: quitting while an install is running\ncancels it partway through `uv`, which can leave the environment\nhalf-updated. That now gets written to the log, and the install is given\na moment to finish cleaning up before the app exits so it cannot leave a\nstray process behind.\n\nPackage-name validation and the editable-install refusal still run\n*before* the hand-off, so the prompt remains the only gate on installing\nthird-party code.\n\n## Tests\n\nEach of the three prompts gets a test that submits the command the way\nthe input widget does, then presses a key. Against the old code the\nkeypress never arrives and the prompt never resolves, so each test\nfails.\n\n`libs/code/AGENTS.md` already warned against waiting on a modal inside a\nslash-command handler. It now names the helper to use instead, and what\na caller owes it: report your own errors, expect to be cancelled\npartway, and take the lock before touching the environment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7b6ba24a-0f53-fd92-09d2-f9e20aca229a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d8018703bc12df57609a6f989ac190421cef73c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d8018703bc12df57609a6f989ac190421cef73c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa26ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeAIQAFN2MrE4rgteQK/UhPqL/NFH\n3GtRpa0tWQWebVAL+9C4BkUQ9biZ8S+Iw0L7Xs6A9LqpvMyv+MifPGoyCl0r+Yll\nj2D/sllvNRhp0KNwXKTnzRub0nKDDG2LKyClCcxQS35QHizqtIbJGElpNRtL9QCS\nz+71168zENlRMuWDde2qTPK7gr+ceLdysJl/dAT7dWHV3DWH6mAv0zziLlDqZf3y\n+zx5oFV+xGURcbywjVRROxfJvZ1svH55Myy/b0MLCzKZhAtJ+1gEsKuGpHmewkAf\nVcSsLQ6HPAr1PXNT3ZcjYViI4SJv+Hih4FWpfO3V08l2nq33rrGDS562ItGK5QCb\nXy4VcuPCxKHCtoujhOdydX5Iu07MSGa0+wfDLPncQSMotLxdCuFuVuDYpglubaAH\nwJqv4iHY4Vj4VFUnvL05d0pCgiO8HLqzWBvPc/TtY8aglLe3jPYsMRZYldlXTTuW\not/MnTj80zo2SJdage5n/jHMlL824EPCEmfeO0v8mzeMe17TS9BRn9HzCqTPOXja\nnzn5eDXUZ1h1/Ec6XI+KrfOan1n1N/hTSm1f4z4IAiqR6HB4arHROsWZQ3s1vdrT\nAkj5Y4gc2Z14DYCncs9H8KJOHZkzClR5uIq1g6O4aSQPwg+gEdal5WH65wPyCb7t\nGoPZIbEu9G00ZaTmQkBS\n=0kOt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d8018703bc12df57609a6f989ac190421cef73c2\nparent b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785425540 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785425540 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep `/update` and `/install --package` prompts responsive (#5127)\n\nRelated #5086\n\nThree confirmation prompts froze the terminal instead of taking an\nanswer: the `/update` dependency-refresh prompt, the `/update --deps`\napp-update prompt, and the `/install <pkg> --package` prompt. Enter and\nEsc did nothing, the quit key did nothing, and the only way out was\nkilling the terminal. They work now.\n\n## Why it happened\n\nTextual delivers keypresses on a single loop, and slash commands are\nhandled on that same loop. These three commands sat there waiting for\nthe user to answer the prompt — so the loop was blocked waiting for a\nkeypress that it was itself responsible for delivering. The prompt could\nnever resolve. Its internal timeout is ten minutes, so the app looked\npermanently dead rather than slow.\n\n#5086 fixed this same deadlock for the post-install restart prompt.\nThese three prompts were missed.\n\n## The fix\n\n`_schedule_off_message_pump` runs the prompt, and whatever depends on\nthe answer, as a separate task. The command handler returns right away,\nthe loop is free, and keypresses reach the prompt. Two blocks of code\nmoved so they could be reached from the new task:\n`_handle_update_command`'s upgrade tail became `_perform_app_upgrade`,\nand the `--package` install body became `_perform_package_install`.\n\n## What that broke\n\nBlocking the loop was also doing two useful things by accident. Both are\nnow done deliberately, and this is most of the diff.\n\n**It prevented two installs at once.** `/install` and `/update` both run\n`uv tool install --reinstall` against the same environment, and each\nrebuilds that environment from what is already recorded in it. Run two\nat once and both read the old state first, so whichever finishes last\nsilently discards the other's package. Only one install or update can\nnow be in progress at a time; a second command waits in the queue rather\nthan starting alongside.\n\n**It kept failures visible.** Code in a separate task is outside the\ncommand handler's error handling, so a crash would only reach a log file\nthe user never sees — leaving `Installing package '<pkg>'...` on screen\nas the last word, with nothing actually running. Each prompt now reports\nits own failures on screen.\n\nThere is also a new case to handle: quitting while an install is running\ncancels it partway through `uv`, which can leave the environment\nhalf-updated. That now gets written to the log, and the install is given\na moment to finish cleaning up before the app exits so it cannot leave a\nstray process behind.\n\nPackage-name validation and the editable-install refusal still run\n*before* the hand-off, so the prompt remains the only gate on installing\nthird-party code.\n\n## Tests\n\nEach of the three prompts gets a test that submits the command the way\nthe input widget does, then presses a key. Against the old code the\nkeypress never arrives and the prompt never resolves, so each test\nfails.\n\n`libs/code/AGENTS.md` already warned against waiting on a modal inside a\nslash-command handler. It now names the helper to use instead, and what\na caller owes it: report your own errors, expect to be cancelled\npartway, and take the lock before touching the environment.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7b6ba24a-0f53-fd92-09d2-f9e20aca229a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T15:32:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5726872cd5efec9367ae2ce678aa7183af74335d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0"}]},{"sha":"b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIwYWU5OGQ3NzUwOTVjOTQ3ZjcxOWNmMDJmNDk0ZDNkYzk1MTRhYjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T15:26:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T15:26:34Z"},"message":"chore(infra): ignore OpenSSH private keys (#5192)\n\nOpenSSH private keys sitting in the working tree (e.g. an `id_rsa`\ncopied in for a deploy) are no longer stageable: the root `.gitignore`\nnow covers the standard private key filenames and the common\n`<name>_<type>` naming convention.\n\n---\n\nThe `.gitignore` \"Local credentials and secrets\" section already covered\n`*.key`, `*.pem`, and friends, but OpenSSH private keys have no file\nextension, so none of those patterns ever matched — an `id_rsa` in the\nrepo root could be `git add`ed and committed without any warning.\n\nAdded to the same section:\n\n```\nid_rsa\nid_dsa\nid_ecdsa\nid_ed25519\n*_rsa\n*_dsa\n*_ecdsa\n*_ed25519\n```\n\nNo negation is needed for public keys: `id_rsa` matches only the exact\nname, so `id_rsa.pub` and `deploy_ed25519.pub` stay committable\n(verified below).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n`git check-ignore` (authoritative, accounts for all ignore sources):\n\n```\nIGNORED      id_rsa\nIGNORED      id_dsa\nIGNORED      id_ed25519\nIGNORED      id_ecdsa\nIGNORED      mykey_rsa\nIGNORED      mykey_dsa\nIGNORED      deploy_ed25519\nIGNORED      other_ecdsa\nNOT IGNORED  id_rsa.pub\nNOT IGNORED  deploy_ed25519.pub\n```\n\n`git ls-files | git check-ignore --stdin` prints nothing, so no\nalready-tracked file changes ignore status.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"fc809398e44deaa42211ef6b4cd2135215a03ab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fc809398e44deaa42211ef6b4cd2135215a03ab9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa20qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAOgQAI6V/VxvlcoCHpNrvVrhT3bY\n5DyendeASiYeg1AMOpDa33gTBd9ZBx0sBUORXdmsHoV4Ms1DjJrw2UN4nVBA7fn2\nP/1wXNUgHffhzZlRxSnpMxgPAT3qdNcuytfl0yb6NtYTuS+Os6ghoiS/7qyj3jo1\ndRrf+gghctq39y7xhuvIkQj6VFAeGkPgTVQr1OLideCiK1J6NKXcKtegKl3up/Xn\n2+WIZRH/DZfh2nu2FNtSZxbuga7XaaQdPSt9UsbyAkKs+uSQkVjfgQvW4WOU4dRw\nn9s95Aa5mzNr2NxeThydkTiJArqtqSp71fegRpF4LrTjTUSZ5rhGRfyVSF51ligl\ntbvzi8sOB03noZAdMpPBgfcwfysl8T/CTt0D5LemlEEURD9tWOSlBTfjMmFhrrOU\nms9lOi2Ypx9e/l7unIOoaYyltFA/GNM4H51dOo9J730jyWXmd2xTCZVE97AJbKjj\n8x7DThBQ+2IFEbm4vp17Mb2PKvg8iwGlEe3lfMRBaqaOcaDyADz5ET9LE4IzyFfm\ni9gflNGBJC4w0/PAUxUaIuAg69vE7Op+8ZOL7RBN56PZSVcSEKNCdMgPkkuAWNwM\nrctDaFc5c11JWok84UTGgt5x5mqPAeMrvCMQ2rFkq/NlBbhAwnyrbku4MyTA9WLm\nnTbSWARlE8QayCZlLygb\n=p2sA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fc809398e44deaa42211ef6b4cd2135215a03ab9\nparent 88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785425194 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785425194 -0400\n\nchore(infra): ignore OpenSSH private keys (#5192)\n\nOpenSSH private keys sitting in the working tree (e.g. an `id_rsa`\ncopied in for a deploy) are no longer stageable: the root `.gitignore`\nnow covers the standard private key filenames and the common\n`<name>_<type>` naming convention.\n\n---\n\nThe `.gitignore` \"Local credentials and secrets\" section already covered\n`*.key`, `*.pem`, and friends, but OpenSSH private keys have no file\nextension, so none of those patterns ever matched — an `id_rsa` in the\nrepo root could be `git add`ed and committed without any warning.\n\nAdded to the same section:\n\n```\nid_rsa\nid_dsa\nid_ecdsa\nid_ed25519\n*_rsa\n*_dsa\n*_ecdsa\n*_ed25519\n```\n\nNo negation is needed for public keys: `id_rsa` matches only the exact\nname, so `id_rsa.pub` and `deploy_ed25519.pub` stay committable\n(verified below).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n`git check-ignore` (authoritative, accounts for all ignore sources):\n\n```\nIGNORED      id_rsa\nIGNORED      id_dsa\nIGNORED      id_ed25519\nIGNORED      id_ecdsa\nIGNORED      mykey_rsa\nIGNORED      mykey_dsa\nIGNORED      deploy_ed25519\nIGNORED      other_ecdsa\nNOT IGNORED  id_rsa.pub\nNOT IGNORED  deploy_ed25519.pub\n```\n\n`git ls-files | git check-ignore --stdin` prints nothing, so no\nalready-tracked file changes ignore status.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T15:26:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0ae98d775095c947f719cf02f494d3dc9514ab0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843"}]},{"sha":"88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg4ZWE3ZGExOGU4YmU4NGU2NWRmMGVkYjhmZmM0YjkwNDE4MmY4NDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T15:25:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T15:25:03Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep server hook state out of task results (#5164)\n\nParallel `task` completions no longer crash parent agent turns when\nserver hooks are active.\n\n---\n\n`ServerHooksMiddleware` keeps two pieces of per-agent bookkeeping in\ngraph state: a snapshot of `PreToolUse` verdicts keyed by tool-call id,\nand a `Stop`-hook continuation count. Both were declared as ordinary\nstate fields, so a finished subagent copied them into the update it\nreturned to its parent.\n\n`_after_model` writes the verdict snapshot on every pass — including an\nempty dict when no hooks are configured — so *every* subagent emits that\nkey regardless of hook setup. When two `task` calls completed in the\nsame graph step, LangGraph received two writes for one single-value\nchannel and raised `InvalidUpdateError`, failing the parent turn. With a\nsingle `task` there was no error, but the subagent's snapshot silently\nreplaced the parent's.\n\nMarking both fields `PrivateStateAttr` keeps them inside the agent that\nowns them. `SubAgentMiddleware` already filters private keys out of\nsubagent results, and `create_deep_agent` derives that key set from each\nmiddleware's `state_schema`, so no extra wiring is required.\n\n**This does not change how hook decisions reach the code that enforces\nthem.** `PrivateStateAttr` is `OmitFromSchema(input=True, output=True)`\n— it removes the fields from the graph's *input and output* schemas\nonly. The channels stay ordinary checkpointed `LastValue` channels, and\nevery node still runs against the full state schema. A `deny` written in\n`after_model` still reaches `wrap_tool_call`, and the continuation count\nstill survives interrupt/resume. `PreToolUse` allow, deny, and ask\nbehavior is unchanged.\n\nOne consequence worth knowing: because `input=True` is also omitted,\nthese keys can no longer be seeded through graph *input*. Nothing does\nthat today, and `update_state` still writes them.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_parallel_tasks_do_not_merge_subagent_server_hook_state` runs two\n`task` calls that complete in one step, parametrized over both subagent\nshapes. The `compiled` case is a bare `CompiledSubAgent` that writes the\nkeys directly, which exercises `SubAgentMiddleware`'s explicit key strip\n— the only layer protecting that shape. The `real` case is a declarative\nsubagent carrying its own `ServerHooksMiddleware`, matching how\nsubagents are built in `create_cli_agent`; it reproduces the crash\nthrough the unconditional snapshot write. Without the fix the two cases\nfail on different keys (`_hooks_stop_continuation_count` and\n`_hooks_pre_tool_outcomes`). Both assert the tool messages come back\nintact *and* that neither key lands in the parent's checkpointed state,\nso swapping in a reducer instead of privacy would not satisfy them.\n\n`test_task_omits_private_server_hook_state_from_subagent_update` covers\nthe single-`task` case, which cannot trip `InvalidUpdateError` and so\nwould otherwise regress silently. It is built through\n`create_deep_agent` so the private-key derivation is exercised rather\nthan reimplemented.\n\n`test_pretool_deny_blocks_tool_through_real_graph` drives a `deny`\nthrough a compiled graph and asserts the tool never executes, with and\nwithout a resume round trip. The other deny tests call the middleware\nhooks directly and copy state between them by hand, so none of them can\ndetect an outcome that fails to cross the node boundary.\n\n`test_server_hook_state_fields_are_private` asserts through the\nproduction detector, so it also catches the case where annotation\nresolution degrades and silently yields an empty key set.\n\n## Types and documentation\n\n`ServerHooksState` now documents why the fields are private, that the\nchannels remain checkpointed, and that the verdict dict is a per-turn\nsnapshot rather than an accumulator — every `_after_model` replaces it\nwholesale, so stale tool-call ids cannot survive into a later turn. It\nalso records that a future reducer on either field must be placed\n*after* `PrivateStateAttr` in the `Annotated` metadata: LangGraph\ninspects only the last metadata entry when detecting reducers, so one\nadded before the marker is ignored without error.\n\n`_PreToolState` becomes a discriminated union of a denied and a passed\nvariant, making a denial without a reason unrepresentable at the three\nsites that construct one.\n\n`pre_tool_behavior` becomes `hook_decided_permission`, returning a\n`bool`. It previously returned one of four values while both call sites\nonly asked whether a hook had settled permission, leaving \"hook\nexpressed no opinion\" and \"no outcome recorded\" indistinguishable to\nevery caller.","tree":{"sha":"8dba4a3c38c48ec1d59f06c89f5888751f053de0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8dba4a3c38c48ec1d59f06c89f5888751f053de0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa2zPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb8oQAGUCdpqvO15qfhbA7bcOy8ad\nLyVGc/1AFVevFSnKUrSZCmQ18ftYDdl7dIsJx9XuN9oOKBWDbXDhlcqDb9byMyrO\nulSNQapyH0vRL9suWzV2gAr970vYKaFWa8r/0jYGSzGaPLHnrby6UkRr63noUy9x\nkBN06t3LE2y/EppsOc8MOdsUx+7mYkJD8/ugz+gmS2B0phGjvc/2oMjjkstyNQCT\ncOqQPadAZpjdPRgmh/9ubDLTwwi5fB1dOdm5RFU58GFTTlMvjO0vmgX0gf/BzQgl\n1heyBNycClbMpfdol3FxpEuKdYXfNA8X+QUvBkPPMO3zXaM3dstyusvsE7IJtsdj\nrUVWBrhV4HU0HBgcxZWgaPW38ccKL4HwGtoFovf04YlXELrPoDeCXxAkWuRZniix\nYMQ1h9L9PmnZqCaY4el8d5eXXS0G4F6a7Iz5dyjz0jru17K80+Ma8SuBmrF5pVvR\n929dfRzyq8TIxtHUaZZpp4q2X7IJSB8h2TMt04fsnd01PDYkq/gn82/+2R43jbZF\nv1A2EzGVRu4kKE92VOkJlY6K5HedA5iyzHnp72HZGmpcdeC+SqJACkoup9OMvh01\nuR/uAStlKp+/QEecrjM88H+CkEfU5nR09QgOTGY7MCNinxeImv10PLLFPnWUBeZ8\nTW/ClbKKAr8LpzUkpuzb\n=IVEK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8dba4a3c38c48ec1d59f06c89f5888751f053de0\nparent be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785425103 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785425103 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep server hook state out of task results (#5164)\n\nParallel `task` completions no longer crash parent agent turns when\nserver hooks are active.\n\n---\n\n`ServerHooksMiddleware` keeps two pieces of per-agent bookkeeping in\ngraph state: a snapshot of `PreToolUse` verdicts keyed by tool-call id,\nand a `Stop`-hook continuation count. Both were declared as ordinary\nstate fields, so a finished subagent copied them into the update it\nreturned to its parent.\n\n`_after_model` writes the verdict snapshot on every pass — including an\nempty dict when no hooks are configured — so *every* subagent emits that\nkey regardless of hook setup. When two `task` calls completed in the\nsame graph step, LangGraph received two writes for one single-value\nchannel and raised `InvalidUpdateError`, failing the parent turn. With a\nsingle `task` there was no error, but the subagent's snapshot silently\nreplaced the parent's.\n\nMarking both fields `PrivateStateAttr` keeps them inside the agent that\nowns them. `SubAgentMiddleware` already filters private keys out of\nsubagent results, and `create_deep_agent` derives that key set from each\nmiddleware's `state_schema`, so no extra wiring is required.\n\n**This does not change how hook decisions reach the code that enforces\nthem.** `PrivateStateAttr` is `OmitFromSchema(input=True, output=True)`\n— it removes the fields from the graph's *input and output* schemas\nonly. The channels stay ordinary checkpointed `LastValue` channels, and\nevery node still runs against the full state schema. A `deny` written in\n`after_model` still reaches `wrap_tool_call`, and the continuation count\nstill survives interrupt/resume. `PreToolUse` allow, deny, and ask\nbehavior is unchanged.\n\nOne consequence worth knowing: because `input=True` is also omitted,\nthese keys can no longer be seeded through graph *input*. Nothing does\nthat today, and `update_state` still writes them.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_parallel_tasks_do_not_merge_subagent_server_hook_state` runs two\n`task` calls that complete in one step, parametrized over both subagent\nshapes. The `compiled` case is a bare `CompiledSubAgent` that writes the\nkeys directly, which exercises `SubAgentMiddleware`'s explicit key strip\n— the only layer protecting that shape. The `real` case is a declarative\nsubagent carrying its own `ServerHooksMiddleware`, matching how\nsubagents are built in `create_cli_agent`; it reproduces the crash\nthrough the unconditional snapshot write. Without the fix the two cases\nfail on different keys (`_hooks_stop_continuation_count` and\n`_hooks_pre_tool_outcomes`). Both assert the tool messages come back\nintact *and* that neither key lands in the parent's checkpointed state,\nso swapping in a reducer instead of privacy would not satisfy them.\n\n`test_task_omits_private_server_hook_state_from_subagent_update` covers\nthe single-`task` case, which cannot trip `InvalidUpdateError` and so\nwould otherwise regress silently. It is built through\n`create_deep_agent` so the private-key derivation is exercised rather\nthan reimplemented.\n\n`test_pretool_deny_blocks_tool_through_real_graph` drives a `deny`\nthrough a compiled graph and asserts the tool never executes, with and\nwithout a resume round trip. The other deny tests call the middleware\nhooks directly and copy state between them by hand, so none of them can\ndetect an outcome that fails to cross the node boundary.\n\n`test_server_hook_state_fields_are_private` asserts through the\nproduction detector, so it also catches the case where annotation\nresolution degrades and silently yields an empty key set.\n\n## Types and documentation\n\n`ServerHooksState` now documents why the fields are private, that the\nchannels remain checkpointed, and that the verdict dict is a per-turn\nsnapshot rather than an accumulator — every `_after_model` replaces it\nwholesale, so stale tool-call ids cannot survive into a later turn. It\nalso records that a future reducer on either field must be placed\n*after* `PrivateStateAttr` in the `Annotated` metadata: LangGraph\ninspects only the last metadata entry when detecting reducers, so one\nadded before the marker is ignored without error.\n\n`_PreToolState` becomes a discriminated union of a denied and a passed\nvariant, making a denial without a reason unrepresentable at the three\nsites that construct one.\n\n`pre_tool_behavior` becomes `hook_decided_permission`, returning a\n`bool`. It previously returned one of four values while both call sites\nonly asked whether a hook had settled permission, leaving \"hook\nexpressed no opinion\" and \"no outcome recorded\" indistinguishable to\nevery caller.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T15:25:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88ea7da18e8be84e65df0edb8ffc4b904182f843/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1"}]},{"sha":"be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJlMmU1MDU0YjlkZmZkZjliYTkwMzJhMTk4YzBhZTVmOGEwY2NjZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T15:02:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T15:02:39Z"},"message":"feat(code): click the splash `thread` ID to copy it (#5173)\n\nClicking the thread ID on the startup splash now copies it, and the row\nlinks to the thread's LangSmith trace.\n\n---\n\nThe Debug Console already lets you click a thread ID to copy it and\nshows an `(open in langsmith)` trace link, but the startup splash\nrendered the same ID as inert text. The splash thread ID is now a\nclick-to-copy span (toast: \"Thread ID copied\"), and the row gains the\nsame `(open in langsmith)` link built from the project URL the banner\nalready resolves in the background — no extra lookup. The copy-span meta\nprotocol moved to a shared `tui/widgets/_copy_spans.py` so the banner\nand the console can't drift apart.\n\nNote: the splash `thread:` row only renders in debug mode\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG`), unchanged by this PR.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3168ee95-5a3e-fe72-c36f-f5ba194e42d4)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"741c0e06186eafebcde278ce9f13313db80876ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/741c0e06186eafebcde278ce9f13313db80876ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa2ePCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjS8QAFIyZDDD38BVFdiP0h5CV2Ki\nGROS5B0YKGDiNoVuewBTfOvj4iSnXpGNS1e/GbLJiv189TOqT/DWh3j96yd9YZp0\nsEON70tWoNpdTQN4191JNXNV62B89xDy2cw1DmMN8R6POHGYVR6gFT/kFHJNfW02\nL8xnApvkmHgVnFB7Hh7/CWSbCPmnUlf83Ih59IHb/OEEGRh2E1xOebBegtFnt0Uu\n2IQiyH/E5zBB6TySw/PjlDIi9dtOxMFi/iVKYIUrp0IkSuUg9jeszrXXy72v72Et\nET1QNv9E6CeImVp6qFVadHNlfPxtlKPQWQkWA3i1tUDuUbdA/oR3F10M3pCRBesL\nXvEGidrSSMe0nSLaSdR2tdjtUJ68gLJjHipcTcznmMPj50FQCU+XASeHxRdTqiV4\nLQWiOAQwn7eHQt4xxsaUfNlWO5uR23avbeQlgM31z1wyJO483jmY5EuCwFgPHL/2\nPX1nkxS4ag+aGlLzIGjC9hJOgmYIbCr/fdtBep0Snu3dm16OfvOTaMqc3gi8lbP9\nDnyaseLP5Y3bjAcAA3FLwvnu0oFnf1+hbU0lMHxKlY4gg6XyqqleOaKE4pfU9ITs\nHFhIssjE4ximCd7xCr70tGfyTndMtwQti3PMVUsOxzVhShm4Flk1iSFJi7POmrkh\nU8YERtf9MecppAQEjZHV\n=P4Qj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 741c0e06186eafebcde278ce9f13313db80876ee\nparent 3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785423759 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785423759 -0400\n\nfeat(code): click the splash `thread` ID to copy it (#5173)\n\nClicking the thread ID on the startup splash now copies it, and the row\nlinks to the thread's LangSmith trace.\n\n---\n\nThe Debug Console already lets you click a thread ID to copy it and\nshows an `(open in langsmith)` trace link, but the startup splash\nrendered the same ID as inert text. The splash thread ID is now a\nclick-to-copy span (toast: \"Thread ID copied\"), and the row gains the\nsame `(open in langsmith)` link built from the project URL the banner\nalready resolves in the background — no extra lookup. The copy-span meta\nprotocol moved to a shared `tui/widgets/_copy_spans.py` so the banner\nand the console can't drift apart.\n\nNote: the splash `thread:` row only renders in debug mode\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG`), unchanged by this PR.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3168ee95-5a3e-fe72-c36f-f5ba194e42d4)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T15:02:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/be2e5054b9dffdf9ba9032a198c0ae5f8a0cccd1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58"}]},{"sha":"3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNiZDYzMDE4MTg0MjZmMzhkMzNkZjJhZjk5MTA2MWNhNDY1OWRjNTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T14:58:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T14:58:19Z"},"message":"chore(infra): ship MIT LICENSE file in every package sdist (#5186)\n\nEvery publishable package sdist now ships the MIT `LICENSE` file, so\ndownstream redistributors (conda-forge, distro packagers) get the\nlicense text directly from PyPI.\n\n---\n\nNo package under `libs/` included a `LICENSE` in its sdist — the file\nonly existed at the repo root. This surfaced on the `deepagents`\nconda-forge feedstock, where `license_file: LICENSE` in the recipe has\nbeen silently unmet for every release.\n\nThe fix copies the repo-root `LICENSE` into each of the six publishable\npackage directories (`acp`, `cli`, `code`, `deepagents`, `evals`,\n`talon`). Both build backends in play pick up a root-level `LICENSE`\nautomatically, so no `pyproject.toml` changes were needed:\n\n- **hatchling** (`acp`, `cli`, `code`, `talon`) includes it in the sdist\nby default.\n- **setuptools** (`deepagents`, `evals`) auto-includes files matching\n`LICEN[CS]E*`.\n\nVerified by building each sdist locally with `uv build --sdist` and\nconfirming the archive contains a top-level `LICENSE` entry:\n\n| Package | sdist |\n|---|---|\n| `acp` | `deepagents_acp-0.0.9.tar.gz` |\n| `cli` | `deepagents_cli-0.2.2.tar.gz` |\n| `code` | `deepagents_code-0.1.49.tar.gz` |\n| `deepagents` | `deepagents-0.7.0.tar.gz` |\n| `evals` | `deepagents_evals-0.0.1.tar.gz` |\n| `talon` | `deepagents_talon-0.0.3.tar.gz` |\n\nAs the before-state, the published `deepagents-0.7.0` sdist on PyPI was\ndownloaded and confirmed to contain no `LICENSE`.","tree":{"sha":"1985b5d61c6885f958c53e59f3392ee10d098850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1985b5d61c6885f958c53e59f3392ee10d098850"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa2aLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgTsQAIF1zHBcaq44iNZ4syUINZoC\nYofT78TgkVsf5rAnL/y5QkSL6P2pY8AiKJFqQ7rM95/j/KkLqPQfzjqhXag4ushi\nc/ZzeATMRhWQ7a9t0XAZKnOjU2PEoetULsa8OaglANW9Ev7FOb+mCm4cl++gTQHR\nSDuiFEfXacyw4IKwuBAatuTpwkbhrBm3pwve35sJ3uvdHtAGDp7Avtas6wRUUVX9\n0Ehj+f9/8oTH1DOQNdIXsmKgFGyzH21THjeMtU5F0d1jrxtjAEXgVk4QgK19VlTj\nBVQn9TNXCMWt6bcl5jVyGOo42YhueVn5Og7bCuWLNQmkZGXWnXj76LPUzTz/Gk7S\nL7fyvsMZNzX2Z15ztqvgmBe93+MdLVF6tpHbYtFIjx23ES6gZaW8NzduMaOeuqJA\nPJV5QbTdlG82H22Ao3y4qkNQX8gJnxdOi0CYVn1vapxaNq3bHjMnR04iLB36nwJe\nbPgsKPF68B8+4QW/58z+LrEQYJWhkDBiwsfFJilXPw1HxSvZOI9Gbtz/ey/UCqKo\n6AZJy/MoLpjmsmNCaMa3FVI26Xx9NTzHFeVFiWIar4PrQlLAiL3cUXa3ql97lagn\nhIDWu5ytXBPf4zg2QiphoXDhREsTbVvnWdKr1bv5XqdAp9IR4uh5WkV6Rnf0TqbR\n2OtV5aWCJXmo71D3u6rT\n=oSM8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1985b5d61c6885f958c53e59f3392ee10d098850\nparent 872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785423499 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785423499 -0400\n\nchore(infra): ship MIT LICENSE file in every package sdist (#5186)\n\nEvery publishable package sdist now ships the MIT `LICENSE` file, so\ndownstream redistributors (conda-forge, distro packagers) get the\nlicense text directly from PyPI.\n\n---\n\nNo package under `libs/` included a `LICENSE` in its sdist — the file\nonly existed at the repo root. This surfaced on the `deepagents`\nconda-forge feedstock, where `license_file: LICENSE` in the recipe has\nbeen silently unmet for every release.\n\nThe fix copies the repo-root `LICENSE` into each of the six publishable\npackage directories (`acp`, `cli`, `code`, `deepagents`, `evals`,\n`talon`). Both build backends in play pick up a root-level `LICENSE`\nautomatically, so no `pyproject.toml` changes were needed:\n\n- **hatchling** (`acp`, `cli`, `code`, `talon`) includes it in the sdist\nby default.\n- **setuptools** (`deepagents`, `evals`) auto-includes files matching\n`LICEN[CS]E*`.\n\nVerified by building each sdist locally with `uv build --sdist` and\nconfirming the archive contains a top-level `LICENSE` entry:\n\n| Package | sdist |\n|---|---|\n| `acp` | `deepagents_acp-0.0.9.tar.gz` |\n| `cli` | `deepagents_cli-0.2.2.tar.gz` |\n| `code` | `deepagents_code-0.1.49.tar.gz` |\n| `deepagents` | `deepagents-0.7.0.tar.gz` |\n| `evals` | `deepagents_evals-0.0.1.tar.gz` |\n| `talon` | `deepagents_talon-0.0.3.tar.gz` |\n\nAs the before-state, the published `deepagents-0.7.0` sdist on PyPI was\ndownloaded and confirmed to contain no `LICENSE`.","verified_at":"2026-07-30T14:58:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3bd6301818426f38d33df2af991061ca4659dc58/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4"}]},{"sha":"872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg3MmY5ZDU2NDc3NTlhODRlN2FiZmE3OWQ0M2ZjMTI4YzU0ZTI5YTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-30T14:58:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-30T14:58:13Z"},"message":"perf(code): refresh `/threads` cache after each turn (#5174)\n\nA thread you just started now shows up in the `/threads` switcher as\nsoon as you open it, instead of appearing a moment later.\n\n---\n\nThe thread picker paints instantly from an in-memory cache of recent\nthreads and only re-queries the session database afterwards. That cache\nwas populated exactly once, by a startup worker, so any thread created\nduring the session was absent from the first paint: the new row only\nappeared after the modal's list query, its configured-agent filesystem\nscan, and a full teardown/rebuild of every row widget had completed. On\na large `sessions.db` the list query alone measured ~0.2 s warm (~0.8 s\non the first call of a process, which also builds the covering index),\nwhich is exactly the window where the user sees a list that is missing\nthe thread they just used.\n\nRather than trying to make that refresh path faster, this keeps the\ncache honest: `_cleanup_agent_task` — the turn-end hook that already\nrefreshes the git branch — now schedules the same prewarm the app runs\nat startup, in an exclusive worker group so overlapping turns coalesce.\nTurn end is the right moment because the turn's checkpoints have just\nbeen written and the app is otherwise idle, and it is cheap to repeat:\nthe per-thread message-count and initial-prompt caches are keyed on\ncheckpoint freshness, so only the thread that actually changed is read\nback from disk. With the cache current, the picker's first paint already\ncontains the new thread (with its updated timestamp and message count),\nand the follow-up query finds nothing to change, so the row rebuild is\nskipped entirely.\n\nDeletion already pruned this cache in place, so this fills in the other\nhalf of keeping it in sync with in-session activity. Scheduling is\nskipped while the app is exiting or not running, mirroring the existing\nskill-rediscovery guard.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/35c3b07d-9fe1-e077-4cdf-e6b7854b4f18)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e195b5ae9cf75a3bc3c12e19023ecb494e3e60cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e195b5ae9cf75a3bc3c12e19023ecb494e3e60cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqa2aFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsy8QAALGzK5U/Az+0SfJ3WTH0CL0\nP/28eYVCYa2VdmW6AYjtDCGmS02TSFSv1sClqMDD88DX1a8CEtLXLYh3kG7IJ6XV\nUEmoVRdwzB/KSQ1XmrO5RdgogfizoeFOmubFOyyEb/g2YHhP/hAJ3wWQxYYxNfy0\ndTLRZZlb+nT2s4c2MUPGjySp8DhEFOm8ovoR0B3no8ePBO8Xxch2k+oB3CHrYRzf\n4+n80oeYxqzob9heckhUZBIHhInIZ+pivzRDB1KaJDvtwbVH05fgeE+bciPrfcGb\nARnywTCegHy1ko9x1JKEdcSuHkLIILJfryizYRF/pKnhhOszkUhDTqN5cFgJ7zoe\n9gd4zL0C2I2uKimmGklReRYr4kRh0CQ67Dk0UTEFc3tdMWlaszBfXnx9PPGee1IC\ndJeubxJPy16gtYsH1i/qEn3REbI9kZDo9NnTZZElShR30C/LVw4U9jRYdsfsB/Ru\nDwS+M3Zrwjby7yVZRv1xlhRXVUVEIEfE7BrSJuJS1ADwKByDtS3KoTTt/T5qjfOM\nD/ZCPeewKDbJ3ZFU0aQucqdOosMbgLQOxfmqDHxgBM308cp5s4PK05DAcajvyXaw\n4QH6J5iPcBGiauOQqsSaefnNtukr7O/7jXaTsOchW5mU3+SOqV4NSUw5yXqmNCQb\nFX7cK8gHASyTt+LbI5gf\n=IvpC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e195b5ae9cf75a3bc3c12e19023ecb494e3e60cd\nparent 991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785423493 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785423493 -0400\n\nperf(code): refresh `/threads` cache after each turn (#5174)\n\nA thread you just started now shows up in the `/threads` switcher as\nsoon as you open it, instead of appearing a moment later.\n\n---\n\nThe thread picker paints instantly from an in-memory cache of recent\nthreads and only re-queries the session database afterwards. That cache\nwas populated exactly once, by a startup worker, so any thread created\nduring the session was absent from the first paint: the new row only\nappeared after the modal's list query, its configured-agent filesystem\nscan, and a full teardown/rebuild of every row widget had completed. On\na large `sessions.db` the list query alone measured ~0.2 s warm (~0.8 s\non the first call of a process, which also builds the covering index),\nwhich is exactly the window where the user sees a list that is missing\nthe thread they just used.\n\nRather than trying to make that refresh path faster, this keeps the\ncache honest: `_cleanup_agent_task` — the turn-end hook that already\nrefreshes the git branch — now schedules the same prewarm the app runs\nat startup, in an exclusive worker group so overlapping turns coalesce.\nTurn end is the right moment because the turn's checkpoints have just\nbeen written and the app is otherwise idle, and it is cheap to repeat:\nthe per-thread message-count and initial-prompt caches are keyed on\ncheckpoint freshness, so only the thread that actually changed is read\nback from disk. With the cache current, the picker's first paint already\ncontains the new thread (with its updated timestamp and message count),\nand the follow-up query finds nothing to change, so the row rebuild is\nskipped entirely.\n\nDeletion already pruned this cache in place, so this fills in the other\nhalf of keeping it in sync with in-session activity. Scheduling is\nskipped while the app is exiting or not running, mirroring the existing\nskill-rediscovery guard.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/35c3b07d-9fe1-e077-4cdf-e6b7854b4f18)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-30T14:58:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/872f9d5647759a84e7abfa79d43fc128c54e29a4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2"}]},{"sha":"991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5MWI3ZTc2OWQ4YWZhOThlZGM4ZGFjMWM2ODk5NGNhNGRjNzY1ZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T21:41:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:41:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): resume hints echo the launched command name (#5119)\n\nResume hints now name the command you actually launched —\n`deepagents-code`, or a renamed shim such as `abc` — instead of always\nsaying `dcode`.\n\n---\n\nThe package ships two console scripts (`dcode` and `deepagents-code`),\nand a common way to run several checkouts side by side is a renamed\nsymlink in `~/.local/bin` pointing at a worktree's `dcode` script. Both\nresume hints (the teardown \"Resume this thread with:\" line and the\nrelaunch hint after an agent switch) hardcoded `dcode`, so those users\nwere told to run a command that may not exist on their `PATH`.\n\nThe launch name is recoverable: for a shebang console script the kernel\nhands the interpreter the pathname passed to `execve` rather than the\nsymlink target, so `sys.argv[0]` keeps the shim name. `invoked_name`\nresolves it and falls back to `dcode` when the value cannot be a command\nthe user typed — `python -m deepagents_code` reports `__main__.py`, an\nembedded interpreter may leave `sys.argv` empty, and the value is\nrendered into a copy-pasteable command, so the shape is allowlisted\nrather than escaped. The startup auto-update re-execs as `python -m\ndeepagents_code`, which discards `argv[0]`, so the resolved name is\nhanded to the next generation through an internal env sentinel (the same\npattern as the existing restart loop-guard sentinel).\n\nDeliberately out of scope: the hand-maintained `--help` usage lines\nstill hardcode `dcode`. That is a mechanical swap of roughly a hundred\nliterals guarded by the help-screen drift test, and is better reviewed\non its own.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/42e64bd7-ceac-c324-9036-69205c1754bc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c791c0a8de834b19c7b1f32d7e6b99d87ad7b6cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c791c0a8de834b19c7b1f32d7e6b99d87ad7b6cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqanOXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0u8QADzNvPAZDrMx5MJsbXFEhPWb\nEjz6qZyevnai7moRpCS8eExIGGnmz1Y2S3q7U48BkemudqGP3/f0f6ZypjwZuOmR\nkdmZbLw1NOANjN4ICqqpTBdzVmP1QPcGQiW/5fIAbL87c4MBVKqm4dPYDUE9KHPg\n0dxuxNJ/rOT+DqR5un/i+viWSrFnPjqUhDNP2DzZ/qvWzIhOxeWYBeca/zI845B/\nLEUuPFRcduLmjw7pqlSahpedwTpeEgLWXuElyc8Hpc3YzkUJYv0tBhCVYwPiSW00\noTdmN/VJ0fdgqT8G2KES1X26p1L36JCdb7/1vewv8XiMgwT0MsBmJgmKthh+2SJf\nX9sI4em6e1DI24QveLbExCMjhRPE25UL8TS7vwAffoU0ZAlYNbyE/H5agOKO4bff\nND4K/KdLIa2W5z6WTJP2zAGGzXL4EKgLQbHuA1OnILOZ8XR4cw3wWPcFqMNzpTZk\nfs30gGHQIL1o3vbbOgpnCtyibNQ7c9FRNOLluwEfuMcB5y53Sc2xdo9pHAaLYnEM\nx4Q7fnhoxgXB56MkGxSW+FL32+i1Y46GmMbXP+ay1j7KutByXDJSVTlqrYHOMhmm\nCWxri+z5MsAsaT909eVI4MSO66lxyL8AOF1u/DhkIIbcE+fQRBDvnSZEQHvcUeQy\nMLjBlnjCicjOS5pPOjyp\n=QB0K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c791c0a8de834b19c7b1f32d7e6b99d87ad7b6cd\nparent 5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785361303 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785361303 -0400\n\nfix(code): resume hints echo the launched command name (#5119)\n\nResume hints now name the command you actually launched —\n`deepagents-code`, or a renamed shim such as `abc` — instead of always\nsaying `dcode`.\n\n---\n\nThe package ships two console scripts (`dcode` and `deepagents-code`),\nand a common way to run several checkouts side by side is a renamed\nsymlink in `~/.local/bin` pointing at a worktree's `dcode` script. Both\nresume hints (the teardown \"Resume this thread with:\" line and the\nrelaunch hint after an agent switch) hardcoded `dcode`, so those users\nwere told to run a command that may not exist on their `PATH`.\n\nThe launch name is recoverable: for a shebang console script the kernel\nhands the interpreter the pathname passed to `execve` rather than the\nsymlink target, so `sys.argv[0]` keeps the shim name. `invoked_name`\nresolves it and falls back to `dcode` when the value cannot be a command\nthe user typed — `python -m deepagents_code` reports `__main__.py`, an\nembedded interpreter may leave `sys.argv` empty, and the value is\nrendered into a copy-pasteable command, so the shape is allowlisted\nrather than escaped. The startup auto-update re-execs as `python -m\ndeepagents_code`, which discards `argv[0]`, so the resolved name is\nhanded to the next generation through an internal env sentinel (the same\npattern as the existing restart loop-guard sentinel).\n\nDeliberately out of scope: the hand-maintained `--help` usage lines\nstill hardcode `dcode`. That is a mechanical swap of roughly a hundred\nliterals guarded by the help-screen drift test, and is better reviewed\non its own.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/42e64bd7-ceac-c324-9036-69205c1754bc)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:41:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/991b7e769d8afa98edc8dac1c68994ca4dc765d2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8"}]},{"sha":"5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViYmNmNDI4YTgxMzFmMGZjYTE0OWFiYmEzNDA5NmZiY2QyZGZkZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T21:38:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:38:38Z"},"message":"fix(code): stop duplicating Auto transcript events on interrupt replay (#5157)\n\nFixed duplicated Auto-mode approval/denial messages in the\n`deepagents-code` transcript after resuming a human approval.\n\n---\n\n`AutoModeHITLMiddleware` emits its sanitized transcript events (`Auto\nfallback: human approval required …`, `Auto denied […]`, `Auto\nclassifier unavailable: …`) over the custom stream writer *before*\ncalling `interrupt()`. LangGraph restarts the entire `after_model` node\nwhen the user answers the approval, so every pre-interrupt emission ran\na second time and the same line was rendered twice. Emissions now go\nthrough a bounded, LRU-evicted ledger keyed by thread + action batch, so\na replay is a no-op while a later batch can still emit the same text.\nThis also generalizes the existing per-invocation coalescing of N-tool\nbatches.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2c64987a-3e83-05bc-66fc-c20f43dd845e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"342daf7dbf414e2dc178bd642bd80cb80aec3dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/342daf7dbf414e2dc178bd642bd80cb80aec3dc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqanLeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxbAQAAUyhkOdEKXhOMwAa3BDIB4Z\nZ7ku5sF316BTfSEhRNnz9yZt/JUGJT6C2MywvhFlTizqJnAKFlVdkk3YLehPRu8R\ni4OPwxQD74LrAvEZgaLCPaFFCWWaVlTAz+K0t5BNOeeGyYykx4nA8L/vPJFCk8am\niKx0PSF/eC4cA9VpNhXee/IzBQsXnTirqsWJsBpR0TCPme8qwvujuxNb8jzdpfNt\nX3laNaLoEIkcs1UNu+N0cI7hetYnC8KS3Buf7504Lhwek6OgXtWzY70ZEpdQLbQ7\n9Vlud6G6CexUOASli11tjC6wY6JqelOALTxsXvKe9/zJnf0vv5s8UoRyFRVh5Ep3\nz1csxfWwNvpeoi3eF1MPlgN7YPzP2IyCwwaLr57FvEocYOfJs5NnGRB4sLPD3DpA\npxA467eP/OKozhHkE3J3WBC4uCNI9qoP2NAZpSiOsvZn04N30jy8WC/EJw2u9W5u\ntl8R45bi0B3Pgi4ChGsVY5yHxY2CxzgZoo6MTn9gCCEaXFW8GC+C5zfVZsYuFxT/\nOvIfJbYDjq2pB97NpcdFzBITcNZ2C0ercHiqpP1sSnDW4Xk4vzVuY++0uRuMi54D\nZlptORBVTtOr3jWf1NlVL4kByrsmRoG13y03Hf0O23IfPyOarL2h5W5as36mJaMb\nozcDrzazSqw+i+IvJtLS\n=pQWn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 342daf7dbf414e2dc178bd642bd80cb80aec3dc3\nparent 3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785361118 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785361118 -0400\n\nfix(code): stop duplicating Auto transcript events on interrupt replay (#5157)\n\nFixed duplicated Auto-mode approval/denial messages in the\n`deepagents-code` transcript after resuming a human approval.\n\n---\n\n`AutoModeHITLMiddleware` emits its sanitized transcript events (`Auto\nfallback: human approval required …`, `Auto denied […]`, `Auto\nclassifier unavailable: …`) over the custom stream writer *before*\ncalling `interrupt()`. LangGraph restarts the entire `after_model` node\nwhen the user answers the approval, so every pre-interrupt emission ran\na second time and the same line was rendered twice. Emissions now go\nthrough a bounded, LRU-evicted ledger keyed by thread + action batch, so\na replay is a no-op while a later batch can still emit the same text.\nThis also generalizes the existing per-invocation coalescing of N-tool\nbatches.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/2c64987a-3e83-05bc-66fc-c20f43dd845e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:38:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bbcf428a8131f0fca149abba34096fbcd2dfde8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434"}]},{"sha":"3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNiYTczMWZiMWM0N2E1NWYyYjQ2ZTQ0MGViMjQ1YzE4YjNhYmU0MzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T21:25:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:25:38Z"},"message":"ci(infra): soft-run release-deps check under acknowledged bypass (#5168)\n\n`release-deps: acknowledged` no longer skips any job. Every check runs\nand reports; the label only stops one of them from blocking.\n\n| Check | Effect of the label |\n| --- | --- |\n| `📦 Check Release Dependencies` | Resolves in report-only mode; check\ngoes green, sticky comment still lists the packages that owe releases. |\n| `📦 Check Dependency Freshness` | None. Advisory in all cases; its\ncomment stays on the PR. |\n| `🔗 Check SDK Pin` | Clears the hard failure on a **prerelease** pin.\nStale-pin behaviour unchanged. |\n\nA green check under the label now means \"the listed packages still owe\nreleases,\" never \"deps resolved.\" Skipping the resolve job instead\nproduced a green check that read as an all-clear while PyPI installs\nwere still broken — and deleted the record of the remaining release\ndebt.\n\n## Follow-up releases are reported on every path\n\nThe check lists sibling release-please packages whose **published** PyPI\n`requires_dist` cannot satisfy a head requirement on the branch — e.g.\npublished `0.1.49` constrains `deepagents` to `==0.7.0b2`; head requires\n`==0.7.0`.\n\nThis is gated on neither the label nor the resolver verdict. Resolution\npassing only proves the *changed* package installs today; a\nreverse-dependent whose published metadata caps the new line still\nbreaks `pip install` for its own users. So a clean resolve with\noutstanding follow-ups posts the sticky and stays green, and the sticky\nclears itself only once nothing is left to report.\n\nThe analysis is advisory and can never fail the gate — a crash in it\ndegrades to a warning on the report. Packages whose PyPI metadata could\nnot be determined are reported as indeterminate and never produce a\n\"needs release\" claim.\n\nOverlap between a published constraint and a head requirement is decided\nby a finite probe sample, which can prove overlap but never\ndisjointness. The error directions are asymmetric — falsely reporting\noverlap hides a real conflict, while falsely reporting disjoint only\nadds a spurious row — so every inconclusive case reports\noverlap-unknown.\n\n`RELEASING.md` gains a \"Releasing a new line ahead of its dependents\"\nsection covering when the label is appropriate (coordinated release\norder) versus when the metadata is simply wrong, plus the table above.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 717 tests pass across the helper suites (`pytest\n.github/scripts/tests`, which is what `ci.yml` runs); `ty check\n.github/scripts/release/` is clean.\n- New unit tests cover: follow-ups rendered on failure and on clean\nresolves; every conflicting package listed even where the resolver would\nprove only one; acknowledged soft-run exits 0 and writes the sticky; an\nacknowledged clean run clears it; indeterminate metadata never claims\n\"needs release\"; an unpublished package is not reported as\nindeterminate; a crash in the advisory analysis does not fail the gate.\n- The overlap heuristic has a boundary matrix (`==` vs `>=,<`, open vs\nclosed edges, `~=`, `!=`, wildcard pins, single-component versions)\nasserting disjointness is only reported when provable.\n- Verified end to end against live PyPI: a simulated\n`release(deepagents)` flags `deepagents-code` (published `0.1.49` pins\n`deepagents==0.7.0b2`, head requires `==0.7.0`); a simulated\n`release(code)` reports no conflicts.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"8b74217e92f16c79cc71d04eb3d5eeff26579227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8b74217e92f16c79cc71d04eb3d5eeff26579227"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqam/SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAu0QAJarN/poWOqJ2dYbB+Z0pI9I\nbzroccv8sFwMgoLVzBlHsZcB/PJYRfti4sXrVCViBJSYcbjy8jw2D6coOuBdDEc1\nUTFqXY0KkJHKLvA7Roy7Yyc/k/hqgoE/ShCjk3lNTrZXqsenOCM9jNzahIFPJrvv\nMtGRE8cnQnT9Zm3Nkfobwlsfvx+etHtyHB9931oK23b9X1QPsuJECCOAKl6ETxoB\npHl8B6GLcI0tEUBlPktIHGAd8PZD2EqB/11GDIMMs7Bnl/T+pXECQAQN2KccJ+Sa\nuSKT/RFpimEmxMbQJe52k42oBfwPnCMvuQYC/HvGaYcTxvvU+KG0dBTaLwFzsfZB\nasQkBzpu5T0gQ5sIpc8ApgGBaQ8QSuSPKN/9sRyM5PznWQs6VPsjHcp3yV3u2at0\nVbZIEZyxRddzpeDgc3mERgSCx4zN5VlsWujGl7tzirSJWfJShyYTiWObGQhMlxnN\nx0qLkYgWn5HSoLQpy4kl5UTFp0KWnkxI2Kw9sDY7XjHOsTQOUrELU4Pv//1BTHv0\nzs+KGNorZuoN1bqHbsjGjiQHiJLkPgGXIX7jmETfqeUUzTqRJsxdCmNbZpVlFj1m\ngAuL9Gd0fvc/ZBRczCPaWePERBu7UAJSjoR/kwGBJGc5/4Qq5JHHAXy6uoYPsSZd\nA2EwBCtIrz8WuiBWVErM\n=k267\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8b74217e92f16c79cc71d04eb3d5eeff26579227\nparent 8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785360338 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785360338 -0400\n\nci(infra): soft-run release-deps check under acknowledged bypass (#5168)\n\n`release-deps: acknowledged` no longer skips any job. Every check runs\nand reports; the label only stops one of them from blocking.\n\n| Check | Effect of the label |\n| --- | --- |\n| `📦 Check Release Dependencies` | Resolves in report-only mode; check\ngoes green, sticky comment still lists the packages that owe releases. |\n| `📦 Check Dependency Freshness` | None. Advisory in all cases; its\ncomment stays on the PR. |\n| `🔗 Check SDK Pin` | Clears the hard failure on a **prerelease** pin.\nStale-pin behaviour unchanged. |\n\nA green check under the label now means \"the listed packages still owe\nreleases,\" never \"deps resolved.\" Skipping the resolve job instead\nproduced a green check that read as an all-clear while PyPI installs\nwere still broken — and deleted the record of the remaining release\ndebt.\n\n## Follow-up releases are reported on every path\n\nThe check lists sibling release-please packages whose **published** PyPI\n`requires_dist` cannot satisfy a head requirement on the branch — e.g.\npublished `0.1.49` constrains `deepagents` to `==0.7.0b2`; head requires\n`==0.7.0`.\n\nThis is gated on neither the label nor the resolver verdict. Resolution\npassing only proves the *changed* package installs today; a\nreverse-dependent whose published metadata caps the new line still\nbreaks `pip install` for its own users. So a clean resolve with\noutstanding follow-ups posts the sticky and stays green, and the sticky\nclears itself only once nothing is left to report.\n\nThe analysis is advisory and can never fail the gate — a crash in it\ndegrades to a warning on the report. Packages whose PyPI metadata could\nnot be determined are reported as indeterminate and never produce a\n\"needs release\" claim.\n\nOverlap between a published constraint and a head requirement is decided\nby a finite probe sample, which can prove overlap but never\ndisjointness. The error directions are asymmetric — falsely reporting\noverlap hides a real conflict, while falsely reporting disjoint only\nadds a spurious row — so every inconclusive case reports\noverlap-unknown.\n\n`RELEASING.md` gains a \"Releasing a new line ahead of its dependents\"\nsection covering when the label is appropriate (coordinated release\norder) versus when the metadata is simply wrong, plus the table above.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 717 tests pass across the helper suites (`pytest\n.github/scripts/tests`, which is what `ci.yml` runs); `ty check\n.github/scripts/release/` is clean.\n- New unit tests cover: follow-ups rendered on failure and on clean\nresolves; every conflicting package listed even where the resolver would\nprove only one; acknowledged soft-run exits 0 and writes the sticky; an\nacknowledged clean run clears it; indeterminate metadata never claims\n\"needs release\"; an unpublished package is not reported as\nindeterminate; a crash in the advisory analysis does not fail the gate.\n- The overlap heuristic has a boundary matrix (`==` vs `>=,<`, open vs\nclosed edges, `~=`, `!=`, wildcard pins, single-component versions)\nasserting disjointness is only reported when provable.\n- Verified end to end against live PyPI: a simulated\n`release(deepagents)` flags `deepagents-code` (published `0.1.49` pins\n`deepagents==0.7.0b2`, head requires `==0.7.0`); a simulated\n`release(code)` reports no conflicts.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:25:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba731fb1c47a55f2b46e440eb245c18b3abe434/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5"}]},{"sha":"8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlODEyMjVlNThhNjE4MTk2NTgwYTA2NTA2NDkyZDZhMzQyNDZjZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T21:17:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:17:32Z"},"message":"style(code): markdown table for built-in tools in `/tools` (#5135)\n\n`/tools` now lists built-in tools in a markdown table, so a long\ndescription wraps inside its own cell instead of spilling back to the\nleft margin and running under the name column.\n\n---\n\nThe interactive tool listing previously assembled fixed-width plain-text\nrows: each description was padded to the widest name in its group, and\nonce a row exceeded the terminal width its continuation lines wrapped to\ncolumn 0, running underneath the name column and undoing the alignment\nthe padding existed to create. `_render_tool_catalog` now returns\nmarkdown source and is mounted through the markdown `AppMessage` path\nthat `/version` already uses, so built-in tools render as a `Tool` /\n`Description` table that Rich lays out and wraps at the current width.\nMCP groups keep their names-only listing (their descriptions live in\n`/mcp`), and unavailable MCP servers become a `Server` / `Status` table;\nwording, pluralization, and the `/mcp` pointer are unchanged.\n\nMarkdown is a new parsing surface for text that originates outside the\ncodebase — MCP server names, statuses and discovery details, and tool\nnames and descriptions read off a custom local agent. `_escape_markdown`\nbackslash-escapes markdown punctuation and collapses line breaks to\nspaces. Both halves matter: unescaped punctuation is parsed, so\n`<b>x</b>` is swallowed as HTML and `[d](u)` collapses to its link text,\nand an embedded newline ends the current block, which would let an\nunavailable server's multi-line `str(exc)` split its table row, end the\ntable and leave the remaining rows as literal pipe syntax, or inject\nheadings of its own. `_markdown_table` escapes every header as well as\nevery cell, so a `|` cannot forge a column, and raises `ValueError` on a\nrow that does not match its headers rather than emitting a table\nmarkdown would silently pad or truncate. Long cells fold instead of\nellipsizing, so a narrow terminal still keeps every character of a tool\nname.\n\nTests round-trip a specimen of each character in the escape table\nthrough the real renderer — the table is load-bearing, and dropping any\nsingle character from it changes what the user sees — and cover header\nescaping, the ragged-row guard, HTML entities and line-break\nnormalization, the fold, and that the built-in section renders as an\nactual table rather than degenerating into paragraphs.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c09b8fee-73cb-6335-2f52-460af1a1bd6a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbb092324fff6d8483da8876fcb756a8ad76fea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bbb092324fff6d8483da8876fcb756a8ad76fea2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqam3sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4fcQAK7R/zunlRdMSlxebqudaplP\nttPpl1kVIwV9bxtKK7UJPwJ3aQvt2aN2Vch3gefmnHSCgI7EptidZZkkZvc31MTy\nvqWPdeVcPKk2vdvjyLYqyeFoow3H2fErtJZCK2vM8dAsYUTRVuB4K6iRBUGBnpRf\nQ2cuZBQE2fVzUkr2gCWfqS0N3vf7v84kNbNilMGUcUj1hjrSaXwDoLS5NTw9Y8z+\nOWPOSVhEFhcmJ4EZBrHl4H/O6afU6IgqUUu6bj5LncIt946/XNbphVnlDb21uZT8\n/eDAsoKxVALDAQ5f8tRnpLucYUrxUV3LUzFP6ncSy6d7grvyWX8LJ3ZdSGGEbW3m\nyfnC+kxxr6cyMVtkNH3AJ2ARXdPXqfBC2GhkPtc75LmTftLilRfNlTSt5nlWlNk/\nZ+wHzvql+m5WIWlT+Das0nyk7GIYaFqxjoKiNcsKnc5HmV93VP6SOWwKFUXV2O0g\n7GsOZKUAhH9Tek7EW1BS5mhDgeM1lpkh/GSIp+jPFLlvnMPuSLL5Kohf6ww1HzjZ\nHF7ZWpE0urf5HyxUFN9KN/jowkn4p5hHR2InOjFKEdPrxI4LRF9gNdztM8xoG9E/\nNVmhFflHWHz6bmzoYGsMq0FHKRXfEN8bbjfseEl7AVs+/JTevJmt6xSHYGL+7ic5\n1BpDvW3nmE9R7S5tRp4P\n=Qnuy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bbb092324fff6d8483da8876fcb756a8ad76fea2\nparent 9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785359852 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785359852 -0400\n\nstyle(code): markdown table for built-in tools in `/tools` (#5135)\n\n`/tools` now lists built-in tools in a markdown table, so a long\ndescription wraps inside its own cell instead of spilling back to the\nleft margin and running under the name column.\n\n---\n\nThe interactive tool listing previously assembled fixed-width plain-text\nrows: each description was padded to the widest name in its group, and\nonce a row exceeded the terminal width its continuation lines wrapped to\ncolumn 0, running underneath the name column and undoing the alignment\nthe padding existed to create. `_render_tool_catalog` now returns\nmarkdown source and is mounted through the markdown `AppMessage` path\nthat `/version` already uses, so built-in tools render as a `Tool` /\n`Description` table that Rich lays out and wraps at the current width.\nMCP groups keep their names-only listing (their descriptions live in\n`/mcp`), and unavailable MCP servers become a `Server` / `Status` table;\nwording, pluralization, and the `/mcp` pointer are unchanged.\n\nMarkdown is a new parsing surface for text that originates outside the\ncodebase — MCP server names, statuses and discovery details, and tool\nnames and descriptions read off a custom local agent. `_escape_markdown`\nbackslash-escapes markdown punctuation and collapses line breaks to\nspaces. Both halves matter: unescaped punctuation is parsed, so\n`<b>x</b>` is swallowed as HTML and `[d](u)` collapses to its link text,\nand an embedded newline ends the current block, which would let an\nunavailable server's multi-line `str(exc)` split its table row, end the\ntable and leave the remaining rows as literal pipe syntax, or inject\nheadings of its own. `_markdown_table` escapes every header as well as\nevery cell, so a `|` cannot forge a column, and raises `ValueError` on a\nrow that does not match its headers rather than emitting a table\nmarkdown would silently pad or truncate. Long cells fold instead of\nellipsizing, so a narrow terminal still keeps every character of a tool\nname.\n\nTests round-trip a specimen of each character in the escape table\nthrough the real renderer — the table is load-bearing, and dropping any\nsingle character from it changes what the user sees — and cover header\nescaping, the ragged-row guard, HTML entities and line-break\nnormalization, the fold, and that the built-in section renders as an\nactual table rather than degenerating into paragraphs.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c09b8fee-73cb-6335-2f52-460af1a1bd6a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:17:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e81225e58a618196580a06506492d6a34246ce5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736"}]},{"sha":"9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlhZDhkZGVkMDg1MzNhNzkxNWRjMzVlMDVmNGM5MmMzYjFlY2I3MzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T21:15:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T21:15:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): consistent styling and links for thread status messages (#5118)\n\nThread status notes in the transcript (`Resumed thread:`, `Started new\nthread:`, `Previous thread:`) now all render with the same dim italic\nstyling, and the mouse pointer changes to a hand when hovering a link\ninside any app message. Re-selecting the thread the session is already\non now shows a transient toast instead of an inline chat message,\nmatching the existing same-model behavior.\n\n---\n\nSeveral related inconsistencies, all visible in a single resume:\n\n- `AppMessage` applies `dim italic` only when it is handed a plain\nstring; a pre-built `Content` is rendered as-is. Thread notes start life\nas plain strings and are upgraded to linked `Content` once the LangSmith\nURL resolves, so they visibly brightened relative to every other app\nmessage. `_build_thread_message` now styles each span `dim italic`,\nmatching what `AppMessage` does for strings (and what other linked app\nmessages such as `/trace` output already do explicitly).\n- `AppMessage` carries a `text` pointer in CSS with no hover handling,\nso an embedded link gave no cursor affordance. It now toggles the\npointer on `MouseMove`/`Leave` using the existing `event_targets_link`\nhelper, mirroring `AssistantMessage`. Link clicks still route through\n`open_style_link`, so URL safety checks are unchanged.\n- The `Already on thread` note was the odd one out: an inline transcript\nmessage for something that changed no state, where the equivalent\n`Already using <model>` no-op is a toast. It is now a toast too. Its\ndedup guard — don't stack an identical toast while the previous one is\npresumed still on-screen, but do re-announce once that has expired — is\nhoisted into `_notify_unchanged_once` and shared by both call sites. A\nsuccessful thread switch re-arms the toast. The sibling `Switched to\nthread directory` message stays inline because it records a real state\nchange.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4b51fe78-171c-1374-8355-489bab7e616d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ad91adf67f6a3751aa71016ba17af85bb6488ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6ad91adf67f6a3751aa71016ba17af85bb6488ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqam2LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAydgQAEQQu/NORvs+xg4EmnECReRV\neQ8myb5mXqbiTbjsS0nwpRcSsgvWw6AxEV1M0cgfCg5UaM11g9okFVEic4aeQ7oQ\n1RY8M94hogDdR1B1SKsBD7I/rRUpfJam+mVE5WEsupBd2AfsdSLIyVDzD42IG4hx\nhab6B66ZLEB5ZCVmbDqGzWdZeR+6WvA+Z7UWcaYXrUWFN5VWemsK7Z5iN5C1ecXS\nZbjGPDq8eXP6+NzUDnuS6f2Asupovaif1eFrwpkZ0GE9492/u7Qn7Cm6RD7/+XQr\ntcOM4bftULqxLAFUuWmXDCgBR5X1vpwvgBqhICDNuV2PdAWKfbuWqKh2LDbTU/Mf\nuuYwBdJcis0ZLkputoTjCiiEP6BgLoJidhlDeMR/F+WBOj4w9Vxx6xqSEgUXddTN\n4bEuH9DNOTXY7OG/xfvqLDT+SJROfb/b68kcGbnbgD+fymQ2PdF4bNkFILbhpbcH\n1xIa6JQOC6J9ah9t1Iz7x/FZOKqD8hvIkuJye3aCaCKkmNCJyqAce0pAQrHaj6O6\ncppJr9XJkOy/YjMkSQcoHQ4NzvhEF/2MxjWFj554ezo6GNZlTyZmatbGk7wDdA8N\nEgj327V+QqHSPYMdPkIX3r13JTzFrHYt3SeJ6AzhKA1hhahBpOstqEIc3Xx3UKjL\nC1ONQh60uMtY7Z3Ejpyi\n=m4q5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6ad91adf67f6a3751aa71016ba17af85bb6488ab\nparent 78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785359755 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785359755 -0400\n\nfix(code): consistent styling and links for thread status messages (#5118)\n\nThread status notes in the transcript (`Resumed thread:`, `Started new\nthread:`, `Previous thread:`) now all render with the same dim italic\nstyling, and the mouse pointer changes to a hand when hovering a link\ninside any app message. Re-selecting the thread the session is already\non now shows a transient toast instead of an inline chat message,\nmatching the existing same-model behavior.\n\n---\n\nSeveral related inconsistencies, all visible in a single resume:\n\n- `AppMessage` applies `dim italic` only when it is handed a plain\nstring; a pre-built `Content` is rendered as-is. Thread notes start life\nas plain strings and are upgraded to linked `Content` once the LangSmith\nURL resolves, so they visibly brightened relative to every other app\nmessage. `_build_thread_message` now styles each span `dim italic`,\nmatching what `AppMessage` does for strings (and what other linked app\nmessages such as `/trace` output already do explicitly).\n- `AppMessage` carries a `text` pointer in CSS with no hover handling,\nso an embedded link gave no cursor affordance. It now toggles the\npointer on `MouseMove`/`Leave` using the existing `event_targets_link`\nhelper, mirroring `AssistantMessage`. Link clicks still route through\n`open_style_link`, so URL safety checks are unchanged.\n- The `Already on thread` note was the odd one out: an inline transcript\nmessage for something that changed no state, where the equivalent\n`Already using <model>` no-op is a toast. It is now a toast too. Its\ndedup guard — don't stack an identical toast while the previous one is\npresumed still on-screen, but do re-announce once that has expired — is\nhoisted into `_notify_unchanged_once` and shared by both call sites. A\nsuccessful thread switch re-arms the toast. The sibling `Switched to\nthread directory` message stays inline because it records a real state\nchange.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4b51fe78-171c-1374-8355-489bab7e616d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T21:15:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9ad8dded08533a7915dc35e05f4c92c3b1ecb736/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717"}]},{"sha":"78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc4ZWJlMmQyN2MwZWM1YjViZjEzNjhmMWYxYjFmNDQyZjkyMTI3MTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T20:58:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:58:10Z"},"message":"feat(code): show `ask_user` answers on the answered tool row (#5100)\n\n`ask_user` rows can now be expanded to show what you answered.\n\nBefore, the row just said \"User answered\" and your replies were gone:\nthe question widget is removed once you submit, and Ctrl+O only reveals\nthe questions, not the answers. The row now keeps the same Q&A text the\nagent received, behind a `… N answers — click to expand` line.\n\n### Keeping the row correct while it waits\n\nThe agent's copy of the answers is the source of truth, so the row stays\npending until the graph sends it back. That puts the row in a state it\nwas never in before: you've answered, but the row isn't finished.\n\nIf the turn then ends early — the agent crashes, you press Ctrl+C, the\nstream drops — cleanup sweeps every unfinished row and marks it failed.\nWithout care, a question you answered normally would show up as an\nerror. So the row records its outcome the moment you answer, and those\nsweeps leave it alone.\n\n### Answers stay out of hook scripts\n\nHooks receive a short summary like \"User answered\", never the answer\ntext. The row's summary also comes from the tool's status rather than\nfrom what you typed — so answering literally `(cancelled)` doesn't make\nthe row look cancelled.\n\n### Edge cases\n\nNeither of these is on the normal path, but both were silent before:\n\n- **Two `ask_user` calls in one turn.** Cancelling one prompt abandons\nthe turn, throwing away answers you already submitted to the other.\nThose rows now say the answers weren't delivered and you get a message\ntelling you, rather than the answers vanishing while the row claims\nsuccess. (A single prompt cancels as a whole — there's no per-question\ncancel — so this needs the model to make two parallel `ask_user` calls,\nwhich its instructions discourage.)\n- **Malformed resume payloads.** If the answers coming back don't line\nup with the questions asked, the tool now reports a failure instead of\nguessing at the pairing — a missing answer used to shift every later\nanswer onto the wrong question, and the agent was told that pairing was\ncorrect. The TUI can't produce this (it always returns one answer per\nquestion); it's hardening for other clients driving the same interrupt.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3cfcfbbb-5100-48fd-0b9f-cd29256e498b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"99f46fdf93a96d06580a388683903d2d780fbee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/99f46fdf93a96d06580a388683903d2d780fbee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqamliCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvNsQAI9tnVqrF2r71Hlb08fH1iLK\ndBF0L+hhjfsDWi19/GMqj0X45X/RVMmV3ySUZ1qS7y4ct5CIeNYOfkIjf/d5UXDi\n6XRwM24xc62NGGKTrWY696++DPyV51F86ud+8jsLCTweAJPm+HGvhXYhwSjt8Rdr\nX8cjG7tueQlVZ9RlnFsBcvMLMkqTrb5nUoeolqBSkM68JumyuJRkSIZux34f3SN7\nCo0LY1+9zYg0dK5hRUF3W5RiCx98wdSJibE/aGxDNfg41ExgI1vd0+OWunJFqur0\nEo1aFjbgYbgwPt/+6z4CoX6K3n8SeAyXSEbYvjK7JlBe3zko7OYyAeZ1xUz/qt2y\nbFRmsmqU7WcfP/em/lPBd5SGZmVmXRmD7Z7hh9vJb2iuO1/UtXK3BRNiRJYx6MV4\nm+l0jd7ItmXPmNX3scXgz7Hnnvo/Y2iM9mbqrUvLGGXYhl3sYS7biG2/NgsV62/D\nWepG/BAWXSNRFjWnVUZAhGDt6Ku5SVVjE1XAY7JyLxH1vqpD2w1ihmQyL/3vf+z4\nUCr3lHlJRC6VBUgrhI4Q4Q3MSv5+SXj8q5qj892Kwmt1xudfb+9IHVwja1penx91\n/7YMJmv+8pzyHOQUq1pyYhpe6pxfwfbqBbErhuRaHNrGw3W6/izodyta2kC5QyDb\nBbmdWv9qxJGGmvAuaUkd\n=d3Zb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 99f46fdf93a96d06580a388683903d2d780fbee3\nparent 66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785358690 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785358690 -0400\n\nfeat(code): show `ask_user` answers on the answered tool row (#5100)\n\n`ask_user` rows can now be expanded to show what you answered.\n\nBefore, the row just said \"User answered\" and your replies were gone:\nthe question widget is removed once you submit, and Ctrl+O only reveals\nthe questions, not the answers. The row now keeps the same Q&A text the\nagent received, behind a `… N answers — click to expand` line.\n\n### Keeping the row correct while it waits\n\nThe agent's copy of the answers is the source of truth, so the row stays\npending until the graph sends it back. That puts the row in a state it\nwas never in before: you've answered, but the row isn't finished.\n\nIf the turn then ends early — the agent crashes, you press Ctrl+C, the\nstream drops — cleanup sweeps every unfinished row and marks it failed.\nWithout care, a question you answered normally would show up as an\nerror. So the row records its outcome the moment you answer, and those\nsweeps leave it alone.\n\n### Answers stay out of hook scripts\n\nHooks receive a short summary like \"User answered\", never the answer\ntext. The row's summary also comes from the tool's status rather than\nfrom what you typed — so answering literally `(cancelled)` doesn't make\nthe row look cancelled.\n\n### Edge cases\n\nNeither of these is on the normal path, but both were silent before:\n\n- **Two `ask_user` calls in one turn.** Cancelling one prompt abandons\nthe turn, throwing away answers you already submitted to the other.\nThose rows now say the answers weren't delivered and you get a message\ntelling you, rather than the answers vanishing while the row claims\nsuccess. (A single prompt cancels as a whole — there's no per-question\ncancel — so this needs the model to make two parallel `ask_user` calls,\nwhich its instructions discourage.)\n- **Malformed resume payloads.** If the answers coming back don't line\nup with the questions asked, the tool now reports a failure instead of\nguessing at the pairing — a missing answer used to shift every later\nanswer onto the wrong question, and the agent was told that pairing was\ncorrect. The TUI can't produce this (it always returns one answer per\nquestion); it's hardening for other clients driving the same interrupt.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/3cfcfbbb-5100-48fd-0b9f-cd29256e498b)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:58:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/78ebe2d27c0ec5b5bf1368f1f1b1f442f9212717/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f"}]},{"sha":"66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY2ZDUyNmYwZTQzYzRjMWM1ZDNhYjljYzNkNDIzZmVmZTE2MDZlNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T20:56:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:56:59Z"},"message":"feat(code): surface Hooks v2 runtime feedback (#5045)\n\nHook execution now reports progress, warnings, notices, and permission\ndecisions consistently in the TUI and non-interactive client. Configured\n`statusMessage` values appear while handlers run, and server-owned hook\noutput is no longer confined to logs.\n\n---\n\nA shared `HookFeedback` presenter keeps event ownership out of the UI\nlayer while preserving ordered engine reduction. It deduplicates visible\ndiagnostics, tracks concurrent handler statuses without clearing a\nstill-running hook, emits validated terminal sequences once, and\nattributes hook-owned allow/deny decisions in both clients.\n\nRe-anchored onto `main` after #5105 squash-merged. Call sites keep the\nparent `WorkspaceTrust` API and layer `HookFeedback` on top.\n\n## Review Guide\n\n1. `hooks/feedback.py` — `HookFeedback` presenter (progress / notices /\ndecisions)\n2. `hooks/engine.py` — handler progress reporting\n3. `hooks/client_lifecycle.py`, `hooks/client.py` — feedback attachment\nvs log-only\n4. `client/non_interactive.py`, `app.py`, `tui/widgets/status.py` —\nUI/status sinks\n5. Skim: `HOOKS.md`, tiny adapter/runtime/threat-model edits\n6. Tests: `test_feedback.py`, then engine / client-lifecycle / status\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Added focused presenter, concurrent progress, `statusMessage`,\nserver-notice, and permission-attribution coverage.\n- Targeted feedback / engine / lifecycle / trust / status suite passed\non the prior stack tip; CI re-runs on this re-anchor.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **feat(code): surface Hooks v2 runtime feedback** :point_left:\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://www.git-town.com)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","tree":{"sha":"ccbd3fe23840c438b85dcd0698b1858266a9945c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ccbd3fe23840c438b85dcd0698b1858266a9945c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqamkbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjL8QAJuYGD37/SlVI+Y0LzSM1ip0\nmmT0VPmmYQWjdeZHM0ROAj2GBn5/VDWrcW29C0p2sfDMF8jRcgPrT0qKTAwC0M9R\nhxygl9ku6O68zRSSfgko81fGUv2jyj0E5sLx4k4qAYG2dYdjC8iJL9z9q4jCNTfv\nwVHS7aYGnBX6YmDUDzD91IUKxaiXjYDVuqqPkIi0w/Saoqalmf20l9LHSncunwCU\nylVUKQsIGOGg+M+iD06sMceETEX3LbuwMKcCD+JPOyn+eTBRsnmZ9nrcJwOPPjGe\nWVgczAB2esNMj05xbfHqo7t35EiMUHXtoA+vDOG7oiXsErlWg59YhkgrGTkE3NVR\njfrA9Il9aj3tsqzPRtcbNi7OjfDmdsdBOeoSh/o3+0NZuuFZvMIQhJiAjDo9jZvc\n8Ud098eAhEMvUUFYTwqP40XtHUhH5g+jYGnZsYGoQmPVNQA73VBGmEnZHvqk1QhK\noQilMeSpt0hXgIT0Hxzgbnvye/OuRdBlmrxdYab9crEq1gTDlM7rBoicdVNxYfTJ\npUnJCKCvwU5Nb++UGuFGVKfZMf/GFGc89G0AkssO16k4DRHQNrA9TcH0RyAANb2g\nAyC4ONPQbWtrvafxQF/AOUDIzeaSXZwCUMWqULimhc7ZqI7t5F6HaZGU97+oCYdG\nQSTDgP/qfj1uZLK3Ea6F\n=S6wX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ccbd3fe23840c438b85dcd0698b1858266a9945c\nparent e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785358619 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785358619 -0700\n\nfeat(code): surface Hooks v2 runtime feedback (#5045)\n\nHook execution now reports progress, warnings, notices, and permission\ndecisions consistently in the TUI and non-interactive client. Configured\n`statusMessage` values appear while handlers run, and server-owned hook\noutput is no longer confined to logs.\n\n---\n\nA shared `HookFeedback` presenter keeps event ownership out of the UI\nlayer while preserving ordered engine reduction. It deduplicates visible\ndiagnostics, tracks concurrent handler statuses without clearing a\nstill-running hook, emits validated terminal sequences once, and\nattributes hook-owned allow/deny decisions in both clients.\n\nRe-anchored onto `main` after #5105 squash-merged. Call sites keep the\nparent `WorkspaceTrust` API and layer `HookFeedback` on top.\n\n## Review Guide\n\n1. `hooks/feedback.py` — `HookFeedback` presenter (progress / notices /\ndecisions)\n2. `hooks/engine.py` — handler progress reporting\n3. `hooks/client_lifecycle.py`, `hooks/client.py` — feedback attachment\nvs log-only\n4. `client/non_interactive.py`, `app.py`, `tui/widgets/status.py` —\nUI/status sinks\n5. Skim: `HOOKS.md`, tiny adapter/runtime/threat-model edits\n6. Tests: `test_feedback.py`, then engine / client-lifecycle / status\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Added focused presenter, concurrent progress, `statusMessage`,\nserver-notice, and permission-attribution coverage.\n- Targeted feedback / engine / lifecycle / trust / status suite passed\non the prior stack tip; CI re-runs on this re-anchor.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n  - **feat(code): surface Hooks v2 runtime feedback** :point_left:\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://www.git-town.com)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:57:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/66d526f0e43c4c1c5d3ab9cc3d423fefe1606e6f/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c"}]},{"sha":"e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU0N2Y5Zjk0MzkyOTBlYjc1OGFlNGZhN2U5MDBjYTNiOGU1NWUzNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T20:27:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:27:05Z"},"message":"fix(infra): run release-please after skipped trigger-releases (#5169)\n\nAfter #5161, ordinary pushes to `main` skipped the `release-please`\nmaintenance job even when the in-flight-publish guard had already\nwritten `skip=false`, so release PRs stopped refreshing.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n#5161 made `guard-pending-release` depend on `trigger-releases` so a\nmerged release commit can dispatch publish first, then refresh sibling\nrelease PRs. On a normal non-release push, `trigger-releases` is\n**skipped**.\n\nThe guard itself already overrode Actions' default `success()` gate with\n`!cancelled()` and explicit `needs.*.result` checks, so it still ran and\ncorrectly reported `skip=false`.\n\n`release-please` only had:\n\n```yaml\nif: needs.guard-pending-release.outputs.skip == 'false'\n```\n\nWithout a status-check function, Actions still applies the implicit\n`success()` gate. With a skipped ancestor behind the successful guard,\nthat gate failed closed and `release-please` was skipped with empty\nsteps — leaving the whole workflow green. Observed on:\n\n- https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30487226539\n(#5161 merge)\n- https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30487483156\n(`fix(sdk)` follow-up)\n\n## Fix\n\nGive `release-please` the same pattern as the guard:\n\n- `!cancelled()` so the upstream-skipped dispatch job does not poison\nmaintenance\n- explicit success checks on every direct dependency\n- still require `outputs.skip == 'false'` so crash / hard-timeout /\ndeferred paths stay fail-closed\n\nTests now pin this truth table (and stop asserting the old bare `skip ==\n'false'` condition, which is exactly what broke main).","tree":{"sha":"c2cad8332a2e4f0f0e82906cd6966e9659122dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c2cad8332a2e4f0f0e82906cd6966e9659122dc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqamIZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGiQQAKc3SK4BohQYCRSsBIbfwXMs\n8B5WNTNg1BvahyyTfjNBEdNXjEDyhr2QiuY2hv4lPqShWIXy1x99V+A73yyN8YPl\nC3W3C00YfKL+ryY9ncZT9fxdNbzh1oTwGyNqWR7k7wFcn5wPDA0971RLVxgmskff\n1dGzDC22XqtaDn4oAPM7eQS8vPeIXtfh2VCFD7cyUi8Nx+ObUdosJbQTSlQSa3gz\ncy5ZRnLdCX1N2PD9UV3hcq2U98jzFRiTAtib3CxVCS6mP9xILtuaRg71wSeUfqH5\nwQPvMR7WYOJ00wl9SSoVtvzHQ5SByqi5ITIJcN0CvdnFoZAL4eHzy7gRuD4sGmAC\nXbz3Bxy64RPispKXSQFKL0E0Mr2Lk1KnpDwhOVhFU7H6f2lF+qne0BOPiokNjtBv\n5e412F4VeOEazOryda33jClAVZyI3VvOnQIl5meJ6yTyh6sXiwJiLGrAOIxu0L17\n+Ia8n5mdYcKQH0SwP6NP0NPRR2VvsziSaceCZhjr1jGktdF13N9UeI1lSNJou/Ng\nK6EP90X8TgEcecrNKulenoD2LvfIzEDlhZXSUEP4Od2juflm+JF5n/5TmesdTswl\n6QOS9lnfkIgnKL0U8ntMn/mBeCeZ0p8a7BhsYjdvf4RcIgicYsnB1Ok56f4uMvUd\n9wSDVMHwutPmvx8rsWTh\n=6+3A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c2cad8332a2e4f0f0e82906cd6966e9659122dc4\nparent 2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785356825 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785356825 -0400\n\nfix(infra): run release-please after skipped trigger-releases (#5169)\n\nAfter #5161, ordinary pushes to `main` skipped the `release-please`\nmaintenance job even when the in-flight-publish guard had already\nwritten `skip=false`, so release PRs stopped refreshing.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n#5161 made `guard-pending-release` depend on `trigger-releases` so a\nmerged release commit can dispatch publish first, then refresh sibling\nrelease PRs. On a normal non-release push, `trigger-releases` is\n**skipped**.\n\nThe guard itself already overrode Actions' default `success()` gate with\n`!cancelled()` and explicit `needs.*.result` checks, so it still ran and\ncorrectly reported `skip=false`.\n\n`release-please` only had:\n\n```yaml\nif: needs.guard-pending-release.outputs.skip == 'false'\n```\n\nWithout a status-check function, Actions still applies the implicit\n`success()` gate. With a skipped ancestor behind the successful guard,\nthat gate failed closed and `release-please` was skipped with empty\nsteps — leaving the whole workflow green. Observed on:\n\n- https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30487226539\n(#5161 merge)\n- https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/30487483156\n(`fix(sdk)` follow-up)\n\n## Fix\n\nGive `release-please` the same pattern as the guard:\n\n- `!cancelled()` so the upstream-skipped dispatch job does not poison\nmaintenance\n- explicit success checks on every direct dependency\n- still require `outputs.skip == 'false'` so crash / hard-timeout /\ndeferred paths stay fail-closed\n\nTests now pin this truth table (and stop asserting the old bare `skip ==\n'false'` condition, which is exactly what broke main).","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:27:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e47f9f9439290eb758ae4fa7e900ca3b8e55e36c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66"}]},{"sha":"2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIwNTRjMDc4MDcxYjQyNDg3MDdjMmIyOGM3ZTUyNTRlMzY3MDNlNjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T20:11:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:11:16Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): warn instead of silently skipping unresolved state schemas (#5166)\n\n`private_state_field_names` resolved annotations under a blanket\n`contextlib.suppress(Exception)`.\n\nA schema whose `PrivateStateAttr` annotation references a\n`TYPE_CHECKING`-only name raises `NameError` from `get_type_hints`, so\nthe function returned an empty set with no diagnostic. Every private\nfield on that schema is then forwarded to, and merged back from,\nsubagents — the exact leak the marker exists to prevent, with nothing in\nthe logs to explain it.\n\nThis catches only the annotation-resolution errors (`NameError`,\n`TypeError`, `AttributeError`), logs which schema failed and what the\nconsequence is, and still skips that schema rather than failing the\nwhole agent — a caller may own several unrelated schemas.\n\nSplit out of #5164.","tree":{"sha":"0aff3ba976be0c4da522491f595b7378966cd23c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0aff3ba976be0c4da522491f595b7378966cd23c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqal5kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6g0QAJwQK82T3jKQVFdROXxiZouf\nJBWLIIEZD1e4fVrdk1MnPNKtyIQTQTP7O77G6YtaD6UcEhRVzrtUEVOaRD9FmIvM\njDja9HM+d9TDIcWcFXCydA+84egEzshTEovLf7A3vfnZTcwGON3oFcQQ/2tvKzsm\nGF6c5tM18fDrl7gysTkpwVfUn0zOvuqIcOvQ0GhkUYG1tYXfU6OVM0A3+j44wls7\nvCwuMVljYUMsidU1FJg5RZpYnM0avF4ebuHfDItxqz7dJXUZLjvEtJVSjRU8pHer\nqpImtRHWB+Oe8fyYpnqNd/TBPKW9Sx1RxWjwtDNlHmeHi2bjnCvuPbO0EYcRS+L0\n3QeSnWa6XvyOYRTUNPS45ukM+9y2qMwJ/s/8q8l2Um7LY7Zg6f0p+BY2dgCKo+8P\niBVZQg3MWakpASbrtOYVJxmv2aFHj3l0Qi6gfjlpHtRp5KgFBpSKkRcJAvCHwOTq\nyf88jgSPJNbOSSTXWtBGsJ3a/70sf3RTgZz+PN8j/jT7/nJzCZ1mtsjAvqCRY1q2\n8Ot0j84Wd3UuqTxdSgPTJYzrrVZXbbGyOXjjNHmhtqa5XhaKyphw5AYaaZa4+pGr\niL9V0snRSsn7Zx58sb4bJqiV09tCQRIrWoiNqlLWcAzZAocgt29CVBBqQQEEpwa8\nxWYFhpEM6lrRHz+9/v2a\n=zcIE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0aff3ba976be0c4da522491f595b7378966cd23c\nparent 453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785355876 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785355876 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): warn instead of silently skipping unresolved state schemas (#5166)\n\n`private_state_field_names` resolved annotations under a blanket\n`contextlib.suppress(Exception)`.\n\nA schema whose `PrivateStateAttr` annotation references a\n`TYPE_CHECKING`-only name raises `NameError` from `get_type_hints`, so\nthe function returned an empty set with no diagnostic. Every private\nfield on that schema is then forwarded to, and merged back from,\nsubagents — the exact leak the marker exists to prevent, with nothing in\nthe logs to explain it.\n\nThis catches only the annotation-resolution errors (`NameError`,\n`TypeError`, `AttributeError`), logs which schema failed and what the\nconsequence is, and still skips that schema rather than failing the\nwhole agent — a caller may own several unrelated schemas.\n\nSplit out of #5164.","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:11:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2054c078071b4248707c2b28c7e5254e36703e66/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747"}]},{"sha":"453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1MzgzODM2N2FhYjNiNjRmZjgyNzVkMWY5OGRjZGI2MGVjYTY3NDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T20:07:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T20:07:11Z"},"message":"ci(infra): refresh open release PRs after sibling merges (#5161)\n\n## The situation before\n\nThis repo releases ten packages independently, so it is normal to have\nseveral open release PRs at once. Those PRs all touch shared files —\nmost importantly `.release-please-manifest.json`. When one of them\nmerges, the others are instantly stale, and release-please is what\nnormally rewrites them.\n\nBut release commits deliberately skipped release-please entirely, for a\ngood reason: running it while a publish is mid-flight is dangerous.\nMerging a release PR bumps the manifest immediately, while the git tag\nis only created minutes later by `release.yml`. In that window\nrelease-please sees a version with no matching tag, concludes the\npackage was never released, and proposes resetting it to `0.1.0` with\nthe full history. That is not hypothetical — it happened once (`0.1.8` →\n`0.1.0`).\n\nSo the workflow chose the safe option: on a release commit, dispatch the\npublish and do nothing else.\n\n## Why that was a problem\n\n**Completing a publish does not push to `main`.** It creates a tag and a\nGitHub release, and neither re-triggers `release-please.yml`.\n\nSo after a release merge there was no follow-up run — ever. The\nremaining open release PRs stayed stale until some unrelated push\nhappened to land, which could be days. This made other release PRs sit\nwith merge conflicts \"forever\" on shared files.\n\n## What this changes\n\nPublishing still goes first and is never blocked. The difference is that\nthe *same run* now sticks around, waits for publishing to settle, and\nthen does the maintenance it used to skip:\n\n1. `detect-release-commit`\n2. `trigger-releases` — fires immediately, `needs` unchanged, still not\nblocked by anything\n3. `guard-pending-release` — new: also runs on release commits, after a\nsuccessful dispatch. Polls until no merged release PR is still labeled\n`autorelease: pending`\n4. `release-please` — runs only on an explicit `skip=false` from the\nguard\n5. `update-lockfiles` — unchanged\n\nNormal (non-release) pushes are unaffected: same wait, same fail-closed\nmaintenance gate as before.\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Why this ordering is safe</b></summary>\n\n**Publishing cannot be delayed by the wait.** `trigger-releases` depends\nonly on `detect-release-commit`, and the guard is deliberately outside\nthe `release-please` concurrency group — a poll of up to 45 minutes must\nnot hold the serialization slot other pushes queue on. Only step 4 is\nserialized, since release-please mutates shared release branches.\n\n**Maintenance requires a positive all-clear.** `release-please` runs\nonly on `skip == 'false'`. A guard that crashes, times out, or is\nskipped leaves that output unset, which blocks maintenance rather than\nletting it recompute against unverified state. `trigger-releases` is\nintentionally *not* in `release-please.needs`, so its skipped status on\nnormal pushes can't loosen that gate.\n\n**The wait is repo-wide by design.** It covers every pending release PR,\nnot just the merged one, because release-please recomputes *all*\ncomponents on every run — any single package sitting between \"version\nbumped\" and \"tag created\" is enough to trigger the downgrade above.\nScoping the wait to your own PR would not be safe.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Hardening added after review</b></summary>\n\nRouting release commits through the guard exposed three paths that\npreviously could not be reached, plus one latent bug:\n\n- **A release commit matching no package used to be a silent no-op.**\nThe package list is hardcoded in both `detect-release-commit` and\n`trigger-releases`. If a future package is wired into one but not the\nother, nothing publishes, nothing refreshes, and every job reports\nsuccess. The detector now fails loudly, and a config-derived test keeps\nthe two lists from drifting.\n- **The guard treated an unreadable API response as \"nothing pending.\"**\n`format_pending` swallowed its own parse failures, so a\nsuccessful-but-unparseable `gh` response was indistinguishable from an\nempty result — which would wave release-please through during exactly\nthe dangerous window. Parse failures now feed the existing\nretry/fail-closed path.\n- **A failed publish reddened two workflows.** Since the pending set is\nrepo-wide, a package left stuck days earlier would also fail an\nunrelated release that dispatched perfectly. Release commits now defer\nwith `skip=true` and a step summary naming the failed run, extending the\nmechanism hotfix pushes already used. Ordinary pushes still fail loudly,\nwhere a red guard is the only signal a human would see. Maintenance is\nskipped either way — this only changes red vs. green and whether the\nmessage is actionable.\n- **`git log` was unchecked**, so a failure would silently misclassify\nthe push and route a failed release down the wrong branch.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Cases that still need a later push</b></summary>\n\nThese are documented in `RELEASING.md` with the signal to look for and\nwhat to do:\n\n| Situation | Signal |\n| --- | --- |\n| Publish still in flight after 45 min | `release-please.yml` green,\n`deferred` step summary |\n| Publish failed (yours, or one stuck earlier) | `release.yml` red;\n`release-please.yml` green with a `deferred (release commit)` summary |\n| GitHub release state unreadable | `release-please.yml` **red** at\n`guard-pending-release` |\n| Several release PRs merged at once | Some `release-please` jobs show\n**cancelled** — expected; the surviving newest run recomputes every\ncomponent |\n\nCross-run sibling merges can still race around the pending-label window.\nThis intentionally does not add a hard global cross-run barrier.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Testing</b></summary>\n\n`.github/scripts/tests` passes (681 tests). The guard's `if:` condition\nis now pinned by a truth table over a small expression evaluator rather\nthan substring checks — mutation-tested against five broken variants\n(flattened parens, `||`↔`&&` swap, negated trigger check, `always()` for\n`!cancelled()`), all of which are caught and four of which passed the\nprevious assertions.\n\nAlso verified directly: every `run:` block passes `bash -n`;\n`format_pending` correctly separates \"empty\" from \"unreadable\" across\nsix payloads; and the guard's three exit paths behave as intended when\ndriven with stubbed `gh`/`git` (ordinary push → exit 1 with `skip`\nunset; release commit and hotfix → exit 0 with `skip=true`).\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"9e26add6069215cefb3e014266074067765547e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9e26add6069215cefb3e014266074067765547e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqal1vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPs8QAGyEnCtWTuv+J3BpCu4sA4X/\nVNx8JOM9LHvftDK1eNQGfmBGPnBim81y6QZhQp4Bkk0l0TTSPqBq0bHFE6SfOMXN\nxdCaHvN59wSJeTTfLCXglZM1PY/JoGx210W29lRG6vQ0d21Gez2kLSPZONKSfQEK\nerU+lvDA1KHCZxoW8RHKvMZZm2bVwgaQT4E2LaaxyI4Q73L1r8FHcpaF7RehPTcf\nc2gIsgkKC3YnwQIRKyyXY/ueklzUz2VGJMqkCTbTkK8tVSVZJlTk79CZobfqTO1h\nZ/0XLRJB7BEWaEfoLXKnkpFRwSKf5EDG+q5Hege4UVGk4Txf9xqmIDqyLnkD51OO\nVfD8ISmE3iIOqnzHWPCHCj7YVEocrXKMHVc/+jTT5rXcA3ar2tDXVc+GGlHRRcuI\ntFzdjCQDNyGGvPVytvqzNy2LqBv/s3XDT7O5KRVJzzNG0DAdQYvPE+OLTLq8qctZ\n+NtJrbZ8b6DGc4TOJPRu2Qb3NCbo167Hp67xuPvdYWRPrfqDlUWue6EupwqgetE7\nEq598rCV5YbImeSq2sgw6fxSnKgDnrCtsHr6OzcoXKTaeH7JKhn2F0bEaUmr7W3S\niQDW/eK45LtnvkHF4HtZSuNXNIa80qoZPuYiqIreEJtywqqBQbiZvPuIvp8GGuj3\nn7PyAADBlSDwhFVKRoHq\n=BUYx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9e26add6069215cefb3e014266074067765547e4\nparent c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785355631 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785355631 -0400\n\nci(infra): refresh open release PRs after sibling merges (#5161)\n\n## The situation before\n\nThis repo releases ten packages independently, so it is normal to have\nseveral open release PRs at once. Those PRs all touch shared files —\nmost importantly `.release-please-manifest.json`. When one of them\nmerges, the others are instantly stale, and release-please is what\nnormally rewrites them.\n\nBut release commits deliberately skipped release-please entirely, for a\ngood reason: running it while a publish is mid-flight is dangerous.\nMerging a release PR bumps the manifest immediately, while the git tag\nis only created minutes later by `release.yml`. In that window\nrelease-please sees a version with no matching tag, concludes the\npackage was never released, and proposes resetting it to `0.1.0` with\nthe full history. That is not hypothetical — it happened once (`0.1.8` →\n`0.1.0`).\n\nSo the workflow chose the safe option: on a release commit, dispatch the\npublish and do nothing else.\n\n## Why that was a problem\n\n**Completing a publish does not push to `main`.** It creates a tag and a\nGitHub release, and neither re-triggers `release-please.yml`.\n\nSo after a release merge there was no follow-up run — ever. The\nremaining open release PRs stayed stale until some unrelated push\nhappened to land, which could be days. This made other release PRs sit\nwith merge conflicts \"forever\" on shared files.\n\n## What this changes\n\nPublishing still goes first and is never blocked. The difference is that\nthe *same run* now sticks around, waits for publishing to settle, and\nthen does the maintenance it used to skip:\n\n1. `detect-release-commit`\n2. `trigger-releases` — fires immediately, `needs` unchanged, still not\nblocked by anything\n3. `guard-pending-release` — new: also runs on release commits, after a\nsuccessful dispatch. Polls until no merged release PR is still labeled\n`autorelease: pending`\n4. `release-please` — runs only on an explicit `skip=false` from the\nguard\n5. `update-lockfiles` — unchanged\n\nNormal (non-release) pushes are unaffected: same wait, same fail-closed\nmaintenance gate as before.\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Why this ordering is safe</b></summary>\n\n**Publishing cannot be delayed by the wait.** `trigger-releases` depends\nonly on `detect-release-commit`, and the guard is deliberately outside\nthe `release-please` concurrency group — a poll of up to 45 minutes must\nnot hold the serialization slot other pushes queue on. Only step 4 is\nserialized, since release-please mutates shared release branches.\n\n**Maintenance requires a positive all-clear.** `release-please` runs\nonly on `skip == 'false'`. A guard that crashes, times out, or is\nskipped leaves that output unset, which blocks maintenance rather than\nletting it recompute against unverified state. `trigger-releases` is\nintentionally *not* in `release-please.needs`, so its skipped status on\nnormal pushes can't loosen that gate.\n\n**The wait is repo-wide by design.** It covers every pending release PR,\nnot just the merged one, because release-please recomputes *all*\ncomponents on every run — any single package sitting between \"version\nbumped\" and \"tag created\" is enough to trigger the downgrade above.\nScoping the wait to your own PR would not be safe.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Hardening added after review</b></summary>\n\nRouting release commits through the guard exposed three paths that\npreviously could not be reached, plus one latent bug:\n\n- **A release commit matching no package used to be a silent no-op.**\nThe package list is hardcoded in both `detect-release-commit` and\n`trigger-releases`. If a future package is wired into one but not the\nother, nothing publishes, nothing refreshes, and every job reports\nsuccess. The detector now fails loudly, and a config-derived test keeps\nthe two lists from drifting.\n- **The guard treated an unreadable API response as \"nothing pending.\"**\n`format_pending` swallowed its own parse failures, so a\nsuccessful-but-unparseable `gh` response was indistinguishable from an\nempty result — which would wave release-please through during exactly\nthe dangerous window. Parse failures now feed the existing\nretry/fail-closed path.\n- **A failed publish reddened two workflows.** Since the pending set is\nrepo-wide, a package left stuck days earlier would also fail an\nunrelated release that dispatched perfectly. Release commits now defer\nwith `skip=true` and a step summary naming the failed run, extending the\nmechanism hotfix pushes already used. Ordinary pushes still fail loudly,\nwhere a red guard is the only signal a human would see. Maintenance is\nskipped either way — this only changes red vs. green and whether the\nmessage is actionable.\n- **`git log` was unchecked**, so a failure would silently misclassify\nthe push and route a failed release down the wrong branch.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Cases that still need a later push</b></summary>\n\nThese are documented in `RELEASING.md` with the signal to look for and\nwhat to do:\n\n| Situation | Signal |\n| --- | --- |\n| Publish still in flight after 45 min | `release-please.yml` green,\n`deferred` step summary |\n| Publish failed (yours, or one stuck earlier) | `release.yml` red;\n`release-please.yml` green with a `deferred (release commit)` summary |\n| GitHub release state unreadable | `release-please.yml` **red** at\n`guard-pending-release` |\n| Several release PRs merged at once | Some `release-please` jobs show\n**cancelled** — expected; the surviving newest run recomputes every\ncomponent |\n\nCross-run sibling merges can still race around the pending-label window.\nThis intentionally does not add a hard global cross-run barrier.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Testing</b></summary>\n\n`.github/scripts/tests` passes (681 tests). The guard's `if:` condition\nis now pinned by a truth table over a small expression evaluator rather\nthan substring checks — mutation-tested against five broken variants\n(flattened parens, `||`↔`&&` swap, negated trigger check, `always()` for\n`!cancelled()`), all of which are caught and four of which passed the\nprevious assertions.\n\nAlso verified directly: every `run:` block passes `bash -n`;\n`format_pending` correctly separates \"empty\" from \"unreadable\" across\nsix payloads; and the guard's three exit paths behave as intended when\ndriven with stubbed `gh`/`git` (ordinary push → exit 1 with `skip`\nunset; release commit and hotfix → exit 0 with `skip=true`).\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T20:07:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/453838367aab3b64ff8275d1f98dcdb60eca6747/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368"}]},{"sha":"c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM5YzBjODNkNWUxMjY3OWQyN2VhMGMwMzQ2NDUwZWZhZTc4NDYzNjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T19:51:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T19:51:18Z"},"message":"fix(infra): harden release-notes draft model configuration (#5162)\n\nRelease-note drafting now rejects OpenAI Responses-API-only models up\nfront and raises the shared output-token ceiling so reasoning models can\nfinish large changelogs.\n\n---\n\n`RELEASE_BOT_MODEL` is an operator-facing Actions variable, so docs and\nthe helper need to stay honest about which models can actually work. The\ndrafter only calls Chat Completions, but `RELEASING.md` told people to\npick any JSON-Schema model — including OpenAI `*-pro` / `*codex*` IDs\nthat only work on Responses. That used to surface as a confusing HTTP\nfailure on the release PR.\n\nThe previous 4096 token cap is also too tight for reasoning models:\nOpenAI counts reasoning against `max_completion_tokens`, and Anthropic\nextended thinking has the same shape. `responseText()` already fails\nclosed on non-stop finishes, so large releases would post a failure\ncomment instead of truncating silently — still not what we want on the\nfirst big multi-package changelog.\n\nThis change:\n- rejects known Responses-only OpenAI names (mirroring\n`langchain-openai`'s prefix/`codex` check) with an error that names\n`RELEASE_BOT_MODEL`\n- raises one shared `MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` ceiling used by all three\nproviders\n- documents the Chat Completions constraint for operators\n\nOut of scope: implementing Responses API support.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8bb15b53f2865a2786db0562f5c738b867e06d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c8bb15b53f2865a2786db0562f5c738b867e06d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqalm2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATg0QAFERs/Ym1DSc86XkbZrFJZPS\nYfBBQ5jL1z7QBCuOaxC89ah/dgn26Bk4ZW5ZPQ0LMbGSIW58KKrZHJWzHUH/Ocsi\nsJ19TPiLfoH7f423H+JDnmw6PlDlpvLtRBWxR/UmVLM1sMEFwLoWKMcVrZFu8SrJ\n0v/fYeBMVhQsu6YOUkbbseDd8IBnrfX6SaDhO+5IUwKAzMtBpAnDA1eAmPIRMIKh\nbRC45i6f8mcmqZjF0X0v+PVEwgwUM+XckF94ACUDscTfIVZnLzfemrxMCI6WSD2i\nKllYM4czV24XgEgWO2GLSul+fNNsLf1oDfJWqPReAfzAjmjQ+6LgoaYuvh3KlQnr\nhWupPdm+pnlDXJFspyQOIUG9oKfj1vA1f0dypKbdbZGhBNRbsobvmFC9ZxfYdyLM\nrxo/s7kn91O8z6J60RH9UpWsmdCgGsB9JwWEiD0LVSLDtGvv9oHVs/hFN6q5diVU\nYrYA8ckbCEh/dMDQ+Qyv/pqJBA7OiTS/D2AVDyd+DGCDrtVXT+eanMmbW6vMe3KW\n+sN3Alkt2E5CWnr4UH81gpYRv+0HV8b2/NPUcCrk9DRYEcLbCeHxnJ0ayjfcnxvp\nlc1qnQ6wG+QFWfwX8vklcb+2ncrdlCO+OLeJAfGQnW6apFft1hqlm5ceAS34w9mf\n93E80pYMKh3A4XBsa0dg\n=Q5zB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c8bb15b53f2865a2786db0562f5c738b867e06d7\nparent 7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785354678 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785354678 -0400\n\nfix(infra): harden release-notes draft model configuration (#5162)\n\nRelease-note drafting now rejects OpenAI Responses-API-only models up\nfront and raises the shared output-token ceiling so reasoning models can\nfinish large changelogs.\n\n---\n\n`RELEASE_BOT_MODEL` is an operator-facing Actions variable, so docs and\nthe helper need to stay honest about which models can actually work. The\ndrafter only calls Chat Completions, but `RELEASING.md` told people to\npick any JSON-Schema model — including OpenAI `*-pro` / `*codex*` IDs\nthat only work on Responses. That used to surface as a confusing HTTP\nfailure on the release PR.\n\nThe previous 4096 token cap is also too tight for reasoning models:\nOpenAI counts reasoning against `max_completion_tokens`, and Anthropic\nextended thinking has the same shape. `responseText()` already fails\nclosed on non-stop finishes, so large releases would post a failure\ncomment instead of truncating silently — still not what we want on the\nfirst big multi-package changelog.\n\nThis change:\n- rejects known Responses-only OpenAI names (mirroring\n`langchain-openai`'s prefix/`codex` check) with an error that names\n`RELEASE_BOT_MODEL`\n- raises one shared `MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` ceiling used by all three\nproviders\n- documents the Chat Completions constraint for operators\n\nOut of scope: implementing Responses API support.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T19:51:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c9c0c83d5e12679d27ea0c0346450efae7846368/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01"}]},{"sha":"7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdkNGFjYjY4MDRjZDE3ZWI0YzIzMzdiOWFmMTFhZWU5ZjM2MDFkMDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T19:44:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T19:44:45Z"},"message":"fix(code): gate Hooks v2 behind `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` (#5146)\n\nHooks v2 now runs only when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` is enabled;\nlegacy hooks are unaffected.\n\n---\n\nHooks v2 is still in progress but already loads and runs user-authored\nhook commands in every session. `_load_runtime` is the only production\nsite that builds a `HooksRuntime`, so returning `None` there unless the\nexperimental flag is truthy leaves `HooksManager` inert — client\nlifecycle events no-op and transcripts are discarded — and\n`apply_hooks_context` strips the hook snapshot id and server-event gate\nfrom the graph context, which keeps `ServerHooksMiddleware` closed for\n`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, and subagent events. Legacy hooks\ndispatch through a separate path guarded by `has_handlers` checks, so\nthey keep firing exactly as before.\n\nGating at that single seam was preferred over per-call-site checks:\nevery other `HooksManager` construction already passes no runtime, so\none gate covers both the interactive and headless clients plus `reload`.\n\nTwo existing `TestLiveApprovalModeWrites` tests patch\n`HooksRuntime.create` as their session-construction probe, so they now\nenable the flag explicitly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `tests/unit_tests/hooks` (173), `test_app.py` (1341),\n`test_non_interactive.py` (116), Textual adapter + offload (290), agent\n/ tool-stream / legacy-hooks / local-context / server-helpers (468) all\npass.\n- New `test_hooks_v2_requires_experimental_flag` asserts\n`HooksManager.create(...).enabled` flips with the flag.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019faecf-b901-755b-abc4-e2c4f5e90726)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3fc4a69824afae632424b9dedfa4d313bdc21737","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3fc4a69824afae632424b9dedfa4d313bdc21737"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqalgtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM8wQAGk5wrkwCalMD2EKPkm2c8t5\n2LsQQX2aV9SDo0M7aSCbsyZDIQ2h7VzSsaDIF/a//hrOUjnRbyPCB/3mJMvb2Z4A\nuLziUk++ftqaNCaa37htfQufP8a5zLPozcH5WHixLuMHd1uH1DIrrm+ntC8HtdX2\nxvj7qZhpIIsEGeJVS+Fa6Ast8vk+Zj/BSOUuR4wwYr++TkRJAffQCezpEH8CGPKW\ntdPGoFzt+Fbumo99aG/1oOrvmvtfi0vNo7l9WO+irG+NjHIHN8zSS+vu2bLIsbQ/\ncDIE83zcw5CbbTIyamjHB8qTNLIYYo5iUiuxjiy/wNJCjeQhenuzL4P0mjH91/Vl\ngSUpnMXg2PMSgf50GAT9F/uwWbGPrU/eMJziQeCTf7YM3YfQ7R7KuH68YieWjn3o\nFqSoX2hNo56UvqGcDY6p1eqahabTL1HXKWFv53dO4M/cE8cmsrTYJlJlnGJ7Cljy\nbxnVMF8iLPVOD9oXlCcRuYxjRQh6vb9BfJ2BGpQywkq579o2371uSiq57eSfLMLc\n6EnfyniO0Dea7XQ5aEgkMtSxOoOc18sOHa07DgVN8zLYctz3+PazGKt4WzqWWfD0\n8vq6021ZdR2kn2UQcvIuK9cdiT7GsLvDQkrzGlswETnhZEDfElCqSkrvbWA/fniz\nHhH8y5BXvrSI4GPVFeUu\n=QpK1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3fc4a69824afae632424b9dedfa4d313bdc21737\nparent bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1785354285 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785354285 -0400\n\nfix(code): gate Hooks v2 behind `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` (#5146)\n\nHooks v2 now runs only when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL` is enabled;\nlegacy hooks are unaffected.\n\n---\n\nHooks v2 is still in progress but already loads and runs user-authored\nhook commands in every session. `_load_runtime` is the only production\nsite that builds a `HooksRuntime`, so returning `None` there unless the\nexperimental flag is truthy leaves `HooksManager` inert — client\nlifecycle events no-op and transcripts are discarded — and\n`apply_hooks_context` strips the hook snapshot id and server-event gate\nfrom the graph context, which keeps `ServerHooksMiddleware` closed for\n`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, and subagent events. Legacy hooks\ndispatch through a separate path guarded by `has_handlers` checks, so\nthey keep firing exactly as before.\n\nGating at that single seam was preferred over per-call-site checks:\nevery other `HooksManager` construction already passes no runtime, so\none gate covers both the interactive and headless clients plus `reload`.\n\nTwo existing `TestLiveApprovalModeWrites` tests patch\n`HooksRuntime.create` as their session-construction probe, so they now\nenable the flag explicitly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `tests/unit_tests/hooks` (173), `test_app.py` (1341),\n`test_non_interactive.py` (116), Textual adapter + offload (290), agent\n/ tool-stream / legacy-hooks / local-context / server-helpers (468) all\npass.\n- New `test_hooks_v2_requires_experimental_flag` asserts\n`HooksManager.create(...).enabled` flips with the flag.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/019faecf-b901-755b-abc4-e2c4f5e90726)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-29T19:44:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d4acb6804cd17eb4c2337b9af11aee9f3601d01/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a"}]},{"sha":"bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJiYTIxZjFlY2ExOGY0NWQxYzE1YTk4MDM4YjViYjcwOWI4NmZlNWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T19:04:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T19:04:19Z"},"message":"fix(infra): exempt release PRs from stale cleanup (#5145)\n\nRelease-please's PRs are no longer warned or auto-closed by the old-PR\ncleanup, and any existing `pending-deletion` label is removed from them\non the next run.\n\n---\n\nRelease-please keeps one long-lived PR per package and updates it in\nplace, so \"days since opened\" — the only staleness signal this workflow\nhas — is meaningless for them. #4297 was warned by this workflow on\n2026-07-29 at 33 days old and needed a manual `do-not-close` to survive.\nRequiring that label duplicates what release-please already maintains.\n\nA PR is exempt when it carries `release` or `autorelease: pending`\n**and** was opened by `github-actions[bot]` on a\n`release-please--branches--main--components--*` branch in this\nrepository. The label alone is not enough: `release` is derived from the\nPR title by the unified labeler, and `release` is an allowed title type,\nso a label-only check would let any contributor opt their own PR out of\ncleanup indefinitely. When a release label appears without matching\nprovenance, the run logs a warning — so genuine drift (a renamed default\nbranch, a `separate-pull-requests` flip, a token change) surfaces in the\nlog instead of silently closing release PRs again.\n\nThe stale-label sweep uses the same classification, so already-warned\nrelease PRs recover automatically. Draft and `do-not-close` behavior and\nthe age thresholds are unchanged. The run summary gains a\n`skippedRelease` sub-count so an over-applying exemption is visible at a\nglance.\n\nTwo pre-existing sweep bugs are fixed alongside, since this change\nroutes a new category of PR through it:\n\n- The sweep swallowed non-404 errors into a warning and returned a green\nrun, so a sweep that died on its first PR looked identical to one with\nnothing to do. It now fails the run, matching how a failed PR search is\nalready handled. **This can turn a currently-green run red if the sweep\nhas been quietly failing.**\n- `staleCleared` counted PRs whose label was already gone — the label\nsearch index lags the removals made earlier in the same run. Only real\nremovals are counted now, so the number may read lower than before.","tree":{"sha":"dbf54b5f91ed41cdb4d322798d248804e2d10455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dbf54b5f91ed41cdb4d322798d248804e2d10455"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqak6zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4HcQACucrDOxmveSpXNnds9mGhAB\nOEkN4yavgtb/4c2F1ZaSoHzIHe8EXDD1udceLK5oE9niT/pEw+x3Qu1Iu6HG+MAS\nbgViTRhY/319b1N3ocMnkcYzo21aL3hfNovRzuuuXmH8W33WsttBff/MbDQfN7GV\n5ltArIOuiRiuCpD15ejbXBeYJbKmYUSYewR93bV6XbKrl2qhUZwfPlvSeFthcLJo\nMzUqjWk/IPvIh0lJq+omM7yzyafTfibtbbcj/5mm84s6g7nIAGU0axfuhXibNwhO\neE4Y86/eYwWBF1N7gnEGg4PeWvvOZOsNLIbnnqlwnDSVSR/lssJc7UD6GAbG+Alh\nza2WE+VulUiRLrcIu3iD06A+Xpub/71hzSnnk3S8UpXH/uI5KILUgVUzX5y5VfS8\nbgyYPmzhcU0yU2At4Wnktc74irHWjuAiO7+JJpRxKxDkMjQl3LUSJ0d30JyUCj9W\nM3lCyv5oFlFmwega4drxWayFIHtdIjOUmI0X+mU0AJmz/R6rayGyZfJU5Jr0ww+B\ndKWkanOkPFe7jf2cwC7uzBNO01M0Q9U2ht8L08YVxqDQSeIaOMwV7rvwQL1NNW3s\nvbxOe3a9DI/MAXf4FJNsnFE2VtPNhImbvdLmFmHPiIOurUqIOFrJmXLLDBamZ0sl\neJUTSl82GZK+2uvbVxH4\n=xaQL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dbf54b5f91ed41cdb4d322798d248804e2d10455\nparent 249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785351859 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785351859 -0400\n\nfix(infra): exempt release PRs from stale cleanup (#5145)\n\nRelease-please's PRs are no longer warned or auto-closed by the old-PR\ncleanup, and any existing `pending-deletion` label is removed from them\non the next run.\n\n---\n\nRelease-please keeps one long-lived PR per package and updates it in\nplace, so \"days since opened\" — the only staleness signal this workflow\nhas — is meaningless for them. #4297 was warned by this workflow on\n2026-07-29 at 33 days old and needed a manual `do-not-close` to survive.\nRequiring that label duplicates what release-please already maintains.\n\nA PR is exempt when it carries `release` or `autorelease: pending`\n**and** was opened by `github-actions[bot]` on a\n`release-please--branches--main--components--*` branch in this\nrepository. The label alone is not enough: `release` is derived from the\nPR title by the unified labeler, and `release` is an allowed title type,\nso a label-only check would let any contributor opt their own PR out of\ncleanup indefinitely. When a release label appears without matching\nprovenance, the run logs a warning — so genuine drift (a renamed default\nbranch, a `separate-pull-requests` flip, a token change) surfaces in the\nlog instead of silently closing release PRs again.\n\nThe stale-label sweep uses the same classification, so already-warned\nrelease PRs recover automatically. Draft and `do-not-close` behavior and\nthe age thresholds are unchanged. The run summary gains a\n`skippedRelease` sub-count so an over-applying exemption is visible at a\nglance.\n\nTwo pre-existing sweep bugs are fixed alongside, since this change\nroutes a new category of PR through it:\n\n- The sweep swallowed non-404 errors into a warning and returned a green\nrun, so a sweep that died on its first PR looked identical to one with\nnothing to do. It now fails the run, matching how a failed PR search is\nalready handled. **This can turn a currently-green run red if the sweep\nhas been quietly failing.**\n- `staleCleared` counted PRs whose label was already gone — the label\nsearch index lags the removals made earlier in the same run. Only real\nremovals are counted now, so the number may read lower than before.","verified_at":"2026-07-29T19:04:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bba21f1eca18f45d1c15a98038b5bb709b86fe5a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d"}]},{"sha":"249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI0OTEyMWM1ODQzMDYwODgxZDJkMGZmNDY0NWYxMzIxMTA5Yjc0OGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T18:46:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T18:46:26Z"},"message":"ci(infra): require the release-notes helper by its current path (#5160)\n\nFollow-up to #5159.\n\n---\n\nThe curated release-notes check resolved its helper through a list of\ncandidate paths, trying the current filename first and falling back to\nthe pre-rename ones. That existed for a single reason: this workflow\ntakes its YAML from the pull request but checks the helper itself out of\n`main`, so during #5159 the new filename did not exist on `main` yet —\nand that PR needed this required check to pass. The fallback bridged\nexactly one merge.\n\n`main` now carries the helper at its current path and neither old path\nexists anywhere, so those entries are unreachable. This replaces the\ncandidate list with a direct `require`, and leaves a comment explaining\nwhy a future rename will need the same temporary fallback — the trap is\nnot obvious from reading the workflow.\n\nThe test that pinned the fallback ordering is replaced with a stronger\ninvariant: every helper script either workflow loads out of its\n`trusted-source` checkout must exist in the repository. A wrong path\nthere is invisible to YAML linting and only surfaces when the workflow\nruns, which in the check workflow means a broken required check. The new\nassertion covers both the automation and check workflows, and both the\n`require` and `run:` call sites.","tree":{"sha":"15d561d5a67ab5c7909a1fc12434d25ca0457205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/15d561d5a67ab5c7909a1fc12434d25ca0457205"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqakqCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx4MQAHBGv/hG0PTLGAqjwmLNvl9d\nYdOvPcVwsdAqyUkAAQcxKIf69gAOHgjEF93/bFkfa6hZ3ysJJxc9LirxK2Tr++9u\nHsIlsf2dmiajMipAFdlymr6mlNpBxlJuagdBvJ01ROPgabgDCJytY5HaaG4eJARY\nPtDsFOepALsbGdn6lWPPCHW9xls9DnEk6T7i6LU0DSVpfEx1XRKINrS6odGLs46x\nX9IJK9PDDYXAy7vGXx81WFbJ3WPG/7zWYAOpzqmnle1Ev2OTSQ1ytgVw93jW4aE5\nhE3snESA15iKN3h8/+CyNrt9W8OozKb3YGBf3Yndh/jG3c9RpjbutgDI+uSrI8ev\nIho3bqJuj7WFavCh2kjLEqG6xfk362TdkQ8UkYfEpaUheVLU9r05ELP5Uab/Xnbo\nNT0WhESgYgI6DGCeuH7raHLyWrwzFJ043OyLDKAgHyOA9OGMwbbgFmiZk3YdtfSb\nUFuzRs9qnwHiwzlaUlRUBET8Kn5LWIf3D1UQkMCtFMo7XVpMbtaEXRYqYNCjwnid\nb6rrk3DBuPDTdLdPn4ouOaHPlZJYvv9G9ha/8RLUOW2pAlEXUlZPl6AmApFTLS96\noYqrHpMhI/mmBUwbVoJ4Y5k9UqESocZ2T+xwW1ArIGuTlWd/Gp6ci0spd7bYlrE8\nF99dPMyzeqiOoAq7VZzg\n=jwVS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 15d561d5a67ab5c7909a1fc12434d25ca0457205\nparent 8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785350786 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785350786 -0400\n\nci(infra): require the release-notes helper by its current path (#5160)\n\nFollow-up to #5159.\n\n---\n\nThe curated release-notes check resolved its helper through a list of\ncandidate paths, trying the current filename first and falling back to\nthe pre-rename ones. That existed for a single reason: this workflow\ntakes its YAML from the pull request but checks the helper itself out of\n`main`, so during #5159 the new filename did not exist on `main` yet —\nand that PR needed this required check to pass. The fallback bridged\nexactly one merge.\n\n`main` now carries the helper at its current path and neither old path\nexists anywhere, so those entries are unreachable. This replaces the\ncandidate list with a direct `require`, and leaves a comment explaining\nwhy a future rename will need the same temporary fallback — the trap is\nnot obvious from reading the workflow.\n\nThe test that pinned the fallback ordering is replaced with a stronger\ninvariant: every helper script either workflow loads out of its\n`trusted-source` checkout must exist in the repository. A wrong path\nthere is invisible to YAML linting and only surfaces when the workflow\nruns, which in the check workflow means a broken required check. The new\nassertion covers both the automation and check workflows, and both the\n`require` and `run:` call sites.","verified_at":"2026-07-29T18:46:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/249121c5843060881d2d0ff4645f1321109b748d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff"}]},{"sha":"8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgzMzdlMzM4MTgzYTQ0ZDBmNDgzMjRkMzBiOTkyZjEwOGQ2YWQyZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-29T18:40:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-29T18:40:20Z"},"message":"ci(infra): generalize curated release notes to all packages (#5159)\n\nCurated release notes now cover every release-please package, not just\n`deepagents-code`.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the release-notes bot and its check gate were hard-coded to\ndcode. Every other package either skipped curation entirely or required\nhand-editing `CHANGELOG.md` plus the PR body and redoing that work after\neach release-please sync.\n\n`@release-bot` now targets whichever package a release PR is for. The\ncomponent is read from the release-please head branch and validated\nagainst `release-please-config.json`, so a package added to that config\nis covered without touching a workflow. On a fanout release each\npackage's PR is drafted and applied on its own.\n\nBecause the changelog path and branch ref are now derived from a head\nref instead of being constants, the component has to resolve to a real\nentry in `release-please-config.json` before any path is built, the\nbranch and the PR title must name the same component, and the apply step\nre-derives its write target from the config rather than trusting the\nstate it was handed. A PR retargeted to a different package part-way\nthrough apply is rejected instead of receiving another package's notes.\n\n### What operators will notice\n\n- The command mention is `@release-bot draft` / `@release-bot apply`\n(was `@dcode-release-bot`).\n- The workflows are `release_notes.yml` and `release_notes_check.yml`.\n- The `curated release notes` required check keeps its name, so branch\nprotection needs no edit.\n- Curation now applies to the partner packages as well, including\nreleases that only bump a dependency. That is a real increase in\nper-release work for those packages; `release: dangerously skip curated\nnotes` still ships a package with the generated changelog as-is.","tree":{"sha":"b58e379abf3dafae7622841f83dcbc0cfd9a2832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b58e379abf3dafae7622841f83dcbc0cfd9a2832"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqakkUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATLIQACRx+EnKgubFIW1tSKK5qg06\natI8PoPSCZ6Udpg4jbLNxfh5iY6bF9mXYsCcQF4xiChqxBcbis6NcpBWmQ6SH/E7\nHULsXWxmdhe4ouOqeA8wZGdWokl0TYWD9tBXq1BQWSEaguL0XeTKZbEyMCYm6gkb\nc+e3NxMGYPhpbxx2GLXZObjdzTyOmLWrsft1s3JsAn3NFXTQI22jIbXa4pEIVwI9\ne82+i8VGVLxkJBuocSxi7JFUAYEjqzH3TYfJTJ2Mq/q/sMedeF4rIjZ4HoNXhXMX\nmSGCJT/SymVh5zg+3xpVKwxbtWO7z+rycU22WydMBWy9/oW6GnR5K0iop8cDkn9k\n1KTXTQf5X3hmRxdtfnkugHJ/uCduMMRYqb1tuc/wUZ1BVxN32ZYGb+1v8dhh46g+\n9DidK7s4cYM+jpUzgiHvGjAnNodLESwGCgOY2u7oXztg1Ma/sY/4pHbap33pCU99\niOKDdfiu8IMp0s0M6uwCuXTGrs5R5nFAS6bZFaxmEKJs7rUA3ARed1T1c9dpx7ue\nmW05BglY8aYTlxJJpkpQYhmYL8tuocDdZd6xfD7npEtm55fs1n0h/ehT3/j2vWeg\nkhAWZejODInN595BMBW1hIRfVaP8LhrEEwyEiKGwCL3KzEsKO36FEoltWNdn7t41\nhw7eYbsrHGXit2557jlo\n=uU0V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b58e379abf3dafae7622841f83dcbc0cfd9a2832\nparent a559f720d94eb8e7d14f96dbdad816dc9f7e3636\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785350420 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785350420 -0400\n\nci(infra): generalize curated release notes to all packages (#5159)\n\nCurated release notes now cover every release-please package, not just\n`deepagents-code`.\n\n---\n\nPreviously the release-notes bot and its check gate were hard-coded to\ndcode. Every other package either skipped curation entirely or required\nhand-editing `CHANGELOG.md` plus the PR body and redoing that work after\neach release-please sync.\n\n`@release-bot` now targets whichever package a release PR is for. The\ncomponent is read from the release-please head branch and validated\nagainst `release-please-config.json`, so a package added to that config\nis covered without touching a workflow. On a fanout release each\npackage's PR is drafted and applied on its own.\n\nBecause the changelog path and branch ref are now derived from a head\nref instead of being constants, the component has to resolve to a real\nentry in `release-please-config.json` before any path is built, the\nbranch and the PR title must name the same component, and the apply step\nre-derives its write target from the config rather than trusting the\nstate it was handed. A PR retargeted to a different package part-way\nthrough apply is rejected instead of receiving another package's notes.\n\n### What operators will notice\n\n- The command mention is `@release-bot draft` / `@release-bot apply`\n(was `@dcode-release-bot`).\n- The workflows are `release_notes.yml` and `release_notes_check.yml`.\n- The `curated release notes` required check keeps its name, so branch\nprotection needs no edit.\n- Curation now applies to the partner packages as well, including\nreleases that only bump a dependency. That is a real increase in\nper-release work for those packages; `release: dangerously skip curated\nnotes` still ships a package with the generated changelog as-is.","verified_at":"2026-07-29T18:40:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8337e338183a44d0f48324d30b992f108d6ad2ff/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/e