lwB\nyu5uzqD6CnLiyWQsKU8KFFAhBbogd87eQe5e7QCxR4v5kqnA9YZsFrpLdl2ZcVSf\nMBuvXvfa8S6tLtRdGgw+pGpHaFIAXitAyT9ZK1cz3bHBOXV0cqvn66HasyZZK14p\nsUgns0Z8Yk59OEdKCm0kwSu50qpRMtqBiRFB6llkiLfknE+5sueda4MUXcHpLi/u\nUkvO2FbhYSQZutUCICTQPCdzTz4+2NuD0Cc3DjhZkdudxZQICNd8H+Umk7es7ktt\nbS6d5gcD1IOr4dl7k5rq57rI8JKi8XQhwtLtd0+VLCAEb/juUw69Z4bKVtYI4YOP\nylGtBU27kk3AwlNc/nhTalWK4OD417bA4QED1cLw97ESEUiiORkkLyufzYI//dGi\neqK/c6htK7EjYQL532PE\n=Dn2w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 180482927d251c0976ddaf949a428d43748c5b62\nparent da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1785266886 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785266886 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump uv to 0.12.0 (#5128)\n\nBumps the uv pin in `.github/actions/uv_setup/action.yml` from `0.11.31`\nto [`0.12.0`](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/tag/0.12.0).\n\nOpened automatically by `bump_uv_pin.yml`. Mirror availability on\n`releases.astral.sh` was verified before this PR was created, so CI\nshould not race the fallback.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T19:28:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b43113d941550128ccdf3c7baa250570fb7af93","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2b43113d941550128ccdf3c7baa250570fb7af93","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2b43113d941550128ccdf3c7baa250570fb7af93/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d"}]},{"sha":"da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRhOGQ0YzNjY2MyMzdlNTcyOTQwODhkMjQzN2IxMzAzMWE3M2M1MmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-28T19:17:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T19:17:49Z"},"message":"fix(code): toast when media is dropped into a free-text question (#5099)\n\nDragging an image or video into a text-only prompt now shows a toast\nthat only text is supported, instead of pasting the file path.\n\n---\n\n### The problem\n\nWhen the agent asks you a question, you answer in a small text box that\nonly accepts text — you can't attach a picture to it the way you can in\nthe main chat input. But nothing stopped you from *trying*. Drag an\nimage onto that box and the terminal hands over the file's location as a\nline of text, which just got typed in for you, so you'd end up answering\nthe question with something like `/Users/you/Desktop/shot.png`. Easy to\nmiss, and the agent never sees the image.\n\nNow you get a warning toast saying only text is supported, and the path\nisn't inserted.\n\n### How it works\n\nTerminals don't have a real \"you dropped a file here\" signal — a drag\njust arrives as ordinary pasted text. The main chat input already deals\nwith this: it takes whatever was pasted, checks whether it points at a\nfile that actually exists on disk, and treats it as an attachment if so.\nThis change reuses that same check for the question box, and rejects\ninstead of attaching.\n\nThree small pieces:\n\n- `is_media_path` decides whether a file is an image or video, just by\nlooking at its extension. No reading the file.\n- `dropped_payload_paths` takes pasted text and returns any real files\nit points at. It first does a quick check that the text even *looks*\nlike a dropped file — a dragged file always arrives as a full path\n(`/Users/...`, `C:\\...`, `file://...`), so anything else is treated as\nordinary typing and left alone. That quick check is deliberately cheap\nso that normal typing never triggers the slower \"does this file exist?\"\nlookup, which involves hitting the disk.\n- The question box watches for both ways a paste can arrive (terminals\nsend it either as one chunk or as a rapid burst of fake keystrokes), and\nshows the toast instead of inserting when it sees media.\n\n### Worth knowing\n\n- This applies to both places the agent asks for free text: `ask_user`\nquestions and goal review.\n- Since a drag is indistinguishable from a normal paste, this also\nblocks pasting an image path as your actual answer. If you genuinely\nwant to talk about a file, add a word after it (`/path/to/shot.png what\nis this?`) and it inserts normally.\n- If you drop several files at once and any of them is an image, none\nare inserted — a half-filled answer would be more confusing than an\nempty one. The toast lists each file so it's clear what was dropped, and\nshows full paths if two files happen to share a name.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f462f4d6-b647-5e72-aca2-158f41dcc95f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6709170892e17e5e5bed06077ee2e62c445524b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d6709170892e17e5e5bed06077ee2e62c445524b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaQBdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMc8QAGb8SsAoFh75Zk7pdHbyLX/H\n7uj3i43im3l7GEYFg0a82KY8OGPrMH99vmBok1M4nB4zDjCKXiR86/r9E3ZPsuGM\nsRTL+NlqD6w1QdpqCdC+l52bqA+BmADBYXrWHxDMXgP49BTesguzUlYT8xaIHrmi\nVjiBmXgdI8UTVZuhx+/RXajMpNGUdU5tvszj/SiNrsB82GuTCsFrQ0fjc/2gry5m\ngUQ2o5WzQe+QnwiLPmlN4Ay2+M1hiwUJZuPPPzkEF302OWBjKDjmpZ8oPjLosWr8\nYdphWd9oVSlHCM0VH6hCbKdADmyUBxbPW2U2zScLK97cmVCqeeyZjq+d9+ouGbby\nZ9AOrCPT/WQ3yeLfgHBEjBcl/oeAoyCqqcg1iRGjjWQ7TqFWM+3yElZHRD0Bmtr9\n1fZ3Kqe2LOYzB93+MvgkO8Md1Jz7CHczHMxBxCPUeqVa4z5LG0IYP/LLy/P5lsdz\nvMDQyvpdhvoum1J7Zj5DHEwlxX8URZwsfIjrOXW7X470a9BHuwi3zWUFCKyGO1rH\nBXa59VKQOmr15h/a0amvCjqUr80uja4XUxiXGmE/uqFjQF78HV6m4QRq8yHvdcXG\n8KQ8iIImcOB9eoTFiEHX1NPUKvx3Z9lNsY1y7MFgVuTRPK2w9o8a9d62xajCsWoz\nkBn4RmwnXUmgMXRG6sgN\n=sU0z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d6709170892e17e5e5bed06077ee2e62c445524b\nparent 18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785266269 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785266269 -0400\n\nfix(code): toast when media is dropped into a free-text question (#5099)\n\nDragging an image or video into a text-only prompt now shows a toast\nthat only text is supported, instead of pasting the file path.\n\n---\n\n### The problem\n\nWhen the agent asks you a question, you answer in a small text box that\nonly accepts text — you can't attach a picture to it the way you can in\nthe main chat input. But nothing stopped you from *trying*. Drag an\nimage onto that box and the terminal hands over the file's location as a\nline of text, which just got typed in for you, so you'd end up answering\nthe question with something like `/Users/you/Desktop/shot.png`. Easy to\nmiss, and the agent never sees the image.\n\nNow you get a warning toast saying only text is supported, and the path\nisn't inserted.\n\n### How it works\n\nTerminals don't have a real \"you dropped a file here\" signal — a drag\njust arrives as ordinary pasted text. The main chat input already deals\nwith this: it takes whatever was pasted, checks whether it points at a\nfile that actually exists on disk, and treats it as an attachment if so.\nThis change reuses that same check for the question box, and rejects\ninstead of attaching.\n\nThree small pieces:\n\n- `is_media_path` decides whether a file is an image or video, just by\nlooking at its extension. No reading the file.\n- `dropped_payload_paths` takes pasted text and returns any real files\nit points at. It first does a quick check that the text even *looks*\nlike a dropped file — a dragged file always arrives as a full path\n(`/Users/...`, `C:\\...`, `file://...`), so anything else is treated as\nordinary typing and left alone. That quick check is deliberately cheap\nso that normal typing never triggers the slower \"does this file exist?\"\nlookup, which involves hitting the disk.\n- The question box watches for both ways a paste can arrive (terminals\nsend it either as one chunk or as a rapid burst of fake keystrokes), and\nshows the toast instead of inserting when it sees media.\n\n### Worth knowing\n\n- This applies to both places the agent asks for free text: `ask_user`\nquestions and goal review.\n- Since a drag is indistinguishable from a normal paste, this also\nblocks pasting an image path as your actual answer. If you genuinely\nwant to talk about a file, add a word after it (`/path/to/shot.png what\nis this?`) and it inserts normally.\n- If you drop several files at once and any of them is an image, none\nare inserted — a half-filled answer would be more confusing than an\nempty one. The toast lists each file so it's clear what was dropped, and\nshows full paths if two files happen to share a name.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f462f4d6-b647-5e72-aca2-158f41dcc95f)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T19:17:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/da8d4c3ccc237e57294088d2437b13031a73c52d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a"}]},{"sha":"18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE4ODIyYjI5MGE3MGY2ZGVkY2EzM2Q2MTk2ZmE1MWRjOGE3MDVkOWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-28T19:04:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T19:04:56Z"},"message":"chore(infra): nest GitHub helper scripts by domain (#5126)\n\nNest GitHub helper scripts into domain folders (`checks`, `evals`,\n`labeling`, `release`, `tests`) and update workflow, pre-commit,\nMakefile, and doc path references.\n\nThis is a structure-only cleanup: runtime behavior is unchanged.\nHelper-script CI path is now `pytest .github/scripts/tests`.\n\n---\n\nWorkflows stay flat under `.github/workflows/` (GitHub only discovers\ntop-level workflow files). Production helpers are grouped by domain;\ncoupled modules stay together (for example `check_dep_freshness` with\n`check_release_deps`).","tree":{"sha":"ff656a5084dda9b130df053e2946d2bd683b0dd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ff656a5084dda9b130df053e2946d2bd683b0dd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaP1YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8egQAE/qO+KlytzReWyv9psTZQyL\nwJ3eu5uajqS0wNro6oa+GdiXH6Go4Yvz/jyU3sa0yCDKST+MKU4HK1gJ3WI1Gt04\nNARr++Rl7Fww7EmxDpj9SLnQtcw0hTs00X38cmG9P79hV61tBu9v8+K7Hm5O2jiN\ni32tnaeoVeBnHToBk8LgIDY2p5EvIXMUnQR/Xmi7HfKIux6KSaKP4Lid01N5O93O\nri/zTIwHvaqWeUDjAhhTOH+dxk5JJPwC+0Gub9CMeBNg3yNcihUzzSezpMuaMYpe\nAT37hsYbLsfiR/I6y1FtDT3fODpSyewosdyFXfwQ4resjK7Xo5zZar72ndLhPqeu\nVS8FWfSM+8Xbk3i3v1PEvVPqFyD+6iLHWneOR5edmQHkAJwP7dHYDAz6MRHaWaeG\niksXqC29/H57xrza35kaWU6pUqG6o8qihtm9gOI6HijZnm3n/Aj2NXowuF6rePqM\nxuDTGukLkket4/no5ar5xEXpoWSgqiplLTJyFrBCqKIyb19VmkBrEc4q4CGOPIu+\noP94mQy8Em0Bad7so/M6BfyjD4M+LKC+FlvRjSDJHe2E0CN6YytAZNbfWr+RHxcS\n5uxCruOJcKDbrOBWP/AI9n3aWGTkV8WIXCzZeVDGHKaqNBP+W9o1MI7I9GsgB96J\nl+qT3+dmjNE9xJGkNkWM\n=JE7V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ff656a5084dda9b130df053e2946d2bd683b0dd5\nparent 5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785265496 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785265496 -0400\n\nchore(infra): nest GitHub helper scripts by domain (#5126)\n\nNest GitHub helper scripts into domain folders (`checks`, `evals`,\n`labeling`, `release`, `tests`) and update workflow, pre-commit,\nMakefile, and doc path references.\n\nThis is a structure-only cleanup: runtime behavior is unchanged.\nHelper-script CI path is now `pytest .github/scripts/tests`.\n\n---\n\nWorkflows stay flat under `.github/workflows/` (GitHub only discovers\ntop-level workflow files). Production helpers are grouped by domain;\ncoupled modules stay together (for example `check_dep_freshness` with\n`check_release_deps`).","verified_at":"2026-07-28T19:04:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18822b290a70f6dedca33d6196fa51dc8a705d9a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa"}]},{"sha":"5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViNTgzODFiNGI1YmVmZjRjZjRiMTlkNzRhMjA0NjlkMzhhMGRhYWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-28T18:32:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T18:32:40Z"},"message":"style(code): document `Enter` toggle in `/notifications` footer (#5125)\n\nThe `/notifications` settings modal footer advertised `Space toggle`,\nbut Enter toggles the focused warning too — Textual's `ToggleButton`\nbinds `enter,space` to its toggle action. The hint now reads\n`Space/Enter toggle` so the advertised keys match real behavior.\n\n---\n\nAdded coverage pins both the Enter keypress path (via `pilot`) and the\nfooter text, so a future screen-level `enter` binding on\n`NotificationSettingsScreen` can't silently steal the toggle key without\na failing test.\n\nAdding an Enter-to-close binding here was considered and rejected: every\n`enter` binding in the TUI means *activate/confirm the highlighted item*\nand `escape` means *close* — no modal closes on Enter, and the sibling\nnotification center and detail modals both use Enter to drill in. A\npriority Enter-to-close would also have silently removed the working\ntoggle key.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c41fc23f-fbb9-6978-fcc3-eb95fc6d203f)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c97fe068c11f41184039615d689abe169589de9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4c97fe068c11f41184039615d689abe169589de9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaPXICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYxQQAKN/BYRq2hhw04ZRjEqQN9wV\nY38ogLt4IEFmNpuJLqLN63j5uZhf3SPj/BPAU1FRWhLu8+xcZm11/Lj6xWHKZCQ3\njGDB7K5VrdPB/l1lVDVl2QivhRAGD6KMmId/fEglsLVdZdQUt6ARFmrdVptlstND\noPTbL5Vcs0tRG/0+85MM6uz2QVNlWs7PnBxXPVqMa/TmrGRDmwkIGBNJWzvs+/HO\n+rZiUkndv0X/GE7QCW4fr1s4xqIJ4ub8FXVDkNGwVMyPOu+9aOmH1Cpx+lnRdw2+\nLDir7SS4ZHXiPITKstZhaBoW5EyqnjtIpgFUITjlDAU1szYcjwhfD2VZPK4pjviZ\ng/PF5uk1RO1WjoaX7OdBDuYJ4jbnaIzKuT4B7yD/FpbbF+yE5rHUpbNOBvXtiy80\nqch2eqa+zEdmT+Q1IG2DqedmG/7qrtE9fiy1zRITTIpQTPKivPpi3YaG5aDTNmj2\nX1Qa1At6DA+HCVFHvQr6oGVRCDsoTNNSFypUBDE9doSttbCv5QTEB7Ge8L64qhda\nqCxkBoIoiM1DC2O/s1qapSiGkJ5bL8NyPzeGXIpLQ0sYkiIhpGBGXmT10gJkwIY1\npKenOaSQ5z2qxMF3RZ1LKOxPVRUIEDaS1UAKwvqbtFmWjj0YIANCu/w9Y3zotY1C\nIdod47cRtggxv4wIwYbz\n=o589\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4c97fe068c11f41184039615d689abe169589de9\nparent 04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785263560 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785263560 -0400\n\nstyle(code): document `Enter` toggle in `/notifications` footer (#5125)\n\nThe `/notifications` settings modal footer advertised `Space toggle`,\nbut Enter toggles the focused warning too — Textual's `ToggleButton`\nbinds `enter,space` to its toggle action. The hint now reads\n`Space/Enter toggle` so the advertised keys match real behavior.\n\n---\n\nAdded coverage pins both the Enter keypress path (via `pilot`) and the\nfooter text, so a future screen-level `enter` binding on\n`NotificationSettingsScreen` can't silently steal the toggle key without\na failing test.\n\nAdding an Enter-to-close binding here was considered and rejected: every\n`enter` binding in the TUI means *activate/confirm the highlighted item*\nand `escape` means *close* — no modal closes on Enter, and the sibling\nnotification center and detail modals both use Enter to drill in. A\npriority Enter-to-close would also have silently removed the working\ntoggle key.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c41fc23f-fbb9-6978-fcc3-eb95fc6d203f)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T18:32:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b58381b4b5beff4cf4b19d74a20469d38a0daaa/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70"}]},{"sha":"04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA0Y2YyNWQyNzA2ODA3MDk3OTU1MmE1YzkxNGZjN2RhZDcxNWNlNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-28T18:31:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-28T18:31:32Z"},"message":"feat(code): show thread message count in the Debug Console (#5117)\n\nThe Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) now reports how many messages the current\nthread holds, alongside how many are currently rendered.\n\n---\n\nThe snapshot already showed the thread id, but nothing about the\nthread's size, so gauging how long a conversation had grown meant\nscrolling the transcript.\n\nThe new `Messages` row reads `MessageStore`, which is cleared on every\nthread switch/reset and is therefore already scoped to the current\nthread. That keeps the snapshot path free of checkpoint I/O — it stays a\nsynchronous, in-memory capture, which matters because the console is a\ndiagnostic that must open even when subsystems are misbehaving. The\ncount is built through the same `_safe` wrapper as the other rows, so a\nfailure degrades to `(unavailable: ...)` rather than aborting the\noverlay.\n\nThe mounted-window count rides along in parentheses (`42 (20 rendered)`)\nso transcript virtualization state is visible in the same place — useful\nwhen debugging windowing or pruning behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/02500a4c-1046-dc3b-3b1a-3a8cfe42b307)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4a2afa15e4359abb5d0d24b3afa0e5e1cf8970f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e4a2afa15e4359abb5d0d24b3afa0e5e1cf8970f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaPWECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmwUQACx6IrGcfYqsnCHrT0XZ76uo\nE/Ag5zV0VbR+9em19lVYd2SlAeMXbBPoiJ6vlZD84F66fG7hi09sxS70XHD6EjHW\nyAWz2hgI9WLZ6d5KI44fpf8n4G6cqo3WcocTb3hlipjuQd2HcUbxcdquXkPvq679\nSMGti891jEWPfupWZhK7p5fPcuSkRsE5Ubqewgge4Q/D5BSw6cKGu7BGA1pNGjqW\nBEpdmtGcrl86CgbRQGu0x4FMtIqKNVA9pICyuKy9aZUOzf/GBV4dXT5QXW6/EhG0\ncPyGTYtBfVBes0UcN69Gstxuz0TiS5KhUTDGQl0E2ZwSIvw87afkVU9UqWKQkxqP\nNpGlPxxkGU1bV4JueLXJwYknbSO5ekCsudeRZuNSGU08uP87v+FmIZJyYDi18N4J\n6d2c+UCGFwm7CSXMYgxH+ObWfmIIcxkSvOqRycmdKF86YzGTUAqlLMwDFNv0T4nH\nFpjybglXbUUyIuGKC0WSe3yLqTQGM3asoFm0Q45GzBfK9bc8lMhYCdO92qZ/dhoc\n1rARRFI0vc/a5wKcWjln8eQv3R4U0XNMp2aTLQPk5uNIcsLJH9LMAEog1M31TuQU\nnGEuacobyctbW0s5+y5KvXjSaUcbonEMLgba6IgG6uzPu0to5H3RPerybI+WnpYq\nQdqb5MxIAegb6objEXaT\n=G6TV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e4a2afa15e4359abb5d0d24b3afa0e5e1cf8970f\nparent 53e55247dad4dc9002f058d9cb69770392ccf900\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785263492 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785263492 -0400\n\nfeat(code): show thread message count in the Debug Console (#5117)\n\nThe Debug Console (`Ctrl+\\`) now reports how many messages the current\nthread holds, alongside how many are currently rendered.\n\n---\n\nThe snapshot already showed the thread id, but nothing about the\nthread's size, so gauging how long a conversation had grown meant\nscrolling the transcript.\n\nThe new `Messages` row reads `MessageStore`, which is cleared on every\nthread switch/reset and is therefore already scoped to the current\nthread. That keeps the snapshot path free of checkpoint I/O — it stays a\nsynchronous, in-memory capture, which matters because the console is a\ndiagnostic that must open even when subsystems are misbehaving. The\ncount is built through the same `_safe` wrapper as the other rows, so a\nfailure degrades to `(unavailable: ...)` rather than aborting the\noverlay.\n\nThe mounted-window count rides along in parentheses (`42 (20 rendered)`)\nso transcript virtualization state is visible in the same place — useful\nwhen debugging windowing or pruning behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/02500a4c-1046-dc3b-3b1a-3a8cfe42b307)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-28T18:31:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/04cf25d27068070979552a5c914fc7dad715ce70/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"htt