"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad"}]},{"sha":"f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYxNzI3Yzc4NWM0NDgwOWU3YjFiN2VkOGM1ZDBiMzFjNTYwYWUzYWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T23:52:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T23:52:45Z"},"message":"fix(code): anchor toasts above the chat input (#5101)\n\nToasts no longer cover the chat input — they now float directly above\nthe input box.\n\n---\n\nTextual docks its `ToastRack` to the bottom of the screen, which puts\nevery toast on top of the composer the user is typing into. Rather than\nrestyling individual toasts, the app now tracks the bottom chrome\n(subagent panel, startup tip, goal status, chat input, and status bar)\nand widens the rack's bottom margin so the stack ends exactly at the top\nedge of that chrome.\n\nThe bottom container announces its own resizes, so the anchor follows\nthe chat input as it grows with a multi-line message and as the bottom\npanels come and go; terminal resizes re-anchor too. On a terminal too\nshort to fit both, the offset is clamped so a toast is never pushed off\nscreen. Modal screens compose their own rack and are deliberately left\nalone.\n\nWorth a careful look: the anchoring math lives in `_anchor_toast_rack`,\nand `_BottomChrome` is a thin `Container` subclass that exists only to\nsurface `Resize` (which does not bubble) to the app.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"586\" height=\"224\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-27 at 4 35 45 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9c5d4a2-a4d9-410e-ad85-a8aacef89bf6\"\n/>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- New pilot-driven tests cover the resting offset, that stacked toasts\nend flush above the chrome, that growing the chat input lifts the rack,\nand the short-terminal clamp. Three of the four fail without the change.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/40b5babe-cea3-6b01-d998-fc3b980ad406)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"73b375445c7193aa5a967ce98d1116807bb119b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/73b375445c7193aa5a967ce98d1116807bb119b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ+9NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA51gQADcWWOzzCqh2W7JNLw+Xv0vE\n826oS+R/E1vWEENeME5/p0pJtnzI6DCrwM9oJ67r6jQ6C6N39o2JElzvM1ztEbfd\nkUAzgtXFBqwI4o+NFFE/rHRym/TCHabVqM+94HFxVHfyljCXGHbFjkzN9VFoLhpr\nUeivNv4jfedro1Kl48KWb5OKywisdINMDg3FVZKU23WgjzBGTlKaAD+iAyM4oORD\nX7zXH/c4yMrzGDe+scWv1DVSNDg3DJw6Slf9s551KRWfBmUvgxsb8zM7rt0cuYHa\nGrpp/nwbe8UiYFv3uc2gXjMvcdMLDYDRNRl+n7SObQqOlJt41MyM6epNT8uNkaG4\n0iGQK0mgwHQr41S5jUoYK/fvyljptgsbBcI9NMOx22HbP1AZVzFDhOAs5ZIK4V5I\nLcAoQXv58dbRKb6frqe0fvKsTWTWuHlYCYPcvL04ZW3OeOfH1wMonpoRGaswK7lP\ndHkQvIMzNqiZZoabGqt0rnKu4r2Tn0N5+e3wsX39JRl8k88BKEeYr8tm2dVdakLl\nyEo1n+s1RYf4H1AJ/upmpmIygD3KssIGki0YqjRuI1dTLvXPNVfXIWe6XEoOUp6p\nfAjO7u6KrJucN5/PViFnWkdmHYHvChm07c07fZ+vVjGaVlpmeY9vADE4j50+i18x\nHOh3AYprTc9XdAgnWHP3\n=LB7S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 73b375445c7193aa5a967ce98d1116807bb119b5\nparent 2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1785196365 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785196365 +0000\n\nfix(code): anchor toasts above the chat input (#5101)\n\nToasts no longer cover the chat input — they now float directly above\nthe input box.\n\n---\n\nTextual docks its `ToastRack` to the bottom of the screen, which puts\nevery toast on top of the composer the user is typing into. Rather than\nrestyling individual toasts, the app now tracks the bottom chrome\n(subagent panel, startup tip, goal status, chat input, and status bar)\nand widens the rack's bottom margin so the stack ends exactly at the top\nedge of that chrome.\n\nThe bottom container announces its own resizes, so the anchor follows\nthe chat input as it grows with a multi-line message and as the bottom\npanels come and go; terminal resizes re-anchor too. On a terminal too\nshort to fit both, the offset is clamped so a toast is never pushed off\nscreen. Modal screens compose their own rack and are deliberately left\nalone.\n\nWorth a careful look: the anchoring math lives in `_anchor_toast_rack`,\nand `_BottomChrome` is a thin `Container` subclass that exists only to\nsurface `Resize` (which does not bubble) to the app.\n\n## Screenshots\n<img width=\"586\" height=\"224\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-27 at 4 35 45 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9c5d4a2-a4d9-410e-ad85-a8aacef89bf6\"\n/>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- New pilot-driven tests cover the resting offset, that stacked toasts\nend flush above the chrome, that growing the chat input lifts the rack,\nand the short-terminal clamp. Three of the four fail without the change.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/40b5babe-cea3-6b01-d998-fc3b980ad406)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-27T23:52:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f1727c785c44809e7b1b7ed8c5d0b31c560ae3ad/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760"}]},{"sha":"2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI0ODdjNGI4N2RmZjI2NGFlMWU4ZDM0YzdjZTkyNDlkZDRiMjk3NjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-27T23:20:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-27T23:20:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): integrate Hooks v2 server lifecycle events (#4997)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\nDepends on #4971\nCloses DCD-69\n\nServer-owned Hooks v2 events now pause the agent over LangGraph\ninterrupts, run on the client `HooksRuntime`, and resume with typed\ndecisions.\n\n---\n\nThis starts the DCD-69 stack on top of the DCD-70 leaf (#4971).\n\n- Adds a versioned `hook_invocation` interrupt/resume transport around\n`HookInvocationRequest` / `HookInvocationResponse`.\n- Installs `ServerHooksMiddleware` for `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`,\n`Stop`, `SubagentStart`, and `SubagentStop`, gated by the session's\nconfigured server events so idle sessions skip the round-trip.\n- Creates a session-scoped client `HooksRuntime` and fulfills server\ninterrupts from both the Textual adapter and headless runner.\n- Applies `deny`/`ask` as blocking tool errors for now; `ask` approval\nUX remains for DCD-71.\n\n## Review Guide\n\n1. `hooks/server_middleware.py` — middleware, gating, interrupt raise,\ndecision apply\n2. `hooks/interrupt.py` — `hook_invocation` pause/resume contract\n3. `hooks/client.py` — client fulfillment + resume ledger\n4. `agent.py` — middleware install (main + subagents)\n5. `tui/textual_adapter.py`, `client/non_interactive.py` — interrupt\nfulfillment call sites\n6. Skim: `envelope.py`, `context.py`, `runtime.py`, `_cli_context.py`,\nsmall `app`/`auto_mode`/`main`/`snapshot`/`engine` touches\n7. Tests: `test_server_lifecycle.py`, then `test_agent` /\n`test_non_interactive` / `test_engine`\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- `uv run --group test pytest tests/unit_tests/hooks` — 133 passed\n- `make lint` in `libs/code`\n\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- branch-stack-start -->\n\n-------------------------\n- main\n- **feat(code): integrate Hooks v2 server lifecycle events**\n:point_left:\n    - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/5010\n      - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/5044\n        - https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/5045\n\n<sup>[Stack](https://www.git-town.com/how-to/proposal-breadcrumb.html)\ngenerated by [Git Town](https://github.com/git-town/git-town)</sup>\n\n<!-- branch-stack-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7f5da5d799dedcedc7107d18e552a3b8f17dad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c7f5da5d799dedcedc7107d18e552a3b8f17dad1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2487c4b87dff264ae1e8d34c7ce9249dd4b29760"